1
00:00:08,282 --> 00:00:10,381
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

2
00:00:10,382 --> 00:00:13,081
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

3
00:00:13,082 --> 00:00:14,721
(Signature choreography takeover match)

4
00:00:14,722 --> 00:00:17,022
(BADA 4, INGYOO 5)

5
00:00:22,192 --> 00:00:23,502
This is brutal.

6
00:00:27,572 --> 00:00:29,632
I was overflowing with confidence.

7
00:00:29,972 --> 00:00:32,341
This is the first time I lost my choreography...

8
00:00:32,342 --> 00:00:35,442
and failed to win my rival's.

9
00:00:35,542 --> 00:00:37,282
I was confused.

10
00:00:38,312 --> 00:00:39,541
(Signature choreography takeover match)

11
00:00:39,542 --> 00:00:40,751
(Back Koo Young 9, Kasper 0)

12
00:00:40,752 --> 00:00:43,582
Something's gone wrong.

13
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:45,451
(Heavy-hearted)

14
00:00:45,452 --> 00:00:47,651
I started feeling anxious...

15
00:00:47,652 --> 00:00:49,492
after seeing the public's reaction.

16
00:00:50,322 --> 00:00:52,362
"He's wobbling too much. Is he an earthworm?"

17
00:00:52,622 --> 00:00:55,431
"That doesn't look any different from the original."

18
00:00:55,432 --> 00:00:56,562
(Kasper's new "Love Shot" received harsh criticisms.)

19
00:00:56,662 --> 00:00:59,231
(When announcing the result)

20
00:00:59,232 --> 00:01:00,232
(He didn't receive a single vote.)

21
00:01:00,233 --> 00:01:02,401
On top of that, it was a total defeat.

22
00:01:02,402 --> 00:01:03,772
(Looking away)

23
00:01:04,072 --> 00:01:07,642
Everyone turned their backs on me.

24
00:01:08,872 --> 00:01:10,842
I wanted to hide.

25
00:01:11,982 --> 00:01:14,111
(Simeez 9, Renan 0)

26
00:01:14,112 --> 00:01:15,582
This is tough.

27
00:01:16,782 --> 00:01:18,822
Is it okay to turn off the light?

28
00:01:20,622 --> 00:01:23,021
The feeling of all that time I spent on "Armageddon..."

29
00:01:23,022 --> 00:01:25,222
felt denied.

30
00:01:25,322 --> 00:01:27,432
That really upset me.

31
00:01:27,562 --> 00:01:28,892
(Heavy-hearted)

32
00:01:29,592 --> 00:01:31,061
(Yelling)

33
00:01:31,062 --> 00:01:32,131
(Glancing)

34
00:01:32,132 --> 00:01:33,931
(Cheers cut through the silence.)

35
00:01:33,932 --> 00:01:35,172
It's over now.

36
00:01:35,872 --> 00:01:37,401
I was happy to hear...

37
00:01:37,402 --> 00:01:38,472
that my name will appear as a choreographer.

38
00:01:38,842 --> 00:01:40,942
I was like, "What? Maybe I did a really good job."

39
00:01:41,742 --> 00:01:44,612
I'm going to win the Director's Credit next.

40
00:01:45,142 --> 00:01:46,581
(INGYOO's room is filled with his humming.)

41
00:01:46,582 --> 00:01:47,882
It felt amazing.

42
00:01:48,312 --> 00:01:50,112
(On cloud nine)

43
00:01:50,212 --> 00:01:52,151
(Laughing)

44
00:01:52,152 --> 00:01:55,391
It requires my choreography in general.

45
00:01:55,392 --> 00:01:57,462
The situation is...

46
00:01:57,562 --> 00:01:58,792
in my favor.

47
00:01:59,022 --> 00:02:01,562
I'm going to enjoy it and have more fun.

48
00:02:01,892 --> 00:02:03,901
(BABYZOO 5, NaiN 4)

49
00:02:03,902 --> 00:02:05,631
I won the choreographer title.

50
00:02:05,632 --> 00:02:07,772
And I need to win the Director Credit too.

51
00:02:07,872 --> 00:02:10,572
I began planning immediately.

52
00:02:11,302 --> 00:02:12,302
(He's about to crush the mission song.)

53
00:02:12,303 --> 00:02:13,942
(Planning mode)

54
00:02:14,042 --> 00:02:16,642
After winning, it got me thinking,

55
00:02:16,772 --> 00:02:19,081
I do have a weapon,

56
00:02:19,082 --> 00:02:22,511
but Hash's good at directing.

57
00:02:22,512 --> 00:02:24,052
I can never be off guard.

58
00:02:24,352 --> 00:02:27,391
I think my performance...

59
00:02:27,392 --> 00:02:28,852
mixed with MIN JUN's choreography...

60
00:02:28,952 --> 00:02:32,862
will feel cooler and fresher.

61
00:02:33,022 --> 00:02:35,661
The signature choreography is a bummer.

62
00:02:35,662 --> 00:02:37,502
It's not over until it's over.

63
00:02:37,602 --> 00:02:40,231
It'll be a matter...

64
00:02:40,232 --> 00:02:41,571
of how creatively each person handles it.

65
00:02:41,572 --> 00:02:42,731
I feel confident...

66
00:02:42,732 --> 00:02:45,571
about developing it and turning the choreography I lost even cooler.

67
00:02:45,572 --> 00:02:46,801
If I lose again,

68
00:02:46,802 --> 00:02:48,111
it'll be like getting kicked out...

69
00:02:48,112 --> 00:02:50,512
to the street naked.

70
00:02:51,012 --> 00:02:53,282
I'll win by 9 to 0 this time.

71
00:03:02,492 --> 00:03:04,721
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

72
00:03:04,722 --> 00:03:07,061
(To be continued)

73
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:08,591
All the results have been announced...

74
00:03:08,592 --> 00:03:10,531
for the signature choreography takeover match.

75
00:03:10,532 --> 00:03:11,932
The first choreographers to have their names...

76
00:03:12,032 --> 00:03:14,371
on the credit board for choreographer are...

77
00:03:14,372 --> 00:03:15,932
Simeez, BABYZOO,

78
00:03:16,202 --> 00:03:17,802
JEONG MIN JUN, INGYOO,

79
00:03:18,042 --> 00:03:19,142
and Back Koo Young.

80
00:03:19,242 --> 00:03:21,912
Now, both signature parts...

81
00:03:22,112 --> 00:03:23,571
will compose of the winner's choreography.

82
00:03:23,572 --> 00:03:26,841
You'll work based on that.

83
00:03:26,842 --> 00:03:29,982
It'll be obvious that I'm working on someone else's choreography.

84
00:03:30,082 --> 00:03:31,421
It's not even my choreography.

85
00:03:31,422 --> 00:03:34,852
My pride isn't hurt. It's rotting.

86
00:03:34,952 --> 00:03:36,851
I've hit rock bottom.

87
00:03:36,852 --> 00:03:37,861
Although I lost my choreography,

88
00:03:37,862 --> 00:03:40,662
I'll win the director title.

89
00:03:40,762 --> 00:03:43,491
I'll get the Director Credit.

90
00:03:43,492 --> 00:03:46,131
In the last run to determine the final director,

91
00:03:46,132 --> 00:03:47,632
the judges will evaluate you...

92
00:03:47,732 --> 00:03:49,031
based on your choreography,

93
00:03:49,032 --> 00:03:51,041
a number of dancers, space structure,

94
00:03:51,042 --> 00:03:56,242
and the ability to direct a large group.

95
00:03:56,942 --> 00:03:58,012
Judges' evaluation?

96
00:03:58,112 --> 00:03:59,611
This is a directing battle.

97
00:03:59,612 --> 00:04:01,481
I might not become a director?

98
00:04:01,482 --> 00:04:03,411
That's not good. I can never accept that.

99
00:04:03,412 --> 00:04:04,922
The cards aren't in my hands.

100
00:04:05,022 --> 00:04:06,081
I'm worried about it.

101
00:04:06,082 --> 00:04:08,451
I can't lose it. Losing that will be a nightmare.

102
00:04:08,452 --> 00:04:11,792
Becoming a director with my choreography won't be easy.

103
00:04:11,892 --> 00:04:13,561
It'll be hard. It'll be tough.

104
00:04:13,562 --> 00:04:15,861
Now, you'll cast dancers...

105
00:04:15,862 --> 00:04:18,132
to complete the work with you.

106
00:04:18,732 --> 00:04:20,101
Oh, we get to cast them?

107
00:04:20,102 --> 00:04:22,031
Because everyone wants to cast talented dancers,

108
00:04:22,032 --> 00:04:23,332
a battle will break out.

109
00:04:23,742 --> 00:04:25,602
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

110
00:04:25,742 --> 00:04:27,441
(To complete the final stage)

111
00:04:27,442 --> 00:04:30,612
I will tell you how the dancer casting works.

112
00:04:30,982 --> 00:04:34,682
There will be a total of 80 dancers per round.

113
00:04:34,982 --> 00:04:36,551
You'll choose five from each round...

114
00:04:36,552 --> 00:04:39,982
with a total of 40 dancers to form a team.

115
00:04:40,122 --> 00:04:41,651
Depending on the direction of your work,

116
00:04:41,652 --> 00:04:44,521
you may cast ten additional dancers.

117
00:04:44,522 --> 00:04:47,092
A team can have up to 50 dancers.

118
00:04:47,192 --> 00:04:48,592
You must come up...

119
00:04:48,692 --> 00:04:51,262
with the best strategy to complete your work.

120
00:04:51,402 --> 00:04:52,462
It's either one.

121
00:04:52,562 --> 00:04:55,932
Either excel or make it even more brutal.

122
00:04:56,032 --> 00:04:58,242
"Renan's the best director ever."

123
00:04:58,502 --> 00:05:00,202
I will have to do my best.

124
00:05:00,272 --> 00:05:03,171
Well, thanks for your choreography.

125
00:05:03,172 --> 00:05:04,312
But I am the director.

126
00:05:04,682 --> 00:05:06,042
(Next morning)

127
00:05:06,242 --> 00:05:08,752
(Back to Directors' Lab)

128
00:05:12,082 --> 00:05:13,351
Dancer casting?

129
00:05:13,352 --> 00:05:14,451
That's the most important.

130
00:05:14,452 --> 00:05:18,061
A director could create a masterpiece...

131
00:05:18,062 --> 00:05:20,192
if they make good use of talented dancers.

132
00:05:20,292 --> 00:05:22,561
Dancers over a choreography.

133
00:05:22,562 --> 00:05:25,161
Dancer casting is the key.

134
00:05:25,162 --> 00:05:27,271
What matters the most in dancer casting is...

135
00:05:27,272 --> 00:05:30,331
a body that can absorb anything.

136
00:05:30,332 --> 00:05:31,641
Spella? No way. She's mine for sure.

137
00:05:31,642 --> 00:05:34,611
I'm good at making use of the dancers' strength.

138
00:05:34,612 --> 00:05:36,911
Dancers with strong presence and identity.

139
00:05:36,912 --> 00:05:38,912
I want someone with ambition and distinct character.

140
00:05:39,012 --> 00:05:41,552
Is this the list of dancers for me and Hash?

141
00:05:41,882 --> 00:05:42,981
Lip J?

142
00:05:42,982 --> 00:05:44,151
(Lip J?)

143
00:05:44,152 --> 00:05:45,821
I fell silent.

144
00:05:45,822 --> 00:05:48,422
What is Lip J doing in there?

145
00:05:48,622 --> 00:05:49,622
For real?

146
00:05:49,623 --> 00:05:51,921
Lip J is good.

147
00:05:51,922 --> 00:05:54,362
She's already earned the public's approval.

148
00:05:54,462 --> 00:05:55,992
Lip J was number one on my list.

149
00:05:56,092 --> 00:05:57,431
I have to get her for sure.

150
00:05:57,432 --> 00:06:00,202
I want to work with Rian so bad.

151
00:06:00,302 --> 00:06:02,571
(Rian!)

152
00:06:02,572 --> 00:06:03,572
(Simeez runs to Rian as soon as she sees her name.)

153
00:06:03,573 --> 00:06:05,201
- I can never lose Rian. - I choose Rian.

154
00:06:05,202 --> 00:06:06,202
(Renan also sees Rian.)

155
00:06:06,203 --> 00:06:08,712
I have to win this time. I couldn't give up.

156
00:06:08,812 --> 00:06:09,812
For sure.

157
00:06:09,813 --> 00:06:11,441
HANYA members for sure.

158
00:06:11,442 --> 00:06:13,811
Since he got the signature choreography, he'll give up on this.

159
00:06:13,812 --> 00:06:14,881
I can never give up.

160
00:06:14,882 --> 00:06:15,911
Why would I? Never.

161
00:06:15,912 --> 00:06:16,912
Who said that?

162
00:06:17,052 --> 00:06:18,322
Wait. Lee Jung?

163
00:06:18,752 --> 00:06:21,651
(Laughing)

164
00:06:21,652 --> 00:06:24,392
Lee Jung's here.

165
00:06:24,622 --> 00:06:25,691
Wait. Mood Dog?

166
00:06:25,692 --> 00:06:26,692
(Passing out)

167
00:06:27,432 --> 00:06:30,662
This is crazy.

168
00:06:31,032 --> 00:06:32,401
(Mood Dog of YGX participated as a rookie class main dancer...)

169
00:06:32,402 --> 00:06:33,871
(in "Street Man Fighter.")

170
00:06:33,872 --> 00:06:35,671
(BABYZOO, Lee Jung, and Mood Dog are...)

171
00:06:35,672 --> 00:06:37,571
(known for being friends.)

172
00:06:37,572 --> 00:06:38,572
I can never give up on them.

173
00:06:38,572 --> 00:06:39,572
I'm going for Lee Jung.

174
00:06:39,572 --> 00:06:40,572
Wait a minute.

175
00:06:40,573 --> 00:06:42,172
I'm not as kind as you think, you know?

176
00:06:42,272 --> 00:06:43,741
First, I need Nino.

177
00:06:43,742 --> 00:06:45,141
It's weird to see Nino...

178
00:06:45,142 --> 00:06:46,941
in someone else's team.

179
00:06:46,942 --> 00:06:48,151
So what are you going to do?

180
00:06:48,152 --> 00:06:49,782
Are you going there or staying here?

181
00:06:49,982 --> 00:06:51,182
(A fierce battle over Nino)

182
00:06:51,282 --> 00:06:53,582
Oh, Shuri?

183
00:06:53,682 --> 00:06:55,752
All directors here want him.

184
00:06:56,152 --> 00:06:58,762
- Shuri's coming? - Shuri?

185
00:06:58,892 --> 00:07:00,161
I want Shuri.

186
00:07:00,162 --> 00:07:01,591
- I want him too. - Oh, Shuri.

187
00:07:01,592 --> 00:07:03,031
- No. - No way.

188
00:07:03,032 --> 00:07:04,032
You can't take him.

189
00:07:04,033 --> 00:07:05,532
I've worked with him before.

190
00:07:05,632 --> 00:07:06,762
Shuri, I live in Japan.

191
00:07:06,862 --> 00:07:08,631
What are you saying? Shuri's mine.

192
00:07:08,632 --> 00:07:09,801
- Hey. - What are you doing?

193
00:07:09,802 --> 00:07:11,341
- He's mine. - I know.

194
00:07:11,342 --> 00:07:14,212
I brought him from Japan.

195
00:07:14,312 --> 00:07:15,771
He's like my son.

196
00:07:15,772 --> 00:07:18,511
(The Japanese dancer who captivated Korea's dance scene)

197
00:07:18,512 --> 00:07:21,111
(Shuri's known for his big physique and strong expression.)

198
00:07:21,112 --> 00:07:23,451
I call him a weapon. My weapon.

199
00:07:23,452 --> 00:07:25,752
Vata's my highest priority.

200
00:07:25,852 --> 00:07:27,252
Vata's here too.

201
00:07:27,352 --> 00:07:29,252
Oh, Tatter!

202
00:07:30,092 --> 00:07:32,692
She's the anchor of my team.

203
00:07:32,792 --> 00:07:34,692
She'll be my highest priority.

204
00:07:35,132 --> 00:07:36,862
I can cast Tatter?

205
00:07:37,462 --> 00:07:39,102
Tatter is my highest priority.

206
00:07:39,462 --> 00:07:41,131
If he takes Tatter?

207
00:07:41,132 --> 00:07:42,471
Then she'll be my spy.

208
00:07:42,472 --> 00:07:44,202
I'll tell her to report...

209
00:07:44,302 --> 00:07:45,772
every detail of INGYOO's plan.

210
00:07:46,202 --> 00:07:47,811
(Ten chairs for directors are...)

211
00:07:47,812 --> 00:07:49,471
(placed in Directors' Lab.)

212
00:07:49,472 --> 00:07:50,472
Oh, there are chairs.

213
00:07:50,473 --> 00:07:52,411
(And the dummies...)

214
00:07:52,412 --> 00:07:54,012
(come alive.)

215
00:07:55,612 --> 00:07:59,722
(An endless rows of dancers)

216
00:08:00,482 --> 00:08:03,252
(Global dancers gathered for Street World Fighter: Directors' War.)

217
00:08:03,352 --> 00:08:06,222
(1-on-1 Signature Mission with 400 Dancers)

218
00:08:06,662 --> 00:08:08,392
- I'm scared. - This is so much pressure.

219
00:08:08,792 --> 00:08:09,792
(Gasping)

220
00:08:12,062 --> 00:08:13,102
This is crazy.

221
00:08:13,862 --> 00:08:15,002
Gosh.

222
00:08:17,102 --> 00:08:18,402
(The first 80 dancers have entered.)

223
00:08:19,772 --> 00:08:21,342
So they're the first round of dancers.

224
00:08:21,442 --> 00:08:22,511
(Exclaiming)

225
00:08:22,512 --> 00:08:23,612
This is awesome.

226
00:08:25,212 --> 00:08:26,481
The first match is...

227
00:08:26,482 --> 00:08:28,182
Simeez versus Renan.

228
00:08:29,052 --> 00:08:30,481
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission Dancer Casting)

229
00:08:30,482 --> 00:08:31,482
This is going to be fun.

230
00:08:31,483 --> 00:08:32,822
- Isn't that Rian? - That's Rian.

231
00:08:33,482 --> 00:08:34,922
She's a very famous dancer...

232
00:08:35,022 --> 00:08:36,922
and a dazzling player.

233
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:40,691
She's a very strong performer.

234
00:08:40,692 --> 00:08:41,692
(Rian is strong at choreography performance.)

235
00:08:42,032 --> 00:08:43,091
There's Spella.

236
00:08:43,092 --> 00:08:44,302
I know. Spella's here too.

237
00:08:44,832 --> 00:08:47,401
Spella's good at soft moves...

238
00:08:47,402 --> 00:08:48,972
as well as strong moves.

239
00:08:49,402 --> 00:08:51,972
I think she's good at performing.

240
00:08:52,842 --> 00:08:54,071
I see JAYME.

241
00:08:54,072 --> 00:08:56,112
Don't you think you're eyeing someone who's too good?

242
00:08:56,272 --> 00:09:00,012
JAYME has a very wide range.

243
00:09:00,612 --> 00:09:02,751
He nails it just by standing there.

244
00:09:02,752 --> 00:09:04,722
He's one and only.

245
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:07,622
We might end up fighting, pulling each other's hair to get him.

246
00:09:08,092 --> 00:09:09,391
- Hello. - Hello.

247
00:09:09,392 --> 00:09:10,962
- I'm Simeez. - I'm Renan.

248
00:09:11,822 --> 00:09:13,722
My signature song is IVE's "BANG BANG."

249
00:09:13,822 --> 00:09:15,461
And Renan's signature song is...

250
00:09:15,462 --> 00:09:16,961
aespa's "Armageddon."

251
00:09:16,962 --> 00:09:18,361
The song's been rearranged.

252
00:09:18,362 --> 00:09:20,531
The song is very intense in general.

253
00:09:20,532 --> 00:09:22,731
The final theme is destruction and awakening.

254
00:09:22,732 --> 00:09:23,771
The final battle.

255
00:09:23,772 --> 00:09:26,041
I really liked Varang...

256
00:09:26,042 --> 00:09:28,441
from "Avatar: Fire and Ash."

257
00:09:28,442 --> 00:09:30,172
That's what I'm thinking about in terms of visualization.

258
00:09:30,572 --> 00:09:32,981
When I heard her theme, I was kind of worried.

259
00:09:32,982 --> 00:09:35,882
I'll tell you about my concept.

260
00:09:36,082 --> 00:09:38,021
I wanted to express...

261
00:09:38,022 --> 00:09:41,151
someone who lives the way he wants...

262
00:09:41,152 --> 00:09:44,492
regardless of what others say.

263
00:09:44,592 --> 00:09:46,391
The biggest difference is...

264
00:09:46,392 --> 00:09:48,532
that I have a clear concept.

265
00:09:48,632 --> 00:09:51,332
Her direction is a shame.

266
00:09:51,962 --> 00:09:55,401
Simeez's concept was clear.

267
00:09:55,402 --> 00:09:57,471
I was like, "That sounds cool."

268
00:09:57,472 --> 00:09:58,801
I could picture it in my head.

269
00:09:58,802 --> 00:10:01,742
I can't tell what Renan wants to do.

270
00:10:02,042 --> 00:10:03,511
Because I must win,

271
00:10:03,512 --> 00:10:05,841
I need dancers with definite style...

272
00:10:05,842 --> 00:10:07,712
and abilities to pull off the dance.

273
00:10:08,312 --> 00:10:09,811
Although I lost the signature choreography,

274
00:10:09,812 --> 00:10:11,181
to turn it around,

275
00:10:11,182 --> 00:10:13,422
I need good dancers.

276
00:10:13,682 --> 00:10:14,692
First.

277
00:10:14,822 --> 00:10:18,722
(Who will get to cast first?)

278
00:10:18,922 --> 00:10:20,961
(1 hour ago)

279
00:10:20,962 --> 00:10:22,762
What do you want to do?

280
00:10:22,862 --> 00:10:23,992
What do you want to do?

281
00:10:24,102 --> 00:10:27,802
Is there any dancer you must have?

282
00:10:27,972 --> 00:10:29,801
Unless we had the same dancer candidates,

283
00:10:29,802 --> 00:10:32,272
it didn't matter who went first.

284
00:10:32,372 --> 00:10:34,972
I'm thinking BIGGY and JAYME.

285
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:37,941
I need Rian for sure.

286
00:10:37,942 --> 00:10:39,881
And I need Spella.

287
00:10:39,882 --> 00:10:41,882
I want BIGGY and JAYME.

288
00:10:42,212 --> 00:10:43,482
How can she do that?

289
00:10:43,582 --> 00:10:45,222
That's everyone.

290
00:10:46,952 --> 00:10:48,451
How can she be so selfish?

291
00:10:48,452 --> 00:10:50,092
How can she be so inconsiderate?

292
00:10:50,992 --> 00:10:53,221
They're here for me.

293
00:10:53,222 --> 00:10:55,192
I don't want to lose them.

294
00:10:56,292 --> 00:10:58,632
I'm planning on many unique angles.

295
00:11:01,002 --> 00:11:03,232
I had no intention of giving in.

296
00:11:03,332 --> 00:11:05,441
JAYME has his own style.

297
00:11:05,442 --> 00:11:06,871
I need someone more than just being a good dancer.

298
00:11:06,872 --> 00:11:09,412
I needed someone with star quality and personality.

299
00:11:10,812 --> 00:11:13,442
I just couldn't give up on JAYME.

300
00:11:13,812 --> 00:11:15,582
Dancer casting is important...

301
00:11:15,682 --> 00:11:17,981
because I like creating main characters.

302
00:11:17,982 --> 00:11:20,581
So for Rian, JAYME, and Spella,

303
00:11:20,582 --> 00:11:22,491
I plan to give them characters.

304
00:11:22,492 --> 00:11:24,721
I was planning to...

305
00:11:24,722 --> 00:11:28,291
give them a different style among the other dancers.

306
00:11:28,292 --> 00:11:30,292
But...

307
00:11:31,132 --> 00:11:33,002
when I do something hip during the song,

308
00:11:33,102 --> 00:11:34,472
I need BIGGY.

309
00:11:36,002 --> 00:11:37,802
I can never give in.

310
00:11:38,602 --> 00:11:40,502
I need BIGGY too.

311
00:11:40,672 --> 00:11:43,242
This is so stressful.

312
00:11:43,612 --> 00:11:45,442
- BIGGY and JAYME? - Yes.

313
00:11:46,342 --> 00:11:49,481
JAYME looks cool even when he just stretches his arm.

314
00:11:49,482 --> 00:11:51,151
He could be my strong weapon.

315
00:11:51,152 --> 00:11:53,022
So I didn't want to lose him.

316
00:11:53,822 --> 00:11:54,952
(Groaning)

317
00:11:57,152 --> 00:11:58,222
This is crazy.

318
00:12:00,932 --> 00:12:03,491
I knew going first was more advantageous.

319
00:12:03,492 --> 00:12:04,801
Because I couldn't lose them.

320
00:12:04,802 --> 00:12:07,232
I knew I had to get them first.

321
00:12:07,572 --> 00:12:09,372
First. Choreographer Renan...

322
00:12:09,472 --> 00:12:11,372
will begin casting the dancers.

323
00:12:11,702 --> 00:12:12,971
(Renan casts the dancers first.)

324
00:12:12,972 --> 00:12:15,541
Simeez! You lost it.

325
00:12:15,542 --> 00:12:18,241
I got the signature choreography,

326
00:12:18,242 --> 00:12:21,512
and I can always come up with new characters. So I gave in.

327
00:12:21,782 --> 00:12:24,881
The first person to cast is...

328
00:12:24,882 --> 00:12:27,592
JAYME.

329
00:12:28,892 --> 00:12:29,922
(Grunting)

330
00:12:31,162 --> 00:12:33,161
I really want to work with you.

331
00:12:33,162 --> 00:12:35,062
I'd like to cast you.

332
00:12:35,362 --> 00:12:38,662
No.

333
00:12:39,362 --> 00:12:41,802
- Thank you. - Thank you.

334
00:12:42,272 --> 00:12:45,542
Seeing her taking JAYME in front of me,

335
00:12:45,702 --> 00:12:47,612
it got me thinking, "Why did I give up JAYME?"

336
00:12:47,842 --> 00:12:49,572
(Scanning)

337
00:12:49,812 --> 00:12:50,982
It still upsets me.

338
00:12:51,342 --> 00:12:53,011
I still regret...

339
00:12:53,012 --> 00:12:54,082
not taking JAYME the most.

340
00:12:54,452 --> 00:12:57,282
Why did I do that? I must've lost it at the time.

341
00:12:57,982 --> 00:13:01,291
And BIGGY.

342
00:13:01,292 --> 00:13:02,452
I'll cast her.

343
00:13:03,192 --> 00:13:04,661
- Are you casting me? - Yes.

344
00:13:04,662 --> 00:13:05,862
(The second dancer she casts is BIGGY.)

345
00:13:06,122 --> 00:13:08,432
No. She's taking everyone.

346
00:13:09,062 --> 00:13:10,332
Why did I let her go first?

347
00:13:10,592 --> 00:13:11,961
If I could go back in time,

348
00:13:11,962 --> 00:13:13,632
I would go first.

349
00:13:13,832 --> 00:13:17,431
I was so happy...

350
00:13:17,432 --> 00:13:19,072
to cast good dancers first.

351
00:13:20,542 --> 00:13:22,072
JEONG MIN JUN versus Hash.

352
00:13:22,272 --> 00:13:24,281
We'll now begin the dancer casting.

353
00:13:24,282 --> 00:13:25,282
(The dancers are warming up.)

354
00:13:26,112 --> 00:13:27,512
(Welcoming)

355
00:13:27,882 --> 00:13:29,882
(Good luck.)

356
00:13:30,612 --> 00:13:32,182
(Greeting)

357
00:13:33,782 --> 00:13:34,791
Who's that?

358
00:13:34,792 --> 00:13:35,892
(A dancer with 19 years of experience?)

359
00:13:36,252 --> 00:13:37,252
Who's that?

360
00:13:37,492 --> 00:13:39,122
I said hi to Lip J.

361
00:13:39,222 --> 00:13:41,032
- Is that Lip J? - Yes.

362
00:13:41,262 --> 00:13:42,861
Lip J's here?

363
00:13:42,862 --> 00:13:43,862
(Lip J of PROWDMON)

364
00:13:44,332 --> 00:13:47,002
She's the top waacker in Korea.

365
00:13:47,462 --> 00:13:50,702
Every gesture she makes is charismatic.

366
00:13:50,932 --> 00:13:53,672
The first dancer to choose was Lip J.

367
00:13:53,772 --> 00:13:55,312
Lip J was my highest priority.

368
00:13:56,112 --> 00:13:57,812
(1 hour ago)

369
00:13:57,982 --> 00:14:00,112
What do we do? Who are you going to pick?

370
00:14:01,152 --> 00:14:03,051
First, Lip J.

371
00:14:03,052 --> 00:14:04,052
Really?

372
00:14:04,452 --> 00:14:09,392
But I should have her.

373
00:14:09,752 --> 00:14:12,162
(Laughing)

374
00:14:12,322 --> 00:14:15,761
Then whoever picks Lip J gives up on five people.

375
00:14:15,762 --> 00:14:16,862
(Give up on five dancers.)

376
00:14:16,992 --> 00:14:18,661
Let's spin the roulette.

377
00:14:18,662 --> 00:14:19,662
(They suddenly spin the roulette.)

378
00:14:19,962 --> 00:14:21,031
Gosh.

379
00:14:21,032 --> 00:14:22,032
(Nervous)

380
00:14:23,602 --> 00:14:25,072
Please.

381
00:14:25,902 --> 00:14:27,242
(JEONG MIN JUN wins.)

382
00:14:27,812 --> 00:14:29,042
(Groaning)

383
00:14:29,542 --> 00:14:31,012
(Joy)

384
00:14:31,212 --> 00:14:33,312
But why?

385
00:14:33,512 --> 00:14:36,452
I'd like to work...

386
00:14:36,682 --> 00:14:40,622
with Korea's top waacker, Lip J.

387
00:14:40,752 --> 00:14:42,221
I'd really appreciate it...

388
00:14:42,222 --> 00:14:43,321
- if you could join me. - Are you casting me?

389
00:14:43,322 --> 00:14:44,461
Yes. I'd really appreciate it.

390
00:14:44,462 --> 00:14:46,322
Can I dance?

391
00:14:47,522 --> 00:14:48,561
Let's go.

392
00:14:48,562 --> 00:14:49,562
(Lip J's ceremony)

393
00:14:50,162 --> 00:14:51,701
So cool!

394
00:14:51,702 --> 00:14:53,702
(Featured by Street World Fighter: Directors' War waacker, BABYZOO)

395
00:14:53,862 --> 00:14:55,372
(Who can refuse this combination?)

396
00:14:59,972 --> 00:15:02,042
Oh, my gosh.

397
00:15:03,612 --> 00:15:04,882
(Immersed)

398
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:06,712
(I'll show you what waacking is.)

399
00:15:10,052 --> 00:15:11,052
Yes.

400
00:15:15,392 --> 00:15:16,892
What? They're like twins.

401
00:15:19,522 --> 00:15:21,331
(In sync)

402
00:15:21,332 --> 00:15:24,032
Yes!

403
00:15:24,732 --> 00:15:26,462
(A fantastic collaboration of Lip J and BABYZOO)

404
00:15:26,502 --> 00:15:28,432
(Amazed)

405
00:15:28,672 --> 00:15:30,572
That's unbelievable.

406
00:15:30,872 --> 00:15:33,672
I kind of sighed because I was jealous.

407
00:15:33,842 --> 00:15:36,512
I've gained a powerful ally.

408
00:15:37,342 --> 00:15:39,682
(JEONG MIN JUN's first dancer to cast is Lip J.)

409
00:15:40,082 --> 00:15:43,712
I have someone on my mind.

410
00:15:44,782 --> 00:15:46,181
(While going over the dancer profiles)

411
00:15:46,182 --> 00:15:47,322
Jung Min?

412
00:15:47,752 --> 00:15:49,492
He was a member of MIN JUN's team.

413
00:15:50,022 --> 00:15:52,261
I knew I had to get Jung Min...

414
00:15:52,262 --> 00:15:54,362
since he was close to MIN JUN.

415
00:15:54,732 --> 00:15:56,792
I have to do MIN JUN's choreography in the end.

416
00:15:57,162 --> 00:15:59,361
From what I heard, he pulls off MIN JUN's choreography...

417
00:15:59,362 --> 00:16:01,062
better than MIN JUN does.

418
00:16:01,302 --> 00:16:03,272
So I'm going to make him stand out...

419
00:16:03,372 --> 00:16:04,802
when he does MIN JUN's choreography.

420
00:16:05,872 --> 00:16:06,872
Please.

421
00:16:07,602 --> 00:16:09,772
Please.

422
00:16:10,912 --> 00:16:12,141
(Laughing)

423
00:16:12,142 --> 00:16:17,052
- Please. No! - MIN JUN's...

424
00:16:17,352 --> 00:16:22,052
I choose MIN JUN's best friend.

425
00:16:22,292 --> 00:16:23,722
- Yes. - No.

426
00:16:24,592 --> 00:16:26,292
- Who is he? - He was a member...

427
00:16:26,392 --> 00:16:27,962
- Really? - of MIN JUN's team.

428
00:16:28,232 --> 00:16:30,691
- No. - Sorry.

429
00:16:30,692 --> 00:16:31,801
(Hash's first dancer to cast is Jung Min.)

430
00:16:31,802 --> 00:16:33,631
I'll treat you nicely.

431
00:16:33,632 --> 00:16:37,072
I was worried about Jung Min the most.

432
00:16:37,132 --> 00:16:39,602
I knew I had to cast him.

433
00:16:40,342 --> 00:16:43,872
She strategically took my card.

434
00:16:44,242 --> 00:16:48,612
Because Hash cast Jung Min...

435
00:16:48,852 --> 00:16:50,111
(Anxious)

436
00:16:50,112 --> 00:16:53,222
I selected a few.

437
00:16:53,852 --> 00:16:54,992
I'm looking forward to working with you.

438
00:16:55,552 --> 00:16:57,292
No.

439
00:16:58,722 --> 00:16:59,722
Who is he?

440
00:17:00,192 --> 00:17:04,091
I found a dancer from COME HERE.

441
00:17:04,092 --> 00:17:05,601
I'm taking this card.

442
00:17:05,602 --> 00:17:06,661
(I won't be beaten.)

443
00:17:06,662 --> 00:17:07,872
I'm looking forward to working with you.

444
00:17:08,332 --> 00:17:09,602
(JEONG MIN JUN's second dancer to cast is TAEM.)

445
00:17:10,002 --> 00:17:12,972
(In despair)

446
00:17:13,002 --> 00:17:15,472
MIN JUN just cast a member of COME HERE.

447
00:17:15,572 --> 00:17:17,842
You're right. What are they doing?

448
00:17:17,942 --> 00:17:19,411
They should cast their own team first.

449
00:17:19,412 --> 00:17:20,842
- That's what I mean. - If they're in different teams,

450
00:17:20,942 --> 00:17:22,012
it's a disaster.

451
00:17:22,912 --> 00:17:25,682
Gosh. What am I going to do?

452
00:17:26,382 --> 00:17:28,622
It felt like the end of the world.

453
00:17:28,752 --> 00:17:33,092
We ended up competing...

454
00:17:33,192 --> 00:17:34,962
with each other's most precious team members.

455
00:17:35,632 --> 00:17:36,832
What am I going to do?

456
00:17:36,932 --> 00:17:38,732
I'm different from others.

457
00:17:38,832 --> 00:17:43,172
I'm going to keep adding my styles...

458
00:17:43,432 --> 00:17:46,572
and come up with a performance that only I can do.

459
00:17:46,672 --> 00:17:47,972
I can hold my own...

460
00:17:48,072 --> 00:17:50,942
because I have Lip J with me.

461
00:17:51,682 --> 00:17:54,912
(Max confidence)

462
00:17:55,782 --> 00:17:58,882
I totally stole Renan's signature choreography.

463
00:17:59,982 --> 00:18:01,691
It's driving me crazy.

464
00:18:01,692 --> 00:18:03,892
My anger was up here.

465
00:18:03,992 --> 00:18:06,392
I had to win this time.

466
00:18:06,592 --> 00:18:08,791
I'm confident about a large group performance.

467
00:18:08,792 --> 00:18:10,491
I want to show the difference...

468
00:18:10,492 --> 00:18:11,802
in the signature choreography structure.

469
00:18:11,902 --> 00:18:13,431
Although she took my signature choreography,

470
00:18:13,432 --> 00:18:15,601
I'll put my name...

471
00:18:15,602 --> 00:18:17,202
in the Director Credit.

472
00:18:17,302 --> 00:18:20,302
I really want this of all time.

473
00:18:22,042 --> 00:18:24,881
I'm going to pour in...

474
00:18:24,882 --> 00:18:26,282
everything I have and everything I'm good at.

475
00:18:26,382 --> 00:18:27,982
Because I'm here to fight as a director.

476
00:18:28,212 --> 00:18:29,752
I'll make it a clean sweep.

477
00:18:29,982 --> 00:18:30,982
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

478
00:18:30,983 --> 00:18:34,122
Now, we'll have time to teach the new choreography...

479
00:18:34,222 --> 00:18:35,321
of "Armageddon..."

480
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:37,391
that won the signature choreography takeover match.

481
00:18:37,392 --> 00:18:38,592
(Simeez begins teaching the new "Armageddon" choreography.)

482
00:18:38,892 --> 00:18:41,331
I have sad news.

483
00:18:41,332 --> 00:18:44,031
Simeez and I had a mission.

484
00:18:44,032 --> 00:18:46,101
We were supposed to steal...

485
00:18:46,102 --> 00:18:47,462
each other's signature choreography.

486
00:18:48,072 --> 00:18:51,202
I had a clean sweep.

487
00:18:51,972 --> 00:18:52,972
Awesome.

488
00:18:53,302 --> 00:18:57,042
My choreography won't be used.

489
00:18:57,442 --> 00:18:59,711
It hurt my pride...

490
00:18:59,712 --> 00:19:02,752
to say that I lost it...

491
00:19:02,852 --> 00:19:06,152
to someone else.

492
00:19:06,282 --> 00:19:07,752
It made me really dogged.

493
00:19:08,152 --> 00:19:09,421
I'd better nail it,

494
00:19:09,422 --> 00:19:10,792
so everyone would want to join my team.

495
00:19:10,892 --> 00:19:12,461
- I want to prove it. - You want to prove it?

496
00:19:12,462 --> 00:19:13,891
That my choreography is better.

497
00:19:13,892 --> 00:19:16,791
A director's job starts with teaching.

498
00:19:16,792 --> 00:19:19,032
I need to teach my choreography in a fun, flavorful way.

499
00:19:19,132 --> 00:19:21,162
- Hello. - Hello.

500
00:19:21,602 --> 00:19:22,671
Hello.

501
00:19:22,672 --> 00:19:23,771
(Clapping without looking)

502
00:19:23,772 --> 00:19:27,341
I'll teach it to you super fast and head out.

503
00:19:27,342 --> 00:19:29,772
Play the music, please. I'll show you.

504
00:19:29,872 --> 00:19:31,912
(Renan also has to learn the choreography from Simeez.)

505
00:19:32,012 --> 00:19:34,342
Music.

506
00:19:35,182 --> 00:19:39,881
It felt a bit awkward. I was intimidated without realizing it.

507
00:19:39,882 --> 00:19:41,322
Let me play the track for you once.

508
00:19:43,092 --> 00:19:46,792
When teaching, giving a shocking demonstration has a real impact.

509
00:19:47,022 --> 00:19:48,892
Learning the choreography of "Armageddon..."

510
00:19:48,992 --> 00:19:52,631
from another choreographer...

511
00:19:52,632 --> 00:19:53,932
was really stressful.

512
00:19:54,032 --> 00:19:56,801
"This is the fun choreography you are going to dance."

513
00:19:56,802 --> 00:19:58,142
I need to show it to them in an impressive way.

514
00:20:01,872 --> 00:20:02,872
(Amazed)

515
00:20:03,412 --> 00:20:06,042
(The new "Armageddon," reborn in Simeez's style)

516
00:20:06,682 --> 00:20:07,781
Honestly, she's good.

517
00:20:07,782 --> 00:20:08,782
- Right. - She's so talented.

518
00:20:08,783 --> 00:20:10,482
She's really cool. She's incredible.

519
00:20:12,322 --> 00:20:14,821
All the dancers loved it,

520
00:20:14,822 --> 00:20:16,452
so I felt a bit down.

521
00:20:16,752 --> 00:20:20,691
I want to build a different formation...

522
00:20:20,692 --> 00:20:22,962
to prove that Renan is the better director...

523
00:20:23,062 --> 00:20:24,292
after all.

524
00:20:24,862 --> 00:20:26,261
My goal during the lesson...

525
00:20:26,262 --> 00:20:28,902
was to assess the dancers.

526
00:20:29,002 --> 00:20:30,931
They followed along better than I expected.

527
00:20:30,932 --> 00:20:32,541
But while they execute it well,

528
00:20:32,542 --> 00:20:34,372
they didn't seem to have any distinct features.

529
00:20:34,572 --> 00:20:36,272
Their individuality and charm fall flat.

530
00:20:36,442 --> 00:20:38,782
My dancers have strong, distinct characters.

531
00:20:38,912 --> 00:20:41,011
I need those with solid technique.

532
00:20:41,012 --> 00:20:42,182
Scorpion.

533
00:20:42,552 --> 00:20:43,852
This is like "Star King."

534
00:20:44,282 --> 00:20:45,621
Where have you been all this time?

535
00:20:45,622 --> 00:20:48,251
I thought I should show how people across various genres...

536
00:20:48,252 --> 00:20:51,992
with great and strong individuality can unite into one.

537
00:20:52,362 --> 00:20:55,891
It looks like she's trying to blend multiple genres together.

538
00:20:55,892 --> 00:20:58,301
If you mix too many colors in,

539
00:20:58,302 --> 00:20:59,831
it just turns into a weird, muddy color.

540
00:20:59,832 --> 00:21:02,331
The most crucial thing in a mega crew performance is...

541
00:21:02,332 --> 00:21:03,831
the synchronization among the dancers.

542
00:21:03,832 --> 00:21:06,341
Working on all those details in a short period of time?

543
00:21:06,342 --> 00:21:07,342
That's impossible.

544
00:21:07,343 --> 00:21:09,071
She's going to regret it.

545
00:21:09,072 --> 00:21:11,011
Since it's an all-genre mega crew performance,

546
00:21:11,012 --> 00:21:13,811
I need to make versatile use of technical formations.

547
00:21:13,812 --> 00:21:15,282
(Team Simeez's practice room)

548
00:21:15,452 --> 00:21:16,782
(Floor technique)

549
00:21:17,212 --> 00:21:18,251
Yes!

550
00:21:18,252 --> 00:21:19,252
(Acrobatics)

551
00:21:19,253 --> 00:21:21,221
Technical styles like tutting, locking, waacking.

552
00:21:21,222 --> 00:21:23,952
I want to use everyone's personal weapons as our specialties.

553
00:21:24,052 --> 00:21:25,662
We're going to look so cool.

554
00:21:27,092 --> 00:21:28,292
The choreography is amazing.

555
00:21:28,662 --> 00:21:30,032
Please express yourselves.

556
00:21:30,262 --> 00:21:32,862
(How will Team Simeez, blending various genres, turn out?)

557
00:21:32,962 --> 00:21:35,101
(Out of sync)

558
00:21:35,102 --> 00:21:38,032
Maybe it's because we focused heavily on individuality.

559
00:21:38,242 --> 00:21:39,902
We do need to sync up our timing a bit.

560
00:21:40,002 --> 00:21:41,101
Since it's a mega crew mission,

561
00:21:41,102 --> 00:21:43,072
we'll need time to get in sync.

562
00:21:43,212 --> 00:21:45,182
Since my team had distinct characters...

563
00:21:45,282 --> 00:21:47,581
and many different genres,

564
00:21:47,582 --> 00:21:49,452
the movements didn't seem to sync well.

565
00:21:49,952 --> 00:21:51,011
(And so, Team Simeez started working on the details.)

566
00:21:51,012 --> 00:21:52,252
I think we should practice here more.

567
00:21:53,452 --> 00:21:54,452
(Stepping back)

568
00:21:54,453 --> 00:21:55,621
(Spotted)

569
00:21:55,622 --> 00:21:57,751
This way, Rina.

570
00:21:57,752 --> 00:22:00,422
You need to move in further here, Rina.

571
00:22:01,392 --> 00:22:02,392
Rina!

572
00:22:02,393 --> 00:22:05,061
(Rina is called out repeatedly for consecutive mistakes.)

573
00:22:05,062 --> 00:22:09,002
I cast Rina because of her technique.

574
00:22:09,932 --> 00:22:11,232
(Where have you been all this time?)

575
00:22:11,402 --> 00:22:13,071
Her technical skills were great,

576
00:22:13,072 --> 00:22:15,742
but she ended up in the front row for the most crucial part.

577
00:22:16,012 --> 00:22:19,012
Rina, you have to practice more. Please.

578
00:22:19,142 --> 00:22:20,142
Practice. Okay?

579
00:22:20,442 --> 00:22:22,081
No more mistakes from here on out.

580
00:22:22,082 --> 00:22:23,152
- Okay. - Okay.

581
00:22:23,282 --> 00:22:26,051
She'd been locked into one specific style for so long.

582
00:22:26,052 --> 00:22:27,922
She'd worn the same clothes for decades,

583
00:22:28,052 --> 00:22:30,952
so trying on a different style was tough for her, of course.

584
00:22:31,192 --> 00:22:33,222
I'm in trouble. This is our biggest hurdle.

585
00:22:33,862 --> 00:22:36,632
(The mistakes keep happening even after time passes.)

586
00:22:37,162 --> 00:22:38,231
It's this way, not that way.

587
00:22:38,232 --> 00:22:39,732
Your foot.

588
00:22:39,802 --> 00:22:41,262
This is crazy. Is it even going to work?

589
00:22:41,432 --> 00:22:42,902
It was pure despair.

590
00:22:42,972 --> 00:22:46,042
Everything had to be perfectly in sync,

591
00:22:46,202 --> 00:22:47,702
but the moves weren't coming together.

592
00:22:48,102 --> 00:22:49,112
Rina!

593
00:22:49,342 --> 00:22:52,142
I really didn't want to get on Rina's case.

594
00:22:52,342 --> 00:22:54,082
Can I have a moment with you, Rina?

595
00:22:55,412 --> 00:22:56,811
I think your timing is...

596
00:22:56,812 --> 00:22:58,222
a little bit different.

597
00:22:58,622 --> 00:23:01,622
I think we have to change your position...

598
00:23:01,722 --> 00:23:03,421
- with another person. - Okay.

599
00:23:03,422 --> 00:23:06,221
Messing up in the front row...

600
00:23:06,222 --> 00:23:08,232
throws off the entire choreography.

601
00:23:08,532 --> 00:23:10,492
I was having a total mental breakdown.

602
00:23:10,862 --> 00:23:11,901
(Groaning)

603
00:23:11,902 --> 00:23:13,962
We can do this!

604
00:23:14,062 --> 00:23:15,671
- Let's go! - Let's go!

605
00:23:15,672 --> 00:23:17,302
(Hang in there, Simeez!)

606
00:23:18,002 --> 00:23:19,942
I really want us to pull this off.

607
00:23:21,612 --> 00:23:23,172
Maybe I shouldn't have gone with all-genre dancers.

608
00:23:23,972 --> 00:23:26,042
Casting dancers is also part of a director's capability.

609
00:23:26,312 --> 00:23:28,081
Let's work on the intro choreography first.

610
00:23:28,082 --> 00:23:30,981
I think it would be great if we did it like crazy people.

611
00:23:30,982 --> 00:23:32,851
I want to bring out the crazy vibe.

612
00:23:32,852 --> 00:23:35,051
The intro. To me, that's my second highlight.

613
00:23:35,052 --> 00:23:36,622
I consider it a second chorus.

614
00:23:37,252 --> 00:23:38,392
We will start like this.

615
00:23:38,492 --> 00:23:39,621
(Dropping to our knees right from the start?)

616
00:23:39,622 --> 00:23:40,622
Yes.

617
00:23:40,623 --> 00:23:41,632
What?

618
00:23:41,792 --> 00:23:42,832
What's going on?

619
00:23:43,232 --> 00:23:45,502
We'll dance while moving like this.

620
00:23:45,702 --> 00:23:48,802
- Oh, my goodness. - A bit like a crazy person.

621
00:23:51,302 --> 00:23:52,841
That's crazy.

622
00:23:52,842 --> 00:23:53,842
I got absolute chills.

623
00:23:54,202 --> 00:23:57,771
That psycho-like madness is the point of my choreography.

624
00:23:57,772 --> 00:24:01,111
I thought about how to make it look unhinged.

625
00:24:01,112 --> 00:24:03,451
I was resting in my hotel room all drowsy.

626
00:24:03,452 --> 00:24:04,951
And I suddenly tried moving like this.

627
00:24:04,952 --> 00:24:07,622
As soon as I saw it, I went, "This is it."

628
00:24:08,022 --> 00:24:09,391
We're going to win for sure.

629
00:24:09,392 --> 00:24:11,352
This is nice. We look crazy.

630
00:24:11,492 --> 00:24:13,692
What if we try lying all the way down?

631
00:24:14,222 --> 00:24:16,291
The 1st 5 seconds must be enchanting for people to keep watching.

632
00:24:16,292 --> 00:24:17,391
This is pretty.

633
00:24:17,392 --> 00:24:19,102
The intro decides everything.

634
00:24:19,432 --> 00:24:21,002
(Chills)

635
00:24:21,532 --> 00:24:23,272
(That's how Renan's signature crazy intro was born.)

636
00:24:23,602 --> 00:24:24,632
Are you a genius?

637
00:24:26,442 --> 00:24:27,542
This is so cool.

638
00:24:27,702 --> 00:24:30,342
The dancers seem so well in sync.

639
00:24:30,742 --> 00:24:31,781
I think we can win this.

640
00:24:31,782 --> 00:24:32,782
(I think we can win this.)

641
00:24:32,882 --> 00:24:34,682
(Directors' Room for Simeez)

642
00:24:34,782 --> 00:24:36,852
The formation is way too off. What do I do?

643
00:24:37,452 --> 00:24:39,451
No matter how many times we adjusted it, it was off.

644
00:24:39,452 --> 00:24:41,281
It kept going right back to square one.

645
00:24:41,282 --> 00:24:44,152
I think it's my mistake that I went all-genre.

646
00:24:44,592 --> 00:24:46,062
What a headache.

647
00:24:49,362 --> 00:24:54,232
I want to create a truly legendary video.

648
00:24:54,432 --> 00:24:55,702
I just really want to do well.

649
00:24:56,232 --> 00:24:58,302
- You're good. - I will be good.

650
00:24:58,802 --> 00:25:00,102
Don't worry. It'll turn out great.

651
00:25:01,812 --> 00:25:04,042
I took a sneak peek at the practice video.

652
00:25:05,112 --> 00:25:06,441
- Varang. - Varang.

653
00:25:06,442 --> 00:25:07,442
Like this.

654
00:25:07,842 --> 00:25:09,782
It fits your face well, which I really like.

655
00:25:10,082 --> 00:25:11,552
It could come off as a bit childish.

656
00:25:13,022 --> 00:25:14,581
That's why I tried not to overemphasize the concept.

657
00:25:14,582 --> 00:25:16,451
I just want to show that I was inspired by it.

658
00:25:16,452 --> 00:25:18,792
You can emphasize it. It suits you well.

659
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,991
There's an area of directing I excel at,

660
00:25:20,992 --> 00:25:22,032
which is concept utilization.

661
00:25:22,062 --> 00:25:25,562
Using props is my strong suit.

662
00:25:25,662 --> 00:25:28,532
I reworked the formation to match...

663
00:25:28,632 --> 00:25:30,271
the concept properly.

664
00:25:30,272 --> 00:25:32,172
(Perfect synchronization)

665
00:25:32,272 --> 00:25:33,942
When you have something in your hands,

666
00:25:34,042 --> 00:25:35,711
even simple movements look...

667
00:25:35,712 --> 00:25:37,572
visually full and satisfying.

668
00:25:37,972 --> 00:25:40,942
- There's something I'd like to get. - Yes.

669
00:25:41,242 --> 00:25:44,352
I need something like flat boards.

670
00:25:44,452 --> 00:25:45,852
I think it will look great.

671
00:25:46,352 --> 00:25:47,681
(Amazed)

672
00:25:47,682 --> 00:25:50,291
It felt like the grandeur was multiplied.

673
00:25:50,292 --> 00:25:53,021
When utilizing props, I figured...

674
00:25:53,022 --> 00:25:54,421
I should compete through visuals and formation...

675
00:25:54,422 --> 00:25:56,492
rather than dancing.

676
00:25:57,432 --> 00:26:00,131
Something's popping up on screen. There's going to be something.

677
00:26:00,132 --> 00:26:02,401
The 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission Practice Video.

678
00:26:02,402 --> 00:26:03,702
Oh, my goodness!

679
00:26:04,172 --> 00:26:06,341
Are they shaking our minds like this?

680
00:26:06,342 --> 00:26:07,702
Honestly, that's what I wanted to see the most.

681
00:26:07,742 --> 00:26:10,611
This is going to be fun.

682
00:26:10,612 --> 00:26:11,881
Oh, gosh.

683
00:26:11,882 --> 00:26:13,582
"Predict the win or loss and directors for each matchup."

684
00:26:13,982 --> 00:26:15,852
I have to win. I put everything into making this.

685
00:26:16,012 --> 00:26:18,752
The one I'm most curious about is Simeez and Renan.

686
00:26:19,452 --> 00:26:21,252
It looked like they were doing something grand.

687
00:26:21,722 --> 00:26:23,752
It must be super flashy, true to Simeez's style.

688
00:26:24,822 --> 00:26:26,062
They're watching mine now.

689
00:26:26,122 --> 00:26:27,122
(Simeez's choreography practice)

690
00:26:27,123 --> 00:26:28,322
Gosh, hang on.

691
00:26:28,992 --> 00:26:31,632
Right from the very start.

692
00:26:32,032 --> 00:26:33,632
This is insane.

693
00:26:34,032 --> 00:26:36,001
She managed to get something incredible.

694
00:26:36,002 --> 00:26:38,031
She seems skilled at using props.

695
00:26:38,032 --> 00:26:40,341
The solar panels look great.

696
00:26:40,342 --> 00:26:41,442
Is that Waackxxxy?

697
00:26:42,612 --> 00:26:44,772
Locking!

698
00:26:45,412 --> 00:26:48,082
In the newly arranged section,

699
00:26:48,182 --> 00:26:50,412
the dance genres were utilized so appropriately.

700
00:26:50,512 --> 00:26:54,452
Watching the beginning, I was a little worried.

701
00:26:54,552 --> 00:26:56,691
I was thinking, "Oh no, what do we do?"

702
00:26:56,692 --> 00:26:59,622
But as it progressed toward the end, I felt like...

703
00:26:59,722 --> 00:27:00,821
we actually had a shot.

704
00:27:00,822 --> 00:27:02,292
But the synchronization is the issue.

705
00:27:02,392 --> 00:27:04,892
As it went on, I noticed that they were out of sync.

706
00:27:05,132 --> 00:27:07,131
Anyway, our team is well in sync.

707
00:27:07,132 --> 00:27:08,832
Let's go, Renan.

708
00:27:09,272 --> 00:27:11,631
Starting with the hand movements?

709
00:27:11,632 --> 00:27:12,642
(Renan's choreography practice)

710
00:27:12,942 --> 00:27:14,372
My goodness. That's so terrifying.

711
00:27:14,572 --> 00:27:16,742
Look at this. They look like ghosts.

712
00:27:17,412 --> 00:27:19,182
(100 percent satisfied)

713
00:27:19,412 --> 00:27:22,582
The intro is so overwhelming.

714
00:27:22,882 --> 00:27:24,552
The intro has an incredible impact.

715
00:27:24,782 --> 00:27:27,052
I don't really feel much of a clear concept.

716
00:27:27,152 --> 00:27:30,691
It feels like the tension drops during the "Bang Bang" part.

717
00:27:30,692 --> 00:27:33,362
They show the entire "Bang Bang" part from the front.

718
00:27:33,462 --> 00:27:35,021
It's like a dragging point.

719
00:27:35,022 --> 00:27:38,562
It seems she placed a lot of weight on utilizing JAYME.

720
00:27:38,732 --> 00:27:41,002
I don't think she fully understands JAYME's strengths.

721
00:27:41,932 --> 00:27:45,502
JAYME isn't the type who shines when doing the same choreography.

722
00:27:46,542 --> 00:27:47,542
The predicted credits?

723
00:27:48,142 --> 00:27:49,711
I think our team's greatest strength is our synchronization.

724
00:27:49,712 --> 00:27:52,082
I came up with such an impactful intro.

725
00:27:52,382 --> 00:27:53,982
I'm going to win this no matter what.

726
00:27:54,242 --> 00:27:55,582
I cannot lose.

727
00:27:56,112 --> 00:27:58,182
I have to take the Director Credit.

728
00:27:58,412 --> 00:27:59,621
Those who love crazy...

729
00:27:59,622 --> 00:28:01,382
and high-impact vibes...

730
00:28:01,622 --> 00:28:03,321
will probably love mine.

731
00:28:03,322 --> 00:28:05,391
I think it comes down to a matter of personal taste.

732
00:28:05,392 --> 00:28:07,162
It's not about personal taste. I want to be...

733
00:28:07,322 --> 00:28:09,162
overwhelmingly better.

734
00:28:12,262 --> 00:28:14,302
(Shocked)

735
00:28:15,672 --> 00:28:17,272
(Sighing)

736
00:28:17,932 --> 00:28:19,271
I assumed I would win.

737
00:28:19,272 --> 00:28:21,142
I was sure it would be me.

738
00:28:21,202 --> 00:28:24,442
Choreographer, Simeez. Director, Simeez.

739
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:28,512
I'm sad because the opponent is so strong.

740
00:28:30,412 --> 00:28:32,022
Gosh, that was too loud.

741
00:28:32,152 --> 00:28:35,151
Having my name listed on both the Director...

742
00:28:35,152 --> 00:28:36,221
and Choreographer Credits...

743
00:28:36,222 --> 00:28:37,552
felt amazing.

744
00:28:37,852 --> 00:28:39,262
Was I being too excited?

745
00:28:39,722 --> 00:28:41,162
(Shouting)

746
00:28:41,362 --> 00:28:44,231
(Simeez's shout echoes all the way into Renan's room.)

747
00:28:44,232 --> 00:28:45,232
(Feeling bitter)

748
00:28:45,233 --> 00:28:48,201
I kept wondering why things weren't working out,

749
00:28:48,202 --> 00:28:50,732
and my confidence hit rock bottom.

750
00:28:51,372 --> 00:28:52,642
I came here to be ambitious, after all.

751
00:28:52,702 --> 00:28:55,372
I got the Choreographer Credit to claim this.

752
00:28:55,572 --> 00:28:58,742
"The momentum in the later part leaves much to be desired."

753
00:28:58,942 --> 00:29:01,212
"The flow drags during the 'Bang Bang' part."

754
00:29:02,112 --> 00:29:04,251
"It's disappointing that the tension drops toward the end,"

755
00:29:04,252 --> 00:29:06,222
"causing the focus to fade." I see.

756
00:29:06,822 --> 00:29:09,652
(Troubled)

757
00:29:11,152 --> 00:29:13,291
There are standout dancers on the team,

758
00:29:13,292 --> 00:29:16,361
but the way they were utilized didn't seem good enough.

759
00:29:16,362 --> 00:29:19,462
There's a specific dance I could've showcased in the front,

760
00:29:19,502 --> 00:29:22,072
so performing the full choreography felt like a waste.

761
00:29:22,302 --> 00:29:23,631
It's a dance break,

762
00:29:23,632 --> 00:29:26,071
but I don't think it feels distinct from what came before.

763
00:29:26,072 --> 00:29:29,612
If I get just ten seconds, I can tear up the entire stage.

764
00:29:29,812 --> 00:29:32,881
It's disappointing that I appear for only about 0.5 seconds.

765
00:29:32,882 --> 00:29:36,412
I wonder if that was a good card to play.

766
00:29:39,382 --> 00:29:41,622
Could you please turn off the lights?

767
00:29:43,122 --> 00:29:46,522
(The lights are out in Renan's Directors' Room.)

768
00:29:47,322 --> 00:29:49,291
Even if she hears it the day before...

769
00:29:49,292 --> 00:29:51,891
I mean, your mindset can awaken,

770
00:29:51,892 --> 00:29:53,762
but it's hard to turn the tables with the piece itself in a day.

771
00:29:54,002 --> 00:29:56,572
(Renan is lost in deep thought.)

772
00:29:57,632 --> 00:29:58,971
(The night of the mid-point review)

773
00:29:58,972 --> 00:30:00,872
It's not easy.

774
00:30:02,442 --> 00:30:03,541
(Sighing)

775
00:30:03,542 --> 00:30:05,412
I was really confident,

776
00:30:05,912 --> 00:30:07,142
but why isn't this working out?

777
00:30:08,952 --> 00:30:10,211
(Street World Fighter: Directors' War)

778
00:30:10,212 --> 00:30:12,052
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

779
00:30:14,282 --> 00:30:18,321
(Who will claim the Director Credit?)

780
00:30:18,322 --> 00:30:19,861
(The 10 choreographers are entering the stage.)

781
00:30:19,862 --> 00:30:22,062
Once I stepped up there, the nerves really hit me.

782
00:30:23,062 --> 00:30:25,762
I don't think I've felt this nervous anytime recently.

783
00:30:25,932 --> 00:30:27,632
Simeez is here.

784
00:30:28,162 --> 00:30:29,901
Why does she have to be right next to me?

785
00:30:29,902 --> 00:30:31,702
It did get on my nerves.

786
00:30:33,502 --> 00:30:34,602
She's so scary.

787
00:30:34,872 --> 00:30:36,511
She's terrifying.

788
00:30:36,512 --> 00:30:38,812
Simeez, it looks like you're going to eat Renan alive.

789
00:30:39,142 --> 00:30:41,341
Seeing Simeez's outfit,

790
00:30:41,342 --> 00:30:43,051
the quality was so high...

791
00:30:43,052 --> 00:30:45,582
that I felt quite intimidated.

792
00:30:45,822 --> 00:30:47,052
I have to win.

793
00:30:47,252 --> 00:30:48,521
There's this particular feeling, you know.

794
00:30:48,522 --> 00:30:50,152
The burning rage of being wronged.

795
00:30:50,392 --> 00:30:53,291
There is a distinct fury known only to those who have lost.

796
00:30:53,292 --> 00:30:55,562
I am going to win this, no matter what.

797
00:30:57,192 --> 00:30:58,862
Hash is here.

798
00:31:00,702 --> 00:31:04,672
MIN JUN had a gentler look in his eyes at first.

799
00:31:05,072 --> 00:31:08,301
But the look in his eyes changed. He looks so determined...

800
00:31:08,302 --> 00:31:10,242
to beat me down.

801
00:31:10,872 --> 00:31:13,841
If I said I was confident, it would be a lie.

802
00:31:13,842 --> 00:31:17,282
You can never underestimate someone with an extensive career.

803
00:31:17,482 --> 00:31:18,882
I'm keeping a close eye on her.

804
00:31:20,022 --> 00:31:22,251
- Hello. - Hi.

805
00:31:22,252 --> 00:31:23,252
Hello.

806
00:31:23,253 --> 00:31:24,722
(Looking away)

807
00:31:25,862 --> 00:31:28,591
I saw an uncomfortable energy, so I tried to stay relaxed.

808
00:31:28,592 --> 00:31:29,592
(Exclaiming)

809
00:31:29,732 --> 00:31:32,961
Deep down, I felt an intense sense of crisis...

810
00:31:32,962 --> 00:31:34,301
and competitiveness,

811
00:31:34,302 --> 00:31:37,202
but I hid it and kept practicing mental control.

812
00:31:37,702 --> 00:31:38,742
(Surprised)

813
00:31:39,542 --> 00:31:40,701
The judges are here.

814
00:31:40,702 --> 00:31:41,702
Who are they?

815
00:31:41,703 --> 00:31:42,711
(Surprised)

816
00:31:42,712 --> 00:31:43,942
(The first judge for the Last Run enters.)

817
00:31:45,242 --> 00:31:47,312
(Passionate welcome)

818
00:31:50,152 --> 00:31:52,012
(Monika left a powerful impression through "Street Woman Fighter.")

819
00:31:52,352 --> 00:31:53,851
A director with distinct visual pictures, clear themes,

820
00:31:53,852 --> 00:31:55,152
and storytelling.

821
00:31:55,852 --> 00:31:57,992
A director who is active across various fields...

822
00:31:58,222 --> 00:32:00,392
and respected by everyone.

823
00:32:01,122 --> 00:32:02,561
Monika!

824
00:32:02,562 --> 00:32:03,562
(Heart)

825
00:32:03,563 --> 00:32:06,331
When Monika came out, I felt a slight twinge.

826
00:32:06,332 --> 00:32:09,702
Because Lip J was on MIN JUN's team.

827
00:32:09,932 --> 00:32:11,331
We haven't been in touch for five days.

828
00:32:11,332 --> 00:32:13,602
Please make sure to spread the word that I'll be fair.

829
00:32:13,942 --> 00:32:16,771
She is sharp, detail-oriented, and decisive.

830
00:32:16,772 --> 00:32:19,682
I thought she would deliver a decisive opinion for one side.

831
00:32:20,112 --> 00:32:21,241
(Next, the second judge for the Last Run enters.)

832
00:32:21,242 --> 00:32:22,451
(Jae Won?)

833
00:32:22,452 --> 00:32:23,912
Jae Won!

834
00:32:24,212 --> 00:32:25,622
It's Jae Won. This is crazy.

835
00:32:25,682 --> 00:32:28,321
He is someone every SM Entertainment fan knows.

836
00:32:28,322 --> 00:32:31,951
In Korea, he is like the cornerstone of performance directing.

837
00:32:31,952 --> 00:32:33,492
The best performance director.

838
00:32:34,162 --> 00:32:35,431
(Starting with "Into the New World" by Girls' Generation)

839
00:32:35,432 --> 00:32:36,491
(SHINee in 2008)

840
00:32:36,492 --> 00:32:37,492
(EXO in 2012)

841
00:32:37,492 --> 00:32:38,492
(Red Velvet in 2014)

842
00:32:38,493 --> 00:32:39,502
(aespa in 2020)

843
00:32:39,832 --> 00:32:41,502
(The choreographer who established the standard for SM's performances)

844
00:32:42,272 --> 00:32:44,332
(The person who directs every single moment on stage)

845
00:32:44,602 --> 00:32:46,872
(Performance Director Shim Jae Won)

846
00:32:47,372 --> 00:32:48,771
He's worked as a performance director for a long.

847
00:32:48,772 --> 00:32:51,511
I believe he will accurately evaluate...

848
00:32:51,512 --> 00:32:53,611
the qualities and role of a director.

849
00:32:53,612 --> 00:32:55,082
It felt reassuring.

850
00:32:55,582 --> 00:32:57,911
- Jae Won! - Jae Won!

851
00:32:57,912 --> 00:32:58,921
Did you know about this?

852
00:32:58,922 --> 00:32:59,922
I had no idea.

853
00:32:59,923 --> 00:33:01,321
(Sighing)

854
00:33:01,322 --> 00:33:02,921
I thought I wouldn't be nervous.

855
00:33:02,922 --> 00:33:04,452
But cold sweat was dripping down my spine.

856
00:33:04,652 --> 00:33:08,361
Jae Won helped me tremendously in my growth.

857
00:33:08,362 --> 00:33:10,231
He's a master who gave me...

858
00:33:10,232 --> 00:33:11,391
so many teachings.

859
00:33:11,392 --> 00:33:13,331
With Koo Young on my right...

860
00:33:13,332 --> 00:33:15,971
and Jae Won sitting there judging us,

861
00:33:15,972 --> 00:33:17,672
an overwhelming emotion suddenly rushed over me.

862
00:33:17,802 --> 00:33:19,902
I wanted to prove myself with performances.

863
00:33:20,372 --> 00:33:21,702
(Surprised)

864
00:33:21,942 --> 00:33:23,412
The person who's meant to come is finally here.

865
00:33:23,742 --> 00:33:24,742
(The third judge enters next.)

866
00:33:26,112 --> 00:33:27,881
Anthony!

867
00:33:27,882 --> 00:33:29,511
I really didn't expect him to come.

868
00:33:29,512 --> 00:33:30,512
My name is Anthony,

869
00:33:30,513 --> 00:33:31,611
representing the KINJAZ crew.

870
00:33:31,612 --> 00:33:33,152
I'm also one of the creative directors.

871
00:33:34,752 --> 00:33:37,452
He is someone leading the global trend of performance.

872
00:33:37,792 --> 00:33:39,122
(The core creator of KINJAZ)

873
00:33:40,192 --> 00:33:41,962
(For his unrivaled, world-class directing skills,)

874
00:33:42,632 --> 00:33:44,162
(Anthony Lee is recognized globally as a world-renowned director.)

875
00:33:44,732 --> 00:33:48,532
Being able to tell a story through my own piece was a huge opportunity.

876
00:33:49,672 --> 00:33:52,441
I was so glad to see him because I love KINJAZ so much.

877
00:33:52,442 --> 00:33:55,172
But I got nervous because I had to be evaluated.

878
00:33:55,302 --> 00:33:58,041
They are all prominent figures in the scene.

879
00:33:58,042 --> 00:34:01,041
I thought we had the rightful judges.

880
00:34:01,042 --> 00:34:02,711
I'm going to get evaluated properly.

881
00:34:02,712 --> 00:34:04,351
I think it started to hit me.

882
00:34:04,352 --> 00:34:06,122
"It's really starting now."

883
00:34:06,682 --> 00:34:09,221
In the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission,

884
00:34:09,222 --> 00:34:10,951
choreographers will be evaluated...

885
00:34:10,952 --> 00:34:13,321
on how they reinterpreted the same signature choreography,

886
00:34:13,322 --> 00:34:14,821
by assessing formations and compositions,

887
00:34:14,822 --> 00:34:16,891
the utilization of main and supporting characters,

888
00:34:16,892 --> 00:34:19,901
and the overall impact delivered on stage.

889
00:34:19,902 --> 00:34:23,731
Only one winning choreographer from each matchup...

890
00:34:23,732 --> 00:34:27,171
will leave their name on the Director Credit.

891
00:34:27,172 --> 00:34:29,472
The 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

892
00:34:29,712 --> 00:34:32,141
We will start the Last Run.

893
00:34:32,142 --> 00:34:33,712
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

894
00:34:34,112 --> 00:34:35,242
Let's go!

895
00:34:35,712 --> 00:34:38,052
My goal is to get my name up there as Director too.

896
00:34:38,182 --> 00:34:41,052
The most important thing was to get my name on the Director Credit.

897
00:34:41,182 --> 00:34:42,792
I have to get it up there, no matter what.

898
00:34:43,592 --> 00:34:44,752
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission, the 1st matchup)

899
00:34:44,892 --> 00:34:48,392
We will now begin the Last Run for the Simeez versus Renan matchup.

900
00:34:49,132 --> 00:34:50,632
Don't be nervous.

901
00:34:50,832 --> 00:34:51,832
We have to do this.

902
00:34:51,833 --> 00:34:52,962
We have to nail it.

903
00:34:53,162 --> 00:34:56,571
Entering together like this made me so nervous.

904
00:34:56,572 --> 00:34:59,271
The pressure was real.

905
00:34:59,272 --> 00:35:02,271
But the look in my crew's eyes and their fierce drive...

906
00:35:02,272 --> 00:35:03,611
gave me confidence,

907
00:35:03,612 --> 00:35:05,812
which eased a lot of my nerves.

908
00:35:07,412 --> 00:35:11,512
The dancers' energy gave me an extra boost of strength.

909
00:35:12,152 --> 00:35:13,882
This feels like a Korea-Japan showdown.

910
00:35:14,382 --> 00:35:15,752
I'm going to win for sure.

911
00:35:15,922 --> 00:35:17,022
No one can beat me.

912
00:35:17,422 --> 00:35:19,021
Team Simeez will enter first.

913
00:35:19,022 --> 00:35:20,062
(Team Simeez)

914
00:35:20,162 --> 00:35:21,821
(Team Renan)

915
00:35:21,822 --> 00:35:24,792
Dancers, please move to the standing area.

916
00:35:26,132 --> 00:35:27,301
(Team Simeez versus Team Renan, the dancers' entry is complete.)

917
00:35:27,302 --> 00:35:28,731
Renan is the best!

918
00:35:28,732 --> 00:35:30,172
- Renan is the best! - Renan is the best!

919
00:35:30,202 --> 00:35:31,601
- Renan is the best! - Renan is the best!

920
00:35:31,602 --> 00:35:33,072
(Happy)

921
00:35:33,402 --> 00:35:36,011
Having my dancers behind me...

922
00:35:36,012 --> 00:35:38,412
gave me a boost of confidence without even realizing it.

923
00:35:38,612 --> 00:35:41,411
- Renan is the best! - Simeez!

924
00:35:41,412 --> 00:35:44,812
- Renan is the best! - Simeez!

925
00:35:44,952 --> 00:35:46,522
We are going to kill it.

926
00:35:47,022 --> 00:35:50,592
We will now begin the Last Run for the Simeez versus Renan matchup.

927
00:35:51,522 --> 00:35:52,792
Look at her costume.

928
00:35:55,092 --> 00:35:56,792
(The 8 teams' green rooms are on air.)

929
00:35:57,262 --> 00:35:58,762
Their outfits are so intense.

930
00:35:59,232 --> 00:36:00,502
I bet Simeez is going to win.

931
00:36:00,602 --> 00:36:01,902
She's just so overwhelming.

932
00:36:02,162 --> 00:36:03,871
The impact is seriously strong.

933
00:36:03,872 --> 00:36:05,031
(Overwhelming)

934
00:36:05,032 --> 00:36:08,172
It's the toes for me. It's the shoes that make it crazy.

935
00:36:08,502 --> 00:36:10,612
I paid attention all the way down to the shoes.

936
00:36:11,612 --> 00:36:12,982
She painted her feet.

937
00:36:13,282 --> 00:36:14,782
She came in with determination.

938
00:36:14,842 --> 00:36:15,882
But...

939
00:36:16,012 --> 00:36:19,181
Renan has so many original moves up her sleeve.

940
00:36:19,182 --> 00:36:21,251
She's a director who excels so much at composition.

941
00:36:21,252 --> 00:36:22,592
She is a dark horse.

942
00:36:22,822 --> 00:36:26,462
I'll deliver an even greater impact through versatile formations.

943
00:36:26,962 --> 00:36:29,962
The Last Run of the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission,

944
00:36:30,262 --> 00:36:31,632
Simeez versus Renan.

945
00:36:32,032 --> 00:36:35,232
We will start with Renan's Last Run first!

946
00:36:35,262 --> 00:36:36,471
(Simeez versus Renan, 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

947
00:36:36,472 --> 00:36:37,801
My goodness!

948
00:36:37,802 --> 00:36:39,471
It's starting now.

949
00:36:39,472 --> 00:36:40,801
I'm so nervous.

950
00:36:40,802 --> 00:36:42,172
We can do this.

951
00:36:42,812 --> 00:36:44,542
It won't be easy for Renan...

952
00:36:44,812 --> 00:36:46,582
to erase the original choreography of "Bang Bang."

953
00:36:48,142 --> 00:36:51,382
The whole process was far from easy.

954
00:36:51,712 --> 00:36:54,782
My pride and confidence hit rock bottom.

955
00:36:54,952 --> 00:36:57,421
Simeez crafted the choreography so well.

956
00:36:57,422 --> 00:36:58,992
I have to give credit where credit is due.

957
00:36:59,192 --> 00:37:01,921
What winning factors do I even have?

958
00:37:01,922 --> 00:37:03,791
Props? Concept?

959
00:37:03,792 --> 00:37:04,932
There were none.

960
00:37:05,162 --> 00:37:07,002
(Rehearsal D-1)

961
00:37:07,432 --> 00:37:10,502
I have some unfortunate news.

962
00:37:10,632 --> 00:37:13,672
We need a massive overhaul of "Bang Bang."

963
00:37:14,372 --> 00:37:18,142
Yes. There will be major revisions.

964
00:37:18,412 --> 00:37:20,012
I'm shocked as well.

965
00:37:20,242 --> 00:37:21,542
It broke my heart.

966
00:37:21,682 --> 00:37:23,182
What if it brings everyone down?

967
00:37:23,912 --> 00:37:26,521
We were confident, thinking that...

968
00:37:26,522 --> 00:37:28,722
we were cool and we would win.

969
00:37:29,222 --> 00:37:31,092
My heart felt so heavy.

970
00:37:31,992 --> 00:37:33,361
Please go to your initial positions...

971
00:37:33,362 --> 00:37:35,792
- for "Bang Bang." - The initial positions.

972
00:37:36,932 --> 00:37:38,661
It starts like this.

973
00:37:38,662 --> 00:37:41,301
I needed to try a different vibe, which is bigger and more powerful.

974
00:37:41,302 --> 00:37:44,432
One, two, three, four, five, six...

975
00:37:45,172 --> 00:37:46,541
I'm sorry. We need to take this out.

976
00:37:46,542 --> 00:37:47,901
- Forget about it. - Okay.

977
00:37:47,902 --> 00:37:49,311
I was hitting a wall right from the start.

978
00:37:49,312 --> 00:37:51,941
Could we make the front row into a horizontal line like this?

979
00:37:51,942 --> 00:37:53,081
With JAYME in the center.

980
00:37:53,082 --> 00:37:54,082
I see.

981
00:37:54,083 --> 00:37:55,542
I'm sorry. This isn't it.

982
00:37:55,782 --> 00:37:57,582
Can we try this move right here?

983
00:37:59,322 --> 00:38:01,281
Or can you try raising your arms?

984
00:38:01,282 --> 00:38:02,282
One, two.

985
00:38:02,283 --> 00:38:03,491
Can you try it while standing up?

986
00:38:03,492 --> 00:38:04,591
One, two.

987
00:38:04,592 --> 00:38:06,062
Hang on a second.

988
00:38:06,462 --> 00:38:08,962
Her energy wasn't going up. She was being sensitive.

989
00:38:09,092 --> 00:38:11,162
It feels like our energy is draining.

990
00:38:11,462 --> 00:38:13,462
My mind is checked out right now.

991
00:38:13,732 --> 00:38:17,132
Time is running out, but my brain just won't work.

992
00:38:17,872 --> 00:38:20,542
I can see the dancers getting exhausted.

993
00:38:21,372 --> 00:38:22,612
This isn't easy.

994
00:38:23,072 --> 00:38:24,772
Can we take a quick five-minute break?

995
00:38:25,012 --> 00:38:26,512
I'm sorry. Wait a moment.

996
00:38:27,912 --> 00:38:30,282
We're ruined.

997
00:38:30,852 --> 00:38:32,152
We're in trouble.

998
00:38:34,452 --> 00:38:37,721
(In the end, she bursts into tears.)

999
00:38:37,722 --> 00:38:39,721
Tears started flowing before I even realized it.

1000
00:38:39,722 --> 00:38:41,422
I was so heartbroken and overwhelmed.

1001
00:38:41,762 --> 00:38:45,061
I kept pretending to be fine...

1002
00:38:45,062 --> 00:38:47,332
and tried my hardest not to show it.

1003
00:38:48,062 --> 00:38:49,572
I worked really hard.

1004
00:38:52,472 --> 00:38:55,401
As bad results kept repeating,

1005
00:38:55,402 --> 00:38:56,972
my mental state was shattered,

1006
00:38:57,372 --> 00:39:00,242
and I felt like giving up.

1007
00:39:01,042 --> 00:39:02,141
Is she going to be okay?

1008
00:39:02,142 --> 00:39:03,411
(The practice room remains frozen in place.)

1009
00:39:03,412 --> 00:39:04,582
(Walking on eggshells)

1010
00:39:04,952 --> 00:39:09,152
Shall we keep working on the poses like this?

1011
00:39:09,952 --> 00:39:11,522
How about working on the poses?

1012
00:39:11,822 --> 00:39:13,921
We can do this. Something like this.

1013
00:39:13,922 --> 00:39:14,961
It's not that hard, is it?

1014
00:39:14,962 --> 00:39:16,961
- Like this. - Make it.

1015
00:39:16,962 --> 00:39:18,932
It would be beautiful if you make it a little better.

1016
00:39:19,502 --> 00:39:21,702
- You got this. - Great.

1017
00:39:21,932 --> 00:39:23,932
That's when I came to my senses.

1018
00:39:24,332 --> 00:39:25,731
I'm the director.

1019
00:39:25,732 --> 00:39:27,941
There's a performance I'm in charge of,

1020
00:39:27,942 --> 00:39:29,971
and there are dancers under my wing,

1021
00:39:29,972 --> 00:39:32,212
so I can't give up like this.

1022
00:39:33,112 --> 00:39:35,782
Because I've got the teammates who got my back,

1023
00:39:36,182 --> 00:39:37,852
I have to try everything I can.

1024
00:39:38,682 --> 00:39:41,322
I apologize for the major change.

1025
00:39:41,452 --> 00:39:43,122
But it's all for a good result.

1026
00:39:43,392 --> 00:39:45,391
- Let's do it! - Let's go!

1027
00:39:45,392 --> 00:39:46,761
(Our team's the best!)

1028
00:39:46,762 --> 00:39:49,231
It had to be easy enough for them to learn in a day,

1029
00:39:49,232 --> 00:39:50,361
and the moves had to be clear.

1030
00:39:50,362 --> 00:39:52,092
And the dancers had to shine.

1031
00:39:52,392 --> 00:39:53,832
I sized up the team.

1032
00:39:54,162 --> 00:39:55,661
I fixed the moves to be as flashy as possible...

1033
00:39:55,662 --> 00:39:57,532
and made the movements bigger.

1034
00:39:58,702 --> 00:40:00,742
JAYME will do some voguing in his part.

1035
00:40:01,602 --> 00:40:05,072
I changed the choreography to utilize each dancer's strength.

1036
00:40:05,372 --> 00:40:07,041
(The quality improves as she fixes the choreography one at a time.)

1037
00:40:07,042 --> 00:40:09,282
Seeing everyone happy made me happy.

1038
00:40:09,682 --> 00:40:11,012
I'm glad I made the changes.

1039
00:40:11,112 --> 00:40:13,551
If they see the changes I've made in a day,

1040
00:40:13,552 --> 00:40:15,022
they will say I'm mad.

1041
00:40:15,752 --> 00:40:17,852
Team Renan will enter now.

1042
00:40:19,392 --> 00:40:20,491
Now I just need to make sure...

1043
00:40:20,492 --> 00:40:21,592
- everything goes smoothly on site. - Okay.

1044
00:40:21,992 --> 00:40:23,032
Renan.

1045
00:40:23,592 --> 00:40:27,131
I've seen her a couple of times when working with aespa.

1046
00:40:27,132 --> 00:40:29,371
I remember her as someone who's good at composition.

1047
00:40:29,372 --> 00:40:31,601
It's fascinating to see the process.

1048
00:40:31,602 --> 00:40:32,802
She must be shocked...

1049
00:40:32,902 --> 00:40:34,772
that we are watching the rehearsal.

1050
00:40:35,472 --> 00:40:37,541
You have an hour and 20 minutes to rehearse.

1051
00:40:37,542 --> 00:40:39,281
(The 1-hour-and-20-minute rehearsal countdown begins.)

1052
00:40:39,282 --> 00:40:40,942
Who's going up to the second floor?

1053
00:40:41,082 --> 00:40:42,541
Should we check the path?

1054
00:40:42,542 --> 00:40:43,551
Yes!

1055
00:40:43,552 --> 00:40:44,711
She's got JAYME.

1056
00:40:44,712 --> 00:40:46,752
I guess JAYME appears from the second floor.

1057
00:40:47,282 --> 00:40:50,251
If she's using the second floor, time will be very tight.

1058
00:40:50,252 --> 00:40:52,051
- She has to check the distance too. - Right.

1059
00:40:52,052 --> 00:40:53,921
It's quite a distance, so she should consider the timing.

1060
00:40:53,922 --> 00:40:55,092
It's very hard.

1061
00:40:56,162 --> 00:40:58,262
Let's dance to the music.

1062
00:40:58,362 --> 00:40:59,362
Okay.

1063
00:40:59,363 --> 00:41:01,801
She's watching from the judges' point of view.

1064
00:41:01,802 --> 00:41:03,101
She is aware of...

1065
00:41:03,102 --> 00:41:04,631
who she's showing it to.

1066
00:41:04,632 --> 00:41:05,831
That's what's great.

1067
00:41:05,832 --> 00:41:07,872
It seems she's got the habit of looking at the big picture.

1068
00:41:08,472 --> 00:41:10,111
- There goes JAYME. - Yes.

1069
00:41:10,112 --> 00:41:11,272
That must be the spot.

1070
00:41:11,612 --> 00:41:12,712
