As for me, it made me...

1335
00:52:58,352 --> 00:53:01,081
realize once again how passionate...

1336
00:53:01,082 --> 00:53:02,221
Simeez really is.

1337
00:53:02,222 --> 00:53:03,451
It's knee-walking versus...

1338
00:53:03,452 --> 00:53:05,752
mirror standing.

1339
00:53:06,452 --> 00:53:07,462
Yo.

1340
00:53:07,862 --> 00:53:09,991
- That was difficult for me. - It's so difficult.

1341
00:53:09,992 --> 00:53:11,861
- Yes, that was difficult. - Different styles.

1342
00:53:11,862 --> 00:53:14,331
I thought they would be surprised to see our performance.

1343
00:53:14,332 --> 00:53:16,001
I thought my performance had the power to win them over.

1344
00:53:16,002 --> 00:53:17,171
We did everything we could,

1345
00:53:17,172 --> 00:53:18,801
and we gave it our best.

1346
00:53:18,802 --> 00:53:20,902
What would the judges think?

1347
00:53:21,142 --> 00:53:22,742
(What would the judges say about the two choreographers?)

1348
00:53:22,902 --> 00:53:25,612
You two ladies, this is going to be a difficult one.

1349
00:53:25,772 --> 00:53:27,811
Simeez, what was good in your show...

1350
00:53:27,812 --> 00:53:30,181
was weak in Renan's show.

1351
00:53:30,182 --> 00:53:32,981
And what was good in your show was weak in her show.

1352
00:53:32,982 --> 00:53:36,151
That makes it complicated, and that makes it fun at the same time.

1353
00:53:36,152 --> 00:53:39,291
So it just depends on what we're going to put value in today.

1354
00:53:39,292 --> 00:53:40,522
(Agreeing)

1355
00:53:40,692 --> 00:53:42,492
(What's the judges' choice?)

1356
00:53:42,622 --> 00:53:44,391
I think Renan's show was just better...

1357
00:53:44,392 --> 00:53:46,161
and there was a more mature offering of movement.

1358
00:53:46,162 --> 00:53:48,762
I think there was more uniqueness. I think it started off strong.

1359
00:53:49,002 --> 00:53:51,432
(Renan's intro captured attention from the start.)

1360
00:53:51,532 --> 00:53:53,471
As each phrase built, the way they unleashed...

1361
00:53:53,472 --> 00:53:55,771
more and more energy...

1362
00:53:55,772 --> 00:53:57,412
looked incredible.

1363
00:53:57,912 --> 00:54:01,481
They created such a powerful stage picture...

1364
00:54:01,482 --> 00:54:04,352
that it made me want to be up there with them.

1365
00:54:04,912 --> 00:54:07,981
It made me realize that the energy I wanted to convey...

1366
00:54:07,982 --> 00:54:09,081
really came across.

1367
00:54:09,082 --> 00:54:12,122
Here's my impression of Simeez's performance.

1368
00:54:13,092 --> 00:54:16,561
I thought the intro was impactful enough...

1369
00:54:16,562 --> 00:54:19,862
to make me think of a Las Vegas show.

1370
00:54:22,032 --> 00:54:24,431
She drew inspiration from the Avatar characters,

1371
00:54:24,432 --> 00:54:26,771
introducing the Fire Tribe and the Water Tribe...

1372
00:54:26,772 --> 00:54:28,901
and setting up a clear conflict between them.

1373
00:54:28,902 --> 00:54:31,972
I thought it was a very intuitive and effective way to stage it.

1374
00:54:35,912 --> 00:54:37,111
How did she think of pulling off a concept like this...

1375
00:54:37,112 --> 00:54:38,881
in such a short given time?

1376
00:54:38,882 --> 00:54:41,622
She's got some serious guts.

1377
00:54:41,922 --> 00:54:45,151
She chose the lift a female dancer would usually avoid.

1378
00:54:45,152 --> 00:54:48,092
She chose an object that's too big to handle.

1379
00:54:48,122 --> 00:54:50,361
I think she constantly wants to break something.

1380
00:54:50,362 --> 00:54:52,531
Seeing her creating what she wants to do...

1381
00:54:52,532 --> 00:54:53,761
and continuing to challenge herself,

1382
00:54:53,762 --> 00:54:55,931
I admire her.

1383
00:54:55,932 --> 00:54:58,832
I believe it's the virtue a choreographer must possess.

1384
00:54:59,732 --> 00:55:02,441
I was very grateful to her for recognizing the challenge I took on.

1385
00:55:02,442 --> 00:55:04,041
It made me realize that my decision was right.

1386
00:55:04,042 --> 00:55:05,211
Ten years from now,

1387
00:55:05,212 --> 00:55:08,081
if you ask me to describe your show,

1388
00:55:08,082 --> 00:55:10,181
I will be able to describe your show easily.

1389
00:55:10,182 --> 00:55:14,082
I also gave a lot of points in props which were memorable.

1390
00:55:14,522 --> 00:55:17,551
The judges praised Simeez's performance.

1391
00:55:17,552 --> 00:55:20,292
I wasn't sure what was going to happen.

1392
00:55:21,062 --> 00:55:23,191
I think it boils down to the difference in energy.

1393
00:55:23,192 --> 00:55:24,331
- Difference in energy. - Yes.

1394
00:55:24,332 --> 00:55:25,332
Who do you think will win?

1395
00:55:25,333 --> 00:55:26,362
Raise your hand if it's Simeez.

1396
00:55:26,832 --> 00:55:28,002
Raise your hand if it's Renan.

1397
00:55:28,962 --> 00:55:30,502
It's hard to tell.

1398
00:55:32,202 --> 00:55:33,901
Here's what I don't understand.

1399
00:55:33,902 --> 00:55:35,801
There was still room for improvement.

1400
00:55:35,802 --> 00:55:37,141
Yes, she's a dancer with quality.

1401
00:55:37,142 --> 00:55:39,211
But she was abandoned after just one use.

1402
00:55:39,212 --> 00:55:40,581
I believe it's the director's role...

1403
00:55:40,582 --> 00:55:42,381
- to lead the team stably. - Yes.

1404
00:55:42,382 --> 00:55:44,911
But when we consider the result,

1405
00:55:44,912 --> 00:55:47,551
it would've been better if her show had had something...

1406
00:55:47,552 --> 00:55:49,122
that was strong enough to overwhelm us.

1407
00:55:49,352 --> 00:55:51,521
It would've been good if she had been bold enough...

1408
00:55:51,522 --> 00:55:53,321
to take the risk of taking a different path.

1409
00:55:53,322 --> 00:55:55,392
Actually, that's what's fun.

1410
00:55:55,492 --> 00:55:57,691
I feel like it's a little cheesy.

1411
00:55:57,692 --> 00:56:00,031
I just don't think she did it well enough.

1412
00:56:00,032 --> 00:56:01,362
- Right. - Right.

1413
00:56:01,902 --> 00:56:05,002
Why is the meeting getting longer?

1414
00:56:05,102 --> 00:56:07,642
I have to win here.

1415
00:56:07,702 --> 00:56:12,042
It would be devastating if I can't perform...

1416
00:56:12,842 --> 00:56:14,682
in front of an audience.

1417
00:56:14,912 --> 00:56:17,351
They put their trust in me and followed my lead.

1418
00:56:17,352 --> 00:56:20,622
I was worried that my conviction might have been wrong.

1419
00:56:21,552 --> 00:56:23,622
1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

1420
00:56:23,792 --> 00:56:26,861
Who will be able to showcase her work to the audience...

1421
00:56:26,862 --> 00:56:30,432
and put her name on the Credit Board?

1422
00:56:30,592 --> 00:56:32,061
(Hands held tightly together)

1423
00:56:32,062 --> 00:56:33,732
(It has to be us.)

1424
00:56:34,632 --> 00:56:37,972
The choreographer whose name will go on the Credit Board is...

1425
00:56:38,472 --> 00:56:41,041
Renan showcased a variety of things.

1426
00:56:41,042 --> 00:56:42,042
Renan did such a good job.

1427
00:56:42,043 --> 00:56:45,312
In terms of development and flow, Simeez did better.

1428
00:56:45,442 --> 00:56:46,612
It's...

1429
00:56:46,672 --> 00:56:48,481
I have to win.

1430
00:56:48,482 --> 00:56:50,412
It has to be my name.

1431
00:56:50,782 --> 00:56:52,051
The director?

1432
00:56:52,052 --> 00:56:53,452
It has to be Simeez.

1433
00:56:54,452 --> 00:56:55,452
It's...

1434
00:56:55,453 --> 00:56:58,092
(To be continued)

1435
00:56:58,552 --> 00:57:00,761
1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

1436
00:57:00,762 --> 00:57:03,831
Who will be able to showcase her work to the audience...

1437
00:57:03,832 --> 00:57:07,302
and put her name on the Credit Board?

1438
00:57:07,562 --> 00:57:09,001
(Hands held tightly together)

1439
00:57:09,002 --> 00:57:10,672
(It has to be us.)

1440
00:57:11,432 --> 00:57:12,502
It's...

1441
00:57:12,702 --> 00:57:14,501
I have to win.

1442
00:57:14,502 --> 00:57:16,542
It has to be my name.

1443
00:57:16,802 --> 00:57:18,071
The director?

1444
00:57:18,072 --> 00:57:19,372
It has to be Simeez.

1445
00:57:20,482 --> 00:57:21,512
It's...

1446
00:57:25,612 --> 00:57:26,852
(Renan wins.)

1447
00:57:28,182 --> 00:57:29,821
It's Renan.

1448
00:57:29,822 --> 00:57:33,452
(Renan put her name on the Director Credit.)

1449
00:57:40,062 --> 00:57:41,201
(Walking on his knees)

1450
00:57:41,202 --> 00:57:42,832
(The result shocks everyone.)

1451
00:57:43,032 --> 00:57:45,271
My name, "Renan" was on the screen.

1452
00:57:45,272 --> 00:57:46,631
I thought I was dreaming.

1453
00:57:46,632 --> 00:57:50,371
I was thrilled beyond words.

1454
00:57:50,372 --> 00:57:51,411
I was so happy.

1455
00:57:51,412 --> 00:57:53,272
(Feeling sorry)

1456
00:57:53,472 --> 00:57:58,682
(Team Renan's dancers enjoy the victory with her.)

1457
00:57:59,512 --> 00:58:00,822
Thank you.

1458
00:58:02,152 --> 00:58:04,151
In terms of utilizing dancers,

1459
00:58:04,152 --> 00:58:06,451
Renan's choice...

1460
00:58:06,452 --> 00:58:08,062
hit home for me.

1461
00:58:08,322 --> 00:58:11,161
I agree with what she said about the dancer utilization.

1462
00:58:11,162 --> 00:58:13,861
The way that she should've debut Waackxxxy...

1463
00:58:13,862 --> 00:58:15,101
It should've been a blowup.

1464
00:58:15,102 --> 00:58:16,102
- That's right. - Yes.

1465
00:58:16,103 --> 00:58:18,331
But she kind of just walks forward, and she's not in the center.

1466
00:58:18,332 --> 00:58:19,601
And you're like, is there...

1467
00:58:19,602 --> 00:58:21,201
I agree wholeheartedly.

1468
00:58:21,202 --> 00:58:23,771
JAYME? Seeing him up there, the way that he...

1469
00:58:23,772 --> 00:58:26,011
The way he walks in front, I'm like,

1470
00:58:26,012 --> 00:58:28,241
that's a blowup. That's a powerful way to have...

1471
00:58:28,242 --> 00:58:30,081
It's not even just dancer utilization.

1472
00:58:30,082 --> 00:58:32,151
It's the setup, the formation, the transition.

1473
00:58:32,152 --> 00:58:33,851
(She agrees.)

1474
00:58:33,852 --> 00:58:36,422
The charm of JAYME...

1475
00:58:36,582 --> 00:58:38,292
was expressed very well.

1476
00:58:38,492 --> 00:58:41,021
I really liked how you used the second floor.

1477
00:58:41,022 --> 00:58:43,762
I was deeply moved by that.

1478
00:58:44,132 --> 00:58:46,892
It was worth redoing the whole "BANG BANG" part.

1479
00:58:47,662 --> 00:58:48,832
Choreographer Renan.

1480
00:58:49,062 --> 00:58:51,571
You became the director of the first mission,

1481
00:58:51,572 --> 00:58:54,342
and you'll be able to showcase your performance to the audience.

1482
00:58:54,802 --> 00:58:57,741
Last night, I prayed for a miracle...

1483
00:58:57,742 --> 00:58:59,272
before I went to bed.

1484
00:58:59,712 --> 00:59:02,341
I changed the choreography over and over again,

1485
00:59:02,342 --> 00:59:05,111
and it gave me the chance to grow.

1486
00:59:05,112 --> 00:59:09,452
I'd like to thank everyone who gave me such a good opportunity.

1487
00:59:09,782 --> 00:59:10,822
Thank you.

1488
00:59:11,192 --> 00:59:14,691
(You're so cool, Director Renan!)

1489
00:59:14,692 --> 00:59:18,132
Actually, losing wasn't an option, so I'm...

1490
00:59:19,492 --> 00:59:21,232
- You did well. - Yes.

1491
00:59:21,362 --> 00:59:22,761
(You're the best, Simeez.)

1492
00:59:22,762 --> 00:59:26,302
I'm just glad I was able to work with all of them.

1493
00:59:26,772 --> 00:59:28,672
Thank you so much.

1494
00:59:28,802 --> 00:59:30,712
I love you!

1495
00:59:32,772 --> 00:59:35,682
I did take over the signature choreography,

1496
00:59:35,842 --> 00:59:37,711
and I didn't expect to lose.

1497
00:59:37,712 --> 00:59:41,622
I'm sad that my name didn't go up on the Credit Board as the director.

1498
00:59:41,782 --> 00:59:43,681
- Captain! - Good job.

1499
00:59:43,682 --> 00:59:45,952
- You're cool. - You're cool.

1500
00:59:46,692 --> 00:59:48,192
Good job.

1501
00:59:48,762 --> 00:59:50,761
The only choreographer...

1502
00:59:50,762 --> 00:59:53,132
who successfully left her name on this stage...

1503
00:59:53,332 --> 00:59:55,732
was Renan.

1504
00:59:55,932 --> 00:59:58,102
Renan, please prepare your performance.

1505
00:59:58,202 --> 01:00:00,442
- Thank you. - You worked hard.

1506
01:00:00,842 --> 01:00:01,872
Thank you.

1507
01:00:03,502 --> 01:00:04,941
(The battle between the two heated rivals...)

1508
01:00:04,942 --> 01:00:06,712
(ends with Renan's victory.)

1509
01:00:06,942 --> 01:00:08,512
- Good job. - Good job.

1510
01:00:08,842 --> 01:00:10,412
Good job.

1511
01:00:10,712 --> 01:00:11,712
Good job.

1512
01:00:12,412 --> 01:00:14,852
- You did so well. - You're the best.

1513
01:00:15,582 --> 01:00:17,121
Don't cry. You did so well.

1514
01:00:17,122 --> 01:00:19,121
- My gosh. - You were so cool.

1515
01:00:19,122 --> 01:00:22,692
I must've made too many risky moves.

1516
01:00:22,862 --> 01:00:24,191
No, you didn't.

1517
01:00:24,192 --> 01:00:25,962
It's just a matter of preference.

1518
01:00:26,092 --> 01:00:27,902
I wanted to make something that would bridge the gap.

1519
01:00:28,032 --> 01:00:29,232
- You did well. - That's not true.

1520
01:00:29,402 --> 01:00:31,771
You'd feel very upset.

1521
01:00:31,772 --> 01:00:33,731
No. We were cool.

1522
01:00:33,732 --> 01:00:35,342
I'm so sorry.

1523
01:00:35,572 --> 01:00:37,972
I said we wouldn't lose.

1524
01:00:39,542 --> 01:00:42,011
I thought we wouldn't lose.

1525
01:00:42,012 --> 01:00:43,951
(She's sorry she didn't win them the victory as promised.)

1526
01:00:43,952 --> 01:00:45,282
- I'm sorry. - No, we're okay.

1527
01:00:45,482 --> 01:00:48,882
It got me thinking that I was doing something wrong.

1528
01:00:49,422 --> 01:00:52,022
I felt bad for the dancers.

1529
01:00:56,322 --> 01:00:57,861
Simeez the best director.

1530
01:00:57,862 --> 01:00:59,131
Thank you so much.

1531
01:00:59,132 --> 01:01:00,762
Seriously, thank you so much.

1532
01:01:01,302 --> 01:01:03,731
They were comforting me.

1533
01:01:03,732 --> 01:01:05,101
It was so touching.

1534
01:01:05,102 --> 01:01:07,242
(It was so touching.)

1535
01:01:07,342 --> 01:01:08,471
(If I lose, I'll die.)

1536
01:01:08,472 --> 01:01:09,472
(The conflict with the dancers arise.)

1537
01:01:09,472 --> 01:01:10,472
(You're being annoying.)

1538
01:01:10,472 --> 01:01:11,472
(I've said this 10 times.)

1539
01:01:11,473 --> 01:01:13,311
(Everyone is running the same way except you.)

1540
01:01:13,312 --> 01:01:15,441
(We need to practice the group dance more.)

1541
01:01:15,442 --> 01:01:16,442
(We have a time limit.)

1542
01:01:16,443 --> 01:01:17,851
(Was my team very inefficient?)

1543
01:01:17,852 --> 01:01:18,981
(Why won't you say this...)

1544
01:01:18,982 --> 01:01:20,211
(when I ask if there's any problem?)

1545
01:01:20,212 --> 01:01:21,551
(I told you to check things like this.)

1546
01:01:21,552 --> 01:01:22,552
(Am I...)

1547
01:01:22,552 --> 01:01:23,552
(too overbearing?)

1548
01:01:24,692 --> 01:01:26,121
(I don't know if they have that big impact.)

1549
01:01:26,122 --> 01:01:27,221
(If I lose, with the kind of personality I have,)

1550
01:01:27,222 --> 01:01:28,822
(I can't leave.)

1551
01:01:28,992 --> 01:01:34,902
(Which 5 performances will they get to showcase to the audience?)

1552
01:01:35,162 --> 01:01:36,162
(1st day of practice)

1553
01:01:36,163 --> 01:01:37,302
You're doing well.

1554
01:01:37,602 --> 01:01:38,871
(Team BADA is practicing.)

1555
01:01:38,872 --> 01:01:40,501
(And so is Team INGYOO.)

1556
01:01:40,502 --> 01:01:43,002
(All the teams are busy practicing.)

1557
01:01:43,172 --> 01:01:45,772
One, two, three, four,

1558
01:01:46,212 --> 01:01:48,782
five, six, seven, eight.

1559
01:01:48,812 --> 01:01:49,842
Lift it up.

1560
01:01:50,482 --> 01:01:51,881
What is happening?

1561
01:01:51,882 --> 01:01:53,921
I'm screwed. Did I join the wrong team?

1562
01:01:53,922 --> 01:01:55,422
We don't have much time.

1563
01:01:55,982 --> 01:01:58,022
I got all the performances as I'd planned.

1564
01:01:58,192 --> 01:02:00,221
(This is his planned performance?)

1565
01:02:00,222 --> 01:02:01,791
Because in my performance,

1566
01:02:01,792 --> 01:02:03,622
I'm the main character.

1567
01:02:03,792 --> 01:02:06,262
(Back Koo Young's concept sheet is full of "I.")

1568
01:02:06,732 --> 01:02:09,302
I'm making full use of myself.

1569
01:02:09,962 --> 01:02:12,571
You need the main character to lead the story,

1570
01:02:12,572 --> 01:02:15,402
and I'm confident as a dancer too.

1571
01:02:16,102 --> 01:02:19,511
I need to do a perfect performance in just six days.

1572
01:02:19,512 --> 01:02:21,981
Can I make 40 Back Koo Youngs? No.

1573
01:02:21,982 --> 01:02:25,011
In a large-group performance, instead of their unique characters,

1574
01:02:25,012 --> 01:02:27,111
it's important to make the overall picture look nice...

1575
01:02:27,112 --> 01:02:29,182
by working together.

1576
01:02:29,452 --> 01:02:32,122
So rather than giving characters to the dancers,

1577
01:02:32,222 --> 01:02:35,061
I decided to use them as an element of the whole picture.

1578
01:02:35,062 --> 01:02:36,862
The keyword is...

1579
01:02:37,122 --> 01:02:38,531
"Back Koo Young's inside."

1580
01:02:38,532 --> 01:02:39,832
(Back Koo Young's inside?)

1581
01:02:39,962 --> 01:02:42,301
You are my cells.

1582
01:02:42,302 --> 01:02:43,362
(I am Back Koo Young's cell?)

1583
01:02:43,462 --> 01:02:45,431
- Some will swim, - Two, three, four.

1584
01:02:45,432 --> 01:02:47,541
some will lift others,

1585
01:02:47,542 --> 01:02:49,501
and some will do the scorpion pose.

1586
01:02:49,502 --> 01:02:51,511
I had it planned long ago.

1587
01:02:51,512 --> 01:02:55,411
That's why I let Kasper choose first.

1588
01:02:55,412 --> 01:02:57,751
About him taking those five dancers,

1589
01:02:57,752 --> 01:02:59,682
it didn't mean much to me.

1590
01:03:00,012 --> 01:03:02,752
As long as my dancers have a strong foundation,

1591
01:03:02,852 --> 01:03:04,022
I'll have no issue with directing them.

1592
01:03:04,092 --> 01:03:05,251
(During the casting session,)

1593
01:03:05,252 --> 01:03:06,922
(Back Koo Young tested them on the basic moves.)

1594
01:03:07,052 --> 01:03:08,461
- He's really doing that. - Five, six, seven, eight.

1595
01:03:08,462 --> 01:03:10,561
- One, two. - What you must practice the most...

1596
01:03:10,562 --> 01:03:11,632
is the basic, fundamental movements.

1597
01:03:11,662 --> 01:03:13,831
That leads to your skills.

1598
01:03:13,832 --> 01:03:14,832
(This is why...)

1599
01:03:14,833 --> 01:03:16,561
(he chose based on the basic moves only.)

1600
01:03:16,562 --> 01:03:18,732
But that aside,

1601
01:03:18,832 --> 01:03:20,942
more than anything, teamwork is most important.

1602
01:03:21,072 --> 01:03:22,971
- Let's do this. - Let's do this.

1603
01:03:22,972 --> 01:03:25,012
(He brings up the excitement with a cheer before the practice starts.)

1604
01:03:25,042 --> 01:03:27,111
Since a lot of them are inexperienced,

1605
01:03:27,112 --> 01:03:29,911
I wanted to give them confidence...

1606
01:03:29,912 --> 01:03:31,152
that they can do well.

1607
01:03:31,312 --> 01:03:33,251
(Confidence up!)

1608
01:03:33,252 --> 01:03:35,351
Everyone is working hard,

1609
01:03:35,352 --> 01:03:36,452
and I don't want them to get hurt.

1610
01:03:36,582 --> 01:03:39,522
I emphasized a lot on the dancers' conditions.

1611
01:03:39,592 --> 01:03:41,121
(Back Koo Young's dancers have gathered in one corner.)

1612
01:03:41,122 --> 01:03:42,821
(And a mysterious box)

1613
01:03:42,822 --> 01:03:44,631
(They're knee pads.)

1614
01:03:44,632 --> 01:03:46,031
(Back Koo Young's flex for the 40 hardworking dancers)

1615
01:03:46,032 --> 01:03:47,401
(You're awesome, Koo Young!)

1616
01:03:47,402 --> 01:03:49,101
A lot of performances require them...

1617
01:03:49,102 --> 01:03:50,671
to kneel.

1618
01:03:50,672 --> 01:03:53,101
It really hurts if you practice those moves...

1619
01:03:53,102 --> 01:03:55,902
without any protective gear.

1620
01:03:55,972 --> 01:03:57,171
Are you wearing the knee pads?

1621
01:03:57,172 --> 01:03:58,172
- Yes. - Yes.

1622
01:03:58,173 --> 01:03:59,972
- Are you wearing the knee pads? - Yes.

1623
01:04:00,112 --> 01:04:03,211
We need to be injury-free to practice together.

1624
01:04:03,212 --> 01:04:05,212
It helps with the quality of the work as well.

1625
01:04:05,382 --> 01:04:06,681
Enabling the dancers...

1626
01:04:06,682 --> 01:04:09,151
to dance as freely as they can...

1627
01:04:09,152 --> 01:04:11,152
is a director's job as well.

1628
01:04:11,292 --> 01:04:13,152
Now, I need to do well.

1629
01:04:13,422 --> 01:04:16,091
As a director, of course,

1630
01:04:16,092 --> 01:04:19,162
but I want to do my part as a dancer as well.

1631
01:04:19,292 --> 01:04:22,532
I run, dance, and run again.

1632
01:04:22,702 --> 01:04:25,071
It will be exhausting. It's very exhausting.

1633
01:04:25,072 --> 01:04:27,172
But I should do it since it's my choreography.

1634
01:04:27,342 --> 01:04:29,401
I dance as the main character,

1635
01:04:29,402 --> 01:04:31,571
and the dancers come together to form a scenery.

1636
01:04:31,572 --> 01:04:33,771
That way, I'm sure I can make a good performance...

1637
01:04:33,772 --> 01:04:36,212
without many outstanding dancers.

1638
01:04:36,512 --> 01:04:37,781
I don't agree.

1639
01:04:37,782 --> 01:04:40,252
I hate using them as random Dancer 1, Dancer 2.

1640
01:04:40,352 --> 01:04:42,581
They shouldn't just act as backup dancers.

1641
01:04:42,582 --> 01:04:44,051
They should become a scene...

1642
01:04:44,052 --> 01:04:47,051
and make a story. I think they have important roles.

1643
01:04:47,052 --> 01:04:48,361
So I gave them characters.

1644
01:04:48,362 --> 01:04:49,961
(Kasper, the true self who tries to maintain the inner peace)

1645
01:04:49,962 --> 01:04:52,032
In the concept I came up with,

1646
01:04:52,332 --> 01:04:55,862
I'll depict the "me" that I want to show others.

1647
01:04:56,162 --> 01:04:58,402
Shuri is my evil self.

1648
01:04:58,702 --> 01:05:01,602
The dancers are evil energy.

1649
01:05:01,702 --> 01:05:03,271
(Evil energy?)

1650
01:05:03,272 --> 01:05:06,972
And the bosses of the evil energy, the four kings.

1651
01:05:07,172 --> 01:05:08,781
(We're the four kings?)

1652
01:05:08,782 --> 01:05:10,081
By giving them character,

1653
01:05:10,082 --> 01:05:11,751
it helps them to get immersed more.

1654
01:05:11,752 --> 01:05:14,352
It gives them responsibilities too.

1655
01:05:14,822 --> 01:05:17,321
We must win no matter what.

1656
01:05:17,322 --> 01:05:18,551
If we lose,

1657
01:05:18,552 --> 01:05:19,852
this performance will be gone.

1658
01:05:20,022 --> 01:05:21,691
Since we came here, we must perform on stage.

1659
01:05:21,692 --> 01:05:22,692
Exactly.

1660
01:05:22,693 --> 01:05:23,761
Shuri.

1661
01:05:23,762 --> 01:05:25,462
Three from Penrose.

1662
01:05:25,592 --> 01:05:26,592
Nino.

1663
01:05:26,593 --> 01:05:28,101
Their dancing and vibe...

1664
01:05:28,102 --> 01:05:30,301
It's of the highest caliber.

1665
01:05:30,302 --> 01:05:32,131
The first important part...

1666
01:05:32,132 --> 01:05:33,871
will be performed by dancers from Penrose.

1667
01:05:33,872 --> 01:05:36,472
Shuri and Nino will dance powerfully...

1668
01:05:36,602 --> 01:05:38,541
and give off the strong energy.

1669
01:05:38,542 --> 01:05:41,241
For the highlight, where it needs to explode,

1670
01:05:41,242 --> 01:05:43,842
Shuri and I will give off the energy.

1671
01:05:44,212 --> 01:05:45,251
How is it?

1672
01:05:45,252 --> 01:05:46,252
(Thumbs up!)

1673
01:05:46,253 --> 01:05:47,881
(Feeling proud)

1674
01:05:47,882 --> 01:05:49,521
"It's impossible for me to lose." Or so I thought.

1675
01:05:49,522 --> 01:05:51,392
But things don't always go according to plan.

1676
01:05:51,592 --> 01:05:53,692
Number 1, Number 2.

1677
01:05:54,052 --> 01:05:55,122
Again.

1678
01:05:55,222 --> 01:05:57,861
Number 1, Number 2.

1679
01:05:57,862 --> 01:06:00,761
Again. You're slow.

1680
01:06:00,762 --> 01:06:02,132
(Me?)

1681
01:06:02,462 --> 01:06:04,472
It wasn't a difficult part,

1682
01:06:04,632 --> 01:06:06,272
but she couldn't do it.

1683
01:06:06,532 --> 01:06:07,972
To be honest, I was frustrated.

1684
01:06:08,142 --> 01:06:09,172
Again.

1685
01:06:09,842 --> 01:06:11,611
(Dancer Noura keeps making the same mistake.)

1686
01:06:11,612 --> 01:06:12,612
Hold on.

1687
01:06:13,142 --> 01:06:14,911
Let's focus, shall we?

1688
01:06:14,912 --> 01:06:16,512
(Noura holds the group back by making the same mistake.)

1689
01:06:16,882 --> 01:06:17,911
(Glancing)

1690
01:06:17,912 --> 01:06:18,912
(Frustrated)

1691
01:06:18,913 --> 01:06:21,681
Some may do their best in every given moment,

1692
01:06:21,682 --> 01:06:23,382
but some may not.

1693
01:06:23,552 --> 01:06:24,791
There's a villain in the team.

1694
01:06:24,792 --> 01:06:29,262
Everyone is talking about the same person.

1695
01:06:29,422 --> 01:06:31,292
We need to do something about Noura.

1696
01:06:32,132 --> 01:06:33,962
We got off on the wrong foot.

1697
01:06:34,062 --> 01:06:35,502
- Alexandra. - Here.

1698
01:06:35,862 --> 01:06:38,102
(They started the first day practice in an upbeat mood.)

1699
01:06:39,302 --> 01:06:41,272
Noura?

1700
01:06:41,572 --> 01:06:42,741
(Looking around)

1701
01:06:42,742 --> 01:06:43,742
Noura?

1702
01:06:44,372 --> 01:06:45,541
Noura isn't here.

1703
01:06:45,542 --> 01:06:47,371
She was late to the first practice.

1704
01:06:47,372 --> 01:06:50,411
I already know she's not the best dancer.

1705
01:06:50,412 --> 01:06:51,412
The formation too...

1706
01:06:51,413 --> 01:06:52,552
(During "Love Shot" formation practice)

1707
01:06:54,322 --> 01:06:56,722
- And go this way. - Why?

1708
01:06:57,892 --> 01:06:59,021
Move to the right.

1709
01:06:59,022 --> 01:07:00,452
(She runs in between them!)

1710
01:07:00,622 --> 01:07:03,262
Noura. Don't stay there. Move immediately.

1711
01:07:03,562 --> 01:07:06,031
Penrose members need to walk to the front,

1712
01:07:06,032 --> 01:07:07,501
and she's still running across.

1713
01:07:07,502 --> 01:07:08,961
If she can't do it,

1714
01:07:08,962 --> 01:07:10,971
she should come in early to practice or something.

1715
01:07:10,972 --> 01:07:14,471
But she keeps checking herself in the mirror and brushing her hair.

1716
01:07:14,472 --> 01:07:16,601
It's the problem of attitude and will.

1717
01:07:16,602 --> 01:07:18,342
That got me angrier.

1718
01:07:18,742 --> 01:07:21,541
Whether your role is big or small, in front or behind,

1719
01:07:21,542 --> 01:07:23,541
you need to do your part...

1720
01:07:23,542 --> 01:07:25,182
for this to become perfect.

1721
01:07:25,552 --> 01:07:27,481
Think of this as your own stage.

1722
01:07:27,482 --> 01:07:29,982
We're all working together to make this performance.

1723
01:07:30,552 --> 01:07:32,251
I hope you'll focus.

1724
01:07:32,252 --> 01:07:33,252
- Okay. - Okay.

1725
01:07:33,622 --> 01:07:34,791
Let's dance to the song.

1726
01:07:34,792 --> 01:07:35,822
- Okay. - Okay.

1727
01:07:36,062 --> 01:07:37,532
(Keeping an eye on her)

1728
01:07:38,592 --> 01:07:40,362
(Noura makes the same mistake again.)

1729
01:07:43,202 --> 01:07:45,272
(What is it?)

1730
01:07:45,372 --> 01:07:46,632
When is your timing?

1731
01:07:48,472 --> 01:07:51,511
(Noura can't answer.)

1732
01:07:51,512 --> 01:07:52,971
I was at a loss for words.

1733
01:07:52,972 --> 01:07:56,041
If your mistake is holding everyone back,

1734
01:07:56,042 --> 01:07:57,342
you should work harder.

1735
01:07:58,452 --> 01:07:59,881
I have no intention to lose,

1736
01:07:59,882 --> 01:08:02,282
but at this rate, I might actually lose.

1737
01:08:04,892 --> 01:08:06,592
Koo Young and Kasper.

1738
01:08:06,922 --> 01:08:08,091
I can't wait to watch them.

1739
01:08:08,092 --> 01:08:10,262
Okay. Let's go, Koo Young.

1740
01:08:10,392 --> 01:08:11,632
I wonder what he did.

1741
01:08:12,332 --> 01:08:13,962
Let's see how impressive it is.

1742
01:08:14,302 --> 01:08:15,302
(Back Koo Young's choreography practice)

1743
01:08:15,303 --> 01:08:16,362
My gosh.

1744
01:08:18,572 --> 01:08:21,872
(Everyone is surprised at the extraordinary intro.)

1745
01:08:22,302 --> 01:08:23,672
I like this choreography.

1746
01:08:24,042 --> 01:08:27,012
How did he train the dancers with this technique?

1747
01:08:27,172 --> 01:08:28,342
Goodness.

1748
01:08:29,512 --> 01:08:31,311
His moves are similar to mine.

1749
01:08:31,312 --> 01:08:33,211
He really made full use of himself.

1750
01:08:33,212 --> 01:08:35,621
Koo Young is so passionate.

1751
01:08:35,622 --> 01:08:37,722
He meant it when he wrote "making full use of Back Koo Young."

1752
01:08:39,022 --> 01:08:42,022
All I can remember is him running.

1753
01:08:42,392 --> 01:08:44,161
He keeps running.

1754
01:08:44,162 --> 01:08:45,792
(He keeps running.)

1755
01:08:46,092 --> 01:08:47,832
Make full use of Back Koo Young.

1756
01:08:48,762 --> 01:08:49,931
The chorus is in perfect sync.

1757
01:08:49,932 --> 01:08:53,632
The perfect sync gives stability.

1758
01:08:54,842 --> 01:08:57,202
(How did Kasper react to Back Koo Young's performance?)

1759
01:08:57,912 --> 01:08:59,911
(Having mixed feelings)

1760
01:08:59,912 --> 01:09:00,912
Okay.

1761
01:09:00,913 --> 01:09:02,712
I felt very worried.

1762
01:09:02,942 --> 01:09:04,282
Koo Young is watching mine.

1763
01:09:04,982 --> 01:09:06,412
I'm looking forward to it.

1764
01:09:06,512 --> 01:09:08,222
I'm so curious.

1765
01:09:08,682 --> 01:09:10,151
I'll watch reverently.

1766
01:09:10,152 --> 01:09:11,292
(Changing her seating position)

1767
01:09:12,192 --> 01:09:14,052
My gosh.

1768
01:09:14,362 --> 01:09:15,422
Nice.

1769
01:09:16,892 --> 01:09:18,131
I like that mirroring.

1770
01:09:18,132 --> 01:09:19,832
(Back Koo Young watches Kasper's video closely.)

1771
01:09:20,092 --> 01:09:21,902
(He's smiling?)

1772
01:09:23,332 --> 01:09:25,471
(The dancers are not in sync.)

1773
01:09:25,472 --> 01:09:27,072
(Oh, dear.)

1774
01:09:28,272 --> 01:09:29,642
I don't know.

1775
01:09:29,842 --> 01:09:30,972
It's so disappointing.

1776
01:09:31,172 --> 01:09:33,041
I get what they're doing,

1777
01:09:33,042 --> 01:09:35,711
and he has a lot of choreography and formations,

1778
01:09:35,712 --> 01:09:39,312
but the dancers are not ready.

1779
01:09:39,452 --> 01:09:41,451
They only have one day left, but this...

1780
01:09:41,452 --> 01:09:45,192
I don't think they can pull it off on the stage.

1781
01:09:45,722 --> 01:09:48,191
I can't face Kasper if I beat him in this too.

1782
01:09:48,192 --> 01:09:49,962
(Gosh, Kasper...)

1783
01:09:50,462 --> 01:09:51,891
(Back Koo Young is voted as the expected director.)

1784
01:09:51,892 --> 01:09:53,092
(Did you see that, Kasper?)

1785
01:09:55,732 --> 01:09:59,032
(I won again!)

1786
01:10:00,872 --> 01:10:02,642
The expected director is Koo Young?

1787
01:10:03,142 --> 01:10:05,211
(He became even more concerned with the result.)

1788
01:10:05,212 --> 01:10:06,572
What should I do?

1789
01:10:07,512 --> 01:10:08,941
(The votes were 7 to 1 for Back Koo Young.)

1790
01:10:08,942 --> 01:10:10,811
The dancers aren't ready.

1791
01:10:10,812 --> 01:10:13,311
Kasper's performance has a risk.

1792
01:10:13,312 --> 01:10:15,782
It is affected way too much by the dancers' skills.

1793
01:10:16,052 --> 01:10:18,492
I'm so grateful for my dancers once again.

1794
01:10:19,952 --> 01:10:21,892
(He stares at the expected Credit Board for a long time.)

1795
01:10:22,092 --> 01:10:23,291
How should I overcome...

1796
01:10:23,292 --> 01:10:24,361
this hurdle?

1797
01:10:24,362 --> 01:10:25,932
I'm at a loss.

1798
01:10:25,962 --> 01:10:27,462
(Kasper becomes more worried. How will the match go?)

1799
01:10:27,962 --> 01:10:29,261
Hello!

1800
01:10:29,262 --> 01:10:31,101
Come in, everyone.

1801
01:10:31,102 --> 01:10:32,731
They're starting smoothly and immediately.

1802
01:10:32,732 --> 01:10:34,871
It's funny how I'm judging them.

1803
01:10:34,872 --> 01:10:36,242
(Their direct senior is watching them.)

1804
01:10:36,302 --> 01:10:37,772
You of all people are here.

1805
01:10:38,372 --> 01:10:41,541
How long have you worked with Koo Young and Kasper?

1806
01:10:41,542 --> 01:10:43,212
More than 20 years.

1807
01:10:43,412 --> 01:10:45,212
I've seen them since they were a novice.

1808
01:10:45,352 --> 01:10:46,412
(Laughing)

1809
01:10:46,582 --> 01:10:47,722
They'll do well.

1810
01:10:47,922 --> 01:10:50,621
Does the countdown start now?

1811
01:10:50,622 --> 01:10:52,691
The 1-hour-20-minute countdown starts now.

1812
01:10:52,692 --> 01:10:55,991
Okay. Dancers, have your free time.

1813
01:10:55,992 --> 01:10:57,292
(Free time?)

1814
01:10:57,422 --> 01:10:58,431
See you later.

1815
01:10:58,432 --> 01:10:59,432
(Back Koo Young goes somewhere, leaving the dancers behind.)

1816
01:10:59,433 --> 01:11:02,562
As soon as I went in, I said bye to the dancers.

1817
01:11:02,702 --> 01:11:06,271
I told them to do as they liked for 5 to 10 minutes.

1818
01:11:06,272 --> 01:11:08,501
Check the backstage...

1819
01:11:08,502 --> 01:11:11,742
and go up the second floor for those who'll be going there.

1820
01:11:11,842 --> 01:11:14,711
A lot of my dancers have little experience being on stage.

1821
01:11:14,712 --> 01:11:17,711
So I taught them how to check the blocking...

1822
01:11:17,712 --> 01:11:18,982
on stage.

1823
01:11:19,182 --> 01:11:21,851
I made the rule for moving in the backstage.

1824
01:11:21,852 --> 01:11:24,081
If you're going to the front, walk inside.

1825
01:11:24,082 --> 01:11:25,721
If you're going to the back, walk outside.

1826
01:11:25,722 --> 01:11:28,321
So your paths don't cross.

1827
01:11:28,322 --> 01:11:31,361
The light fixtures, the staff members' chairs,

1828
01:11:31,362 --> 01:11:33,161
the cameras they're not using.

1829
01:11:33,162 --> 01:11:34,531
You could find these stuff there.

1830
01:11:34,532 --> 01:11:37,871
You need to check those out and block based on that.

1831
01:11:37,872 --> 01:11:39,601
You must remember this...

1832
01:11:39,602 --> 01:11:42,041
to use the 80 minutes effectively tomorrow.

1833
01:11:42,042 --> 01:11:43,172
- Okay. - Okay.

1834
01:11:43,442 --> 01:11:45,541
Where's the stage manager?

1835
01:11:45,542 --> 01:11:47,141
I want to check the lighting.

1836
01:11:47,142 --> 01:11:49,981
I'm going to find the stage manager as soon as I go in...

1837
01:11:49,982 --> 01:11:50,982
to check the lighting.

1838
01:11:50,983 --> 01:11:54,151
Can I check the lighting for each scene?

1839
01:11:54,152 --> 01:11:56,681
- That's good. - He gives off the veteran vibe.

1840
01:11:56,682 --> 01:12:00,291
I'll discuss the lighting cues with the stage manager,

1841
01:12:00,292 --> 01:12:03,291
and once it's done, we'll check it over...

1842
01:12:03,292 --> 01:12:04,562
with the music.

1843
01:12:04,892 --> 01:12:07,132
Ten minutes have passed.

1844
01:12:07,232 --> 01:12:09,901
I'll join as a dancer to rehearse.

1845
01:12:09,902 --> 01:12:10,902
He's joining them.

1846
01:12:10,903 --> 01:12:12,301
- He should check first. - Exactly.

1847
01:12:12,302 --> 01:12:13,401
He should check overall.

1848
01:12:13,402 --> 01:12:16,401
(The first rehearsal starts with Back Koo Young's technique.)

1849
01:12:16,402 --> 01:12:17,672
(The dancers need to enter from the backstage.)

1850
01:12:17,972 --> 01:12:19,271
Gosh, stay focused.

1851
01:12:19,272 --> 01:12:20,411
- Oh, dear. - My gosh.

1852
01:12:20,412 --> 01:12:21,612
What to do with them?

1853
01:12:22,042 --> 01:12:23,042
Goodness.

1854
01:12:23,242 --> 01:12:24,951
You can't see that when you're on stage yourself.

1855
