01:23:08,922 --> 01:23:10,421
I was in the lighting room...

2120
01:23:10,422 --> 01:23:11,961
when he performed "Long Way Home."

2121
01:23:11,962 --> 01:23:14,392
I want to battle it out with those details.

2122
01:23:14,562 --> 01:23:16,131
I'm certain that performances using lights...

2123
01:23:16,132 --> 01:23:18,501
will shine brighter on the stage.

2124
01:23:18,502 --> 01:23:21,232
Can we see what the complete blackout is like?

2125
01:23:21,372 --> 01:23:22,872
Let's check the complete blackout.

2126
01:23:23,402 --> 01:23:25,272
Can the dancers turn on the lights?

2127
01:23:26,442 --> 01:23:28,642
Okay. Let's check the first formation.

2128
01:23:28,982 --> 01:23:30,011
I have a bad feeling about this.

2129
01:23:30,012 --> 01:23:32,051
When using objects like those, it must be completely dark.

2130
01:23:32,052 --> 01:23:33,252
Then, they won't be able to see.

2131
01:23:33,712 --> 01:23:36,522
That can become a risk.

2132
01:23:37,622 --> 01:23:39,221
(They try the flashlight part during the blackout.)

2133
01:23:39,222 --> 01:23:41,292
- Can you see? - I can't see at all.

2134
01:23:42,762 --> 01:23:45,132
- The center is right here. - No. This won't work.

2135
01:23:45,732 --> 01:23:46,732
This won't work.

2136
01:23:46,733 --> 01:23:48,731
They had to be in formation during the blackout,

2137
01:23:48,732 --> 01:23:50,301
but they couldn't, as they weren't able to see.

2138
01:23:50,302 --> 01:23:51,401
We'll stop here.

2139
01:23:51,402 --> 01:23:53,032
It's hard to see where we are.

2140
01:23:53,332 --> 01:23:56,402
Dancers, can you see the marks?

2141
01:23:56,742 --> 01:23:59,041
- It's hard to see. - It's hard to see?

2142
01:23:59,042 --> 01:24:00,841
How do the silhouette lights sound?

2143
01:24:00,842 --> 01:24:02,441
The formation had to be neat.

2144
01:24:02,442 --> 01:24:05,251
The prism colors are seen with the silhouette lights,

2145
01:24:05,252 --> 01:24:06,482
creating a unique vibe.

2146
01:24:06,852 --> 01:24:08,281
The silhouette lights were only used...

2147
01:24:08,282 --> 01:24:10,822
right before the flashlight part.

2148
01:24:11,222 --> 01:24:12,792
I think this will work.

2149
01:24:13,852 --> 01:24:15,122
Was the glitch effect used on purpose?

2150
01:24:15,392 --> 01:24:16,621
He did a really good job.

2151
01:24:16,622 --> 01:24:18,732
He's very quick to adapt.

2152
01:24:18,762 --> 01:24:20,431
He provides a solution right away.

2153
01:24:20,432 --> 01:24:21,762
- Those lights look nice. - Right.

2154
01:24:22,062 --> 01:24:24,802
Kasper moves differently with the lights.

2155
01:24:25,132 --> 01:24:26,971
The lights determine...

2156
01:24:26,972 --> 01:24:28,542
the angles of the performance.

2157
01:24:28,772 --> 01:24:30,741
As Kasper has experience with concerts,

2158
01:24:30,742 --> 01:24:32,642
he knows how important the lights are.

2159
01:24:33,172 --> 01:24:34,412
How many minutes do we have left, Shuri?

2160
01:24:34,512 --> 01:24:35,712
- We have 59 minutes left. - We have 59 minutes left.

2161
01:24:36,182 --> 01:24:37,611
Shall we try that part?

2162
01:24:37,612 --> 01:24:38,612
- Yes. - Yes.

2163
01:24:39,352 --> 01:24:40,581
(During the transition section...)

2164
01:24:40,582 --> 01:24:41,811
(when the Penrose members move forward,)

2165
01:24:41,812 --> 01:24:43,552
(one dancer is late to move out.)

2166
01:24:44,522 --> 01:24:46,622
Noura made a mistake again.

2167
01:24:47,592 --> 01:24:49,621
The Penrose members had to move forward,

2168
01:24:49,622 --> 01:24:51,792
but she kept getting in the way on her own.

2169
01:24:52,162 --> 01:24:54,292
That kept causing a problem with the movement.

2170
01:24:55,462 --> 01:24:57,502
(During every "Love Shot" practice session,)

2171
01:24:57,632 --> 01:24:59,071
(Noura kept forgetting her line and position.)

2172
01:24:59,072 --> 01:25:00,331
(Move right here.)

2173
01:25:00,332 --> 01:25:01,332
Noura.

2174
01:25:01,333 --> 01:25:02,401
(Move to the right!)

2175
01:25:02,402 --> 01:25:03,902
(Running right through the middle)

2176
01:25:04,142 --> 01:25:05,142
(Noura!)

2177
01:25:05,143 --> 01:25:06,872
(Don't stay there. Move immediately.)

2178
01:25:06,972 --> 01:25:09,912
We already knew she lacked skill.

2179
01:25:10,042 --> 01:25:11,782
(Again. You're slow.)

2180
01:25:12,482 --> 01:25:16,382
(Noura keeps making mistakes with the moves and timing.)

2181
01:25:17,182 --> 01:25:19,692
Noura! Why are you moving out late?

2182
01:25:20,752 --> 01:25:21,992
You have to be faster to move away.

2183
01:25:22,292 --> 01:25:24,462
You have to think it'll be death if you don't move away.

2184
01:25:24,592 --> 01:25:26,862
It ruins the formation for the next part.

2185
01:25:28,292 --> 01:25:29,501
(They keep trying that part.)

2186
01:25:29,502 --> 01:25:30,901
Boom, two, three, four,

2187
01:25:30,902 --> 01:25:33,102
- Are you listening to the song? - five, six, seven, eight.

2188
01:25:33,932 --> 01:25:35,131
(Sighing)

2189
01:25:35,132 --> 01:25:37,542
Hold on. I'll take that part.

2190
01:25:37,702 --> 01:25:40,712
(Kasper ends up going down to take Noura's part.)

2191
01:25:40,742 --> 01:25:42,111
(Feeling nervous)

2192
01:25:42,112 --> 01:25:44,042
I want to know why Kasper is going down.

2193
01:25:44,142 --> 01:25:46,351
- He called out someone's name. - I see.

2194
01:25:46,352 --> 01:25:47,912
She'll be trembling right now.

2195
01:25:48,452 --> 01:25:50,821
Make the formation for the outro of "Love Shot."

2196
01:25:50,822 --> 01:25:52,192
(Moving in perfect order)

2197
01:25:52,292 --> 01:25:53,752
Did you two keep getting into each other?

2198
01:25:54,522 --> 01:25:56,821
We got into each other when I moved this way.

2199
01:25:56,822 --> 01:25:58,632
But she moved behind me just now.

2200
01:25:59,032 --> 01:26:00,062
Move out.

2201
01:26:01,262 --> 01:26:02,362
Play the song...

2202
01:26:02,962 --> 01:26:05,332
at around 1 minute and 15 seconds.

2203
01:26:06,032 --> 01:26:08,132
This is a mindset problem in the end.

2204
01:26:08,232 --> 01:26:09,771
"It won't work."

2205
01:26:09,772 --> 01:26:12,072
But you haven't tried everything you could.

2206
01:26:13,012 --> 01:26:15,512
(He tries that part instead of Noura.)

2207
01:26:16,182 --> 01:26:18,611
(Kasper moves away without any problems.)

2208
01:26:18,612 --> 01:26:21,211
It works. I saw it with my own eyes.

2209
01:26:21,212 --> 01:26:22,852
But she kept saying it wouldn't work.

2210
01:26:23,952 --> 01:26:25,622
I got away right away, didn't I?

2211
01:26:26,492 --> 01:26:30,292
If I move to that side at the last part...

2212
01:26:31,222 --> 01:26:33,962
It should be like this, but...

2213
01:26:34,092 --> 01:26:35,262
It's like that for everyone.

2214
01:26:36,202 --> 01:26:37,832
It's not just you. It's like that for everyone.

2215
01:26:38,632 --> 01:26:39,702
Right.

2216
01:26:40,202 --> 01:26:42,172
Just run out.

2217
01:26:42,672 --> 01:26:45,471
- Nothing is impossible, everyone. - Right.

2218
01:26:45,472 --> 01:26:47,512
You must not wander around.

2219
01:26:47,772 --> 01:26:51,041
Kasper is precise with his standards.

2220
01:26:51,042 --> 01:26:54,612
If a part doesn't match what he imagined,

2221
01:26:54,682 --> 01:26:56,951
he's the type to be harsh on his juniors.

2222
01:26:56,952 --> 01:26:59,221
He's someone...

2223
01:26:59,222 --> 01:27:01,951
who wants to express exactly what he imagined.

2224
01:27:01,952 --> 01:27:03,892
I believe that's positive to a certain extent.

2225
01:27:04,622 --> 01:27:07,932
I worked on the details of the lights and movement.

2226
01:27:08,132 --> 01:27:09,332
I felt anxious.

2227
01:27:10,032 --> 01:27:11,961
Get ready for the rehearsal.

2228
01:27:11,962 --> 01:27:13,272
- Okay. - Rehearsal.

2229
01:27:13,432 --> 01:27:15,542
Let's get into the intro formation quickly.

2230
01:27:16,042 --> 01:27:18,001
Make sure to hide your flashlights.

2231
01:27:18,002 --> 01:27:19,041
- Okay. - Okay.

2232
01:27:19,042 --> 01:27:20,172
You must not get it wrong.

2233
01:27:21,072 --> 01:27:24,182
(The dress rehearsal of Team Kasper begins.)

2234
01:27:24,882 --> 01:27:26,181
(However,)

2235
01:27:26,182 --> 01:27:28,582
(some of the flashlights can be seen.)

2236
01:27:28,852 --> 01:27:31,221
The lights looked so messy.

2237
01:27:31,222 --> 01:27:32,521
That looks quite messy.

2238
01:27:32,522 --> 01:27:33,591
(Shaking her head)

2239
01:27:33,592 --> 01:27:34,592
(Noura)

2240
01:27:34,592 --> 01:27:35,592
(During the problematic part,)

2241
01:27:35,592 --> 01:27:36,592
(Noura moves out late again.)

2242
01:27:36,593 --> 01:27:37,622
Gosh!

2243
01:27:38,192 --> 01:27:39,492
Noura! Why...

2244
01:27:40,662 --> 01:27:41,662
We won.

2245
01:27:41,663 --> 01:27:43,831
I thought that the quality of our performance...

2246
01:27:43,832 --> 01:27:46,201
was much better.

2247
01:27:46,202 --> 01:27:47,372
What was the problem?

2248
01:27:47,532 --> 01:27:49,841
Noura. You got in the way when you moved out.

2249
01:27:49,842 --> 01:27:51,472
I forgot again.

2250
01:27:51,602 --> 01:27:53,842
You have to move away as the others are coming in.

2251
01:27:56,042 --> 01:27:58,542
(The waiting room is silent after the dress rehearsal.)

2252
01:27:59,052 --> 01:28:00,982
Did you work on moving away, Noura?

2253
01:28:01,512 --> 01:28:03,182
I forgot. I'm sorry.

2254
01:28:04,952 --> 01:28:06,252
Are you going to constantly say...

2255
01:28:06,852 --> 01:28:08,922
you're sorry after messing up in the actual performance?

2256
01:28:10,092 --> 01:28:12,632
- I'll work harder. - That's not what's important.

2257
01:28:13,132 --> 01:28:14,892
Who won't work hard here?

2258
01:28:15,902 --> 01:28:18,032
It's important not to make a mistake today.

2259
01:28:18,702 --> 01:28:20,872
Where should you position yourself to move out perfectly?

2260
01:28:21,972 --> 01:28:24,002
I'll recover from my stress.

2261
01:28:24,342 --> 01:28:26,011
- What? - I'll recover...

2262
01:28:26,012 --> 01:28:28,842
- from my stress. - Right.

2263
01:28:29,282 --> 01:28:30,511
Rather than that...

2264
01:28:30,512 --> 01:28:31,912
- I'll do a better job. - Hey, keep quiet.

2265
01:28:32,912 --> 01:28:33,912
What was that?

2266
01:28:34,782 --> 01:28:36,322
I'll do a better job.

2267
01:28:37,482 --> 01:28:40,122
(Noura is about to shed tears.)

2268
01:28:41,892 --> 01:28:43,222
Don't cry.

2269
01:28:44,092 --> 01:28:45,892
Crying won't change anything.

2270
01:28:48,692 --> 01:28:51,261
(She ends up shedding tears.)

2271
01:28:51,262 --> 01:28:52,271
That's not it.

2272
01:28:52,272 --> 01:28:53,802
(Reading the room)

2273
01:28:59,812 --> 01:29:02,281
She made the same mistake even during the last rehearsal.

2274
01:29:02,282 --> 01:29:05,382
I was standing on the edge of a cliff.

2275
01:29:05,552 --> 01:29:07,552
A simple push would make me fall over.

2276
01:29:08,082 --> 01:29:10,551
It won't matter if I lose against something amazing.

2277
01:29:10,552 --> 01:29:12,122
But that isn't the case.

2278
01:29:12,392 --> 01:29:13,491
Right now,

2279
01:29:13,492 --> 01:29:16,192
I'm starting to think that we're going to lose.

2280
01:29:16,592 --> 01:29:18,291
The one who fails will continue to fail.

2281
01:29:18,292 --> 01:29:21,162
This is a matter of failing to concentrate.

2282
01:29:21,662 --> 01:29:24,261
"Oh, I made a mistake." This means nothing.

2283
01:29:24,262 --> 01:29:27,532
Between a dancer and director,

2284
01:29:27,572 --> 01:29:30,171
the dancer who gets the job done...

2285
01:29:30,172 --> 01:29:33,011
will be given another chance to work with me.

2286
01:29:33,012 --> 01:29:35,311
It's all up to you, not me.

2287
01:29:35,312 --> 01:29:37,712
"I will work hard." This won't mean anything to me.

2288
01:29:38,012 --> 01:29:41,212
Getting your job done is all you can do.

2289
01:29:43,052 --> 01:29:44,151
I can't lose.

2290
01:29:44,152 --> 01:29:46,621
I'm already at the edge of a cliff. One more wrong step...

2291
01:29:46,622 --> 01:29:47,822
will get me killed.

2292
01:29:47,952 --> 01:29:49,061
I'm confident.

2293
01:29:49,062 --> 01:29:50,262
I must win.

2294
01:29:50,522 --> 01:29:52,491
But I think this team can win.

2295
01:29:52,492 --> 01:29:54,832
The lights can change the game.

2296
01:29:55,092 --> 01:29:58,561
The dancers came out sweating buckets.

2297
01:29:58,562 --> 01:30:00,031
It's the fog!

2298
01:30:00,032 --> 01:30:01,332
It'll look great, right?

2299
01:30:01,402 --> 01:30:02,402
Gosh!

2300
01:30:02,742 --> 01:30:03,972
Let's hurry.

2301
01:30:04,172 --> 01:30:05,471
And now,

2302
01:30:05,472 --> 01:30:07,741
it's time for Kasper's Last Run.

2303
01:30:07,742 --> 01:30:08,942
Are you ready?

2304
01:30:09,142 --> 01:30:10,742
(He's ready.)

2305
01:30:11,342 --> 01:30:13,282
Ready, fight!

2306
01:30:15,282 --> 01:30:16,321
(Synopsis: Expression of mutual destruction...)

2307
01:30:16,322 --> 01:30:17,351
(of human duality and inevitable contradiction)

2308
01:30:17,352 --> 01:30:18,421
(Main characters: Kasper, ego that tries to maintain inner peace,)

2309
01:30:18,422 --> 01:30:19,452
(Shuri, the conflicting ego that destroys oneself)

2310
01:30:19,492 --> 01:30:20,592
(Performance by Team Kasper)

2311
01:30:24,622 --> 01:30:25,691
Gosh, check out the presentation.

2312
01:30:25,692 --> 01:30:27,032
He disappeared.

2313
01:30:27,132 --> 01:30:28,732
(Focused)

2314
01:30:28,832 --> 01:30:31,062
That's so impressive! Oh, my gosh!

2315
01:30:38,442 --> 01:30:39,772
The fog was well used.

2316
01:30:41,172 --> 01:30:42,781
He's filming a music video.

2317
01:30:42,782 --> 01:30:44,512
He went epic.

2318
01:30:46,852 --> 01:30:49,951
This one feels like a show with the movement of the lights.

2319
01:30:49,952 --> 01:30:51,221
It's like watching a concert.

2320
01:30:51,222 --> 01:30:53,392
Kasper is taking TAEMIN's role.

2321
01:30:56,762 --> 01:30:58,862
(Cheering)

2322
01:30:59,032 --> 01:31:00,631
- He made it eye-catching. - Right.

2323
01:31:00,632 --> 01:31:02,602
I believe our performance was more impressive.

2324
01:31:04,262 --> 01:31:07,101
(Back Koo Young's signature choreography part in "Guilty")

2325
01:31:07,102 --> 01:31:08,531
He has been possessed by TAEMIN.

2326
01:31:08,532 --> 01:31:10,101
It feels completely different.

2327
01:31:10,102 --> 01:31:12,742
This one makes you focus even more.

2328
01:31:19,152 --> 01:31:20,182
I like it.

2329
01:31:22,422 --> 01:31:23,582
I like this formation.

2330
01:31:23,722 --> 01:31:24,952
(Satisfied)

2331
01:31:26,392 --> 01:31:28,251
They're against each other.

2332
01:31:28,252 --> 01:31:30,462
It's the mirror image!

2333
01:31:30,792 --> 01:31:33,731
This seems like the signature part. It was planned out well.

2334
01:31:33,732 --> 01:31:36,462
There was a diagonal transition and it turned out well.

2335
01:31:37,902 --> 01:31:39,231
Shuri, the super dancer.

2336
01:31:39,232 --> 01:31:41,532
Someone has come inside Shuri.

2337
01:31:45,542 --> 01:31:47,112
Gosh, there you go, Shuri!

2338
01:31:50,612 --> 01:31:52,881
- Hey! - They worked hard with the lights.

2339
01:31:52,882 --> 01:31:54,312
He's using the lights really well.

2340
01:31:56,852 --> 01:31:58,582
I thought my team could be in danger.

2341
01:31:58,822 --> 01:31:59,852
(Screaming)

2342
01:32:00,052 --> 01:32:02,522
He's not an easy opponent. He won't go down.

2343
01:32:12,002 --> 01:32:13,802
He's flying around.

2344
01:32:19,672 --> 01:32:21,312
(Amazed by the lights)

2345
01:32:21,812 --> 01:32:23,042
The lights are insane.

2346
01:32:26,612 --> 01:32:31,622
(Back Koo Young's signature choreography part in "Love Shot")

2347
01:32:32,252 --> 01:32:35,592
He made it feel more like a fantasy.

2348
01:32:36,492 --> 01:32:38,522
Are they making an arrow for "Love Shot?"

2349
01:32:39,692 --> 01:32:40,692
They're the two suns.

2350
01:32:40,693 --> 01:32:42,562
This team used the lights really well.

2351
01:32:50,802 --> 01:32:52,102
So clean.

2352
01:32:56,982 --> 01:32:58,712
- Let's go. - Let's go.

2353
01:32:58,742 --> 01:33:00,152
Let's go, Penrose!

2354
01:33:00,252 --> 01:33:01,681
Come on, Penrose!

2355
01:33:01,682 --> 01:33:03,221
- Gosh, I'm a huge fan. - Let's go!

2356
01:33:03,222 --> 01:33:05,352
- Let's go! - Let's go!

2357
01:33:05,722 --> 01:33:06,952
Let's go, Penrose!

2358
01:33:07,622 --> 01:33:09,292
Gosh, they're so good!

2359
01:33:10,222 --> 01:33:11,592
The pop can be seen from here.

2360
01:33:13,362 --> 01:33:14,431
He brought these three?

2361
01:33:14,432 --> 01:33:15,461
How can they dance like that?

2362
01:33:15,462 --> 01:33:16,632
They're such great dancers.

2363
01:33:19,502 --> 01:33:20,671
(Audience satisfaction: 100 percent)

2364
01:33:20,672 --> 01:33:21,772
Nino!

2365
01:33:25,042 --> 01:33:27,642
It feels like this team has more talented dancers.

2366
01:33:27,772 --> 01:33:29,011
Shuri is insane.

2367
01:33:29,012 --> 01:33:30,512
He's such a great dancer.

2368
01:33:30,782 --> 01:33:32,412
Let's go! Yes!

2369
01:33:33,052 --> 01:33:34,112
There we go.

2370
01:33:39,992 --> 01:33:41,791
It looks nice with the two tall ones.

2371
01:33:41,792 --> 01:33:42,792
That's insane.

2372
01:33:46,862 --> 01:33:49,102
Hold on. It's completely different from the rehearsal.

2373
01:33:57,602 --> 01:34:00,411
- That was great! - Awesome!

2374
01:34:00,412 --> 01:34:02,111
Nice!

2375
01:34:02,112 --> 01:34:04,611
(Watch the comparison video on "The CHOOM" and "Mnet Plus.")

2376
01:34:04,612 --> 01:34:05,612
(Kasper's performance is over.)

2377
01:34:05,613 --> 01:34:07,511
The energy for the ending was great.

2378
01:34:07,512 --> 01:34:08,812
- Right. - The ending was great.

2379
01:34:09,122 --> 01:34:12,451
The lights were definitely captivating.

2380
01:34:12,452 --> 01:34:13,492
Right.

2381
01:34:14,252 --> 01:34:15,892
The lights were insane.

2382
01:34:16,022 --> 01:34:19,192
The lights were really important for this performance.

2383
01:34:19,362 --> 01:34:20,492
Yummy lights.

2384
01:34:20,592 --> 01:34:22,931
Do you know what's incredible?

2385
01:34:22,932 --> 01:34:24,802
I had Koo Young in my mind as the winner.

2386
01:34:25,062 --> 01:34:26,231
Has your mind changed?

2387
01:34:26,232 --> 01:34:27,332
I think it will.

2388
01:34:27,772 --> 01:34:28,932
I prefer Koo Young's performance.

2389
01:34:29,702 --> 01:34:31,472
There was something thrilling about it.

2390
01:34:32,172 --> 01:34:34,141
- This is a win by a landslide. - This one?

2391
01:34:34,142 --> 01:34:35,312
It's the opposite for me.

2392
01:34:35,982 --> 01:34:40,182
I'm not sure what the Judges will think about the lights.

2393
01:34:40,712 --> 01:34:43,021
It will be a headache for them.

2394
01:34:43,022 --> 01:34:44,622
I don't know what to expect.

2395
01:34:46,492 --> 01:34:48,352
Please come up to the stage, Back Koo Young.

2396
01:34:51,692 --> 01:34:53,062
Great job.

2397
01:34:55,132 --> 01:34:56,901
We will hear the evaluation...

2398
01:34:56,902 --> 01:34:59,602
on Back Koo Young's Last Run.

2399
01:34:59,802 --> 01:35:01,701
The whole show as a thing,

2400
01:35:01,702 --> 01:35:03,601
so much happened in the first half...

2401
01:35:03,602 --> 01:35:05,101
that I was kind of just like...

2402
01:35:05,102 --> 01:35:06,671
I will say that I didn't like...

2403
01:35:06,672 --> 01:35:08,441
transitioning like this...

2404
01:35:08,442 --> 01:35:10,412
or running like this.

2405
01:35:11,412 --> 01:35:13,682
(The transitions were done in a stooped posture.)

2406
01:35:13,952 --> 01:35:15,251
But I know you're more talented than that...

2407
01:35:15,252 --> 01:35:17,152
and I know where you're telling us to focus.

2408
01:35:17,282 --> 01:35:19,752
You just have to know that you're still...

2409
01:35:19,992 --> 01:35:21,091
You're always performing.

2410
01:35:21,092 --> 01:35:23,062
It feels very...

2411
01:35:23,592 --> 01:35:26,162
I dont know. College level?

2412
01:35:27,032 --> 01:35:28,191
Gosh.

2413
01:35:28,192 --> 01:35:29,702
I felt a chill down my spine.

2414
01:35:30,032 --> 01:35:32,201
He wasn't able to make a good start.

2415
01:35:32,202 --> 01:35:33,332
There's a gap.

2416
01:35:33,472 --> 01:35:35,771
I didn't feel anything crazy...

2417
01:35:35,772 --> 01:35:37,802
until the girl showed up in the middle...

2418
01:35:37,972 --> 01:35:39,441
and then feel something...

2419
01:35:39,442 --> 01:35:40,941
in the second half. That's what I got.

2420
01:35:40,942 --> 01:35:43,081
That girl showed up and I went, "Woah."

2421
01:35:43,082 --> 01:35:45,581
And then she ends up over there, and I'm like, "Wow!"

2422
01:35:45,582 --> 01:35:48,311
"This is great!" I even told them, "That was so cool!"

2423
01:35:48,312 --> 01:35:50,621
I was like, "That was so cool!" Amazing job.

2424
01:35:50,622 --> 01:35:51,622
(Satisfied)

2425
01:35:51,722 --> 01:35:54,921
While watching the rehearsal yesterday,

2426
01:35:54,922 --> 01:35:57,891
it felt like you were struggling as you tried to take care of...

2427
01:35:57,892 --> 01:36:00,891
many different things on your own. That was disappointing to see.

2428
01:36:00,892 --> 01:36:02,931
But with today's performance,

2429
01:36:02,932 --> 01:36:06,671
I believe you've done a lot with your own abilities.

2430
01:36:06,672 --> 01:36:09,841
With you as an experienced lead,

2431
01:36:09,842 --> 01:36:13,842
it was impressive how the performance was well-structered.

2432
01:36:14,172 --> 01:36:17,241
As the story was expressed well,

2433
01:36:17,242 --> 01:36:20,582
the meaning of the running made sense.

2434
01:36:20,912 --> 01:36:23,581
I was impressed by the expression of...

2435
01:36:23,582 --> 01:36:26,422
how the man and woman failed to meet each other.

2436
01:36:26,722 --> 01:36:27,921
Was there a significant reason...

2437
01:36:27,922 --> 01:36:31,361
for the music to be struck exactly on the beat?

2438
01:36:31,362 --> 01:36:32,562
Gosh, that's sharp.

2439
01:36:32,862 --> 01:36:36,032
There were quite a lot of dancers without any stage experience.

2440
01:36:36,762 --> 01:36:38,801
I didn't make the rhythm-making feel difficult.

2441
01:36:38,802 --> 01:36:40,831
I came up with a choreography that was on the beat...

2442
01:36:40,832 --> 01:36:44,102
and uniformized the dancers to be seen as one big chunk.

2443
01:36:44,472 --> 01:36:46,871
It was the process to bring up the quality as much as possible.

2444
01:36:46,872 --> 01:36:48,241
That point...

2445
01:36:48,242 --> 01:36:50,681
was right up my alley.

2446
01:36:50,682 --> 01:36:53,481
I noticed that you tried to fit the density of that energy...

2447
01:36:53,482 --> 01:36:54,482
in one beat.

2448
01:36:54,483 --> 01:36:57,222
I want to give you a big round of applause for the quality.

2449
01:36:59,492 --> 01:37:02,922
I felt so grateful that she noticed those things.

2450
01:37:02,962 --> 01:37:05,021
The Judges are so sharp.

2451
01:37:05,022 --> 01:37:07,732
Gosh, I never thought about losing.

2452
01:37:08,332 --> 01:37:10,762
I felt a rush of anxiety.

2453
01:37:10,862 --> 01:37:12,202
Gosh, I'm feeling nervous.

2454
01:37:12,362 --> 01:37:14,002
(What did they think about Kasper's Last Run?)

2455
01:37:14,232 --> 01:37:17,101
You're also a person who likes making challenges.

2456
01:37:17,102 --> 01:37:18,541
This was the challenge you made.

2457
01:37:18,542 --> 01:37:21,511
The objects you must have used many different times before...

2458
01:37:21,512 --> 01:37:23,711
were placed at an important part.

2459
01:37:23,712 --> 01:37:26,611
The expressions you wanted to make of the ego...

2460
01:37:26,612 --> 01:37:28,781
were clearly presented.

2461
01:37:28,782 --> 01:37:31,051
You understood many different types of lights.

2462
01:37:31,052 --> 01:37:33,222
You did well to use those lights...

2463
01:37:34,252 --> 01:37:35,821
in an effective way.

2464
01:37:35,822 --> 01:37:37,791
I learned a lot from you. Thank you.

2465
01:37:37,792 --> 01:37:39,431
I loved that you started small.

2466
01:37:39,432 --> 01:37:41,591
Especially because the stage is so big.

2467
01:37:41,592 --> 01:37:44,201
You took the lighting away. You took everything away.

2468
01:37:44,202 --> 01:37:48,331
Small dramatics. The smoke came in, and then all the dancers showed up.

2469
01:37:48,332 --> 01:37:50,772
It just took me into your world.

2470
01:37:51,002 --> 01:37:52,672
A lot of good things were said to me.

2471
01:37:52,812 --> 01:37:54,841
"I did it. I survived."

2472
01:37:54,842 --> 01:37:56,311
I've got to admit.

2473
01:37:56,312 --> 01:37:58,482
The first half was better than the second half.

2474
01:37:58,782 --> 01:38:01,452
"What? What's going on all of a sudden?"

2475
01:38:01,552 --> 01:38:04,521
You're making me feel like my heart is beating...

2476
01:38:04,522 --> 01:38:05,881
"Oh, my gosh! What's going to happen?"

2477
01:38:05,882 --> 01:38:08,292
And then, when the beat drops and the moment happens...

2478
01:38:08,452 --> 01:38:10,622
(The buildup phase)

2479
01:38:11,922 --> 01:38:13,931
It just doesn't make me explode...

2480
01:38:13,932 --> 01:38:15,562
the way you're making me feel the setup.

2481
01:38:15,762 --> 01:38:17,231
Your setups are so good.

2482
01:38:17,232 --> 01:38:20,032
You need to be able to pay it off right when you get to the top. Okay?

2483
01:38:20,332 --> 01:38:23,342
It made me wonder if I was going to lose again.

2484
01:38:23,872 --> 01:38:25,841
The moment I heard the evaluations from the judges,

2485
01:38:25,842 --> 01:38:27,211
I thought I was going to win.

2486
01:38:27,212 --> 01:38:28,872
I was certain that I was going to win.

2487
01:38:29,012 --> 01:38:31,311
When you compare the formation of their performances,

2488
01:38:31,312 --> 01:38:32,982
Kasper's performance was more varied.

2489
01:38:33,152 --> 01:38:35,481
But from a judge's perspective,

2490
01:38:35,482 --> 01:38:38,252
I'd say that this guy's performance made a greater impact.

2491
01:38:38,352 --> 01:38:39,792
- Sounds good. - Okay.

2492
01:38:40,092 --> 01:38:41,151
Let's do that.

2493
01:38:41,152 --> 01:38:43,492
Kasper definitely came up with better setups.

2494
01:38:43,792 --> 01:38:47,192
But wasn't his storyline a bit less clear than Koo Young's?

2495
01:38:47,432 --> 01:38:48,691
Koo Young's performance had a solid storyline.

2496
01:38:48,692 --> 01:38:51,131
But Kasper just had a high level of performance. Right?

2497
01:38:51,132 --> 01:38:53,132
Earlier in the 1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission,

2498
01:38:53,272 --> 01:38:54,331
the choreographers faced off...

2499
01:38:54,332 --> 01:38:56,202
in the signature choreography takeover match.

2500
01:38:56,502 --> 01:38:58,242
Koo Young took the win,

2501
01:38:58,402 --> 01:39:00,612
and the song, "Guilty," went to Koo Young.

2502
01:39:00,812 --> 01:39:03,081
Will Koo Young be able to keep the momentum going...

2503
01:39:03,082 --> 01:39:06,082
and secure his spot on the Credit Board as a director?

2504
01:39:06,282 --> 01:39:07,282
It was my choreography.

2505
01:39:07,283 --> 01:39:09,312
I couldn't let him become the director.

2506
01:39:09,522 --> 01:39:10,951
Or will Kasper turn the tables...

2507
01:39:10,952 --> 01:39:13,721
and establish himself as a director?

2508
01:39:13,722 --> 01:39:16,522
I believe my name deserves to go to the board as the director.

2509
01:39:16,922 --> 01:39:18,262
We'll reveal it now.

2510
01:39:18,592 --> 01:39:19,692
- Yes! - Let's go!

2511
01:39:20,392 --> 01:39:22,492
- Oh, please. - This is making me nervous.

2512
01:39:22,762 --> 01:39:24,102
- Please. - I'm getting more nervous for him.

2513
01:39:24,602 --> 01:39:25,902
I think Kasper is going to win.

2514
01:39:26,062 --> 01:39:27,971
I'd say Koo Young's performance...

2515
01:39:27,972 --> 01:39:29,171
exploded with an wow factor.

2516
01:39:29,172 --> 01:39:30,842
It's neck and neck.

2517
01:39:33,542 --> 01:39:35,212
I have no idea how this is going to pan out.

2518
01:39:35,542 --> 01:39:37,842
I'll win for sure. It's impossible to lose with this performance.

2519
01:39:37,982 --> 01:39:39,552
I can definitely turn the tables around.

2520
01:39:39,812 --> 01:39:41,612
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

2521
01:39:46,822 --> 01:39:47,851
What?

2522
01:39:47,852 --> 01:39:48,992
For real? Why?

2523
01:39:49,092 --> 01:39:51,562
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

2524
01:39:51,622 --> 01:39:53,732
(Kasper wins.)

2525
01:39:54,062 --> 01:39:58,361
- Yes! - Yes!

2526
01:39:58,362 --> 01:40:00,032
I heard people cheering.

2527
01:40:00,732 --> 01:40:02,502
(Cheering)

2528
01:40:03,172 --> 01:40:04,172
(Screaming)

2529
01:40:07,272 --> 01:40:09,072
There was a huge burst of cheering.

2530
01:40:09,412 --> 01:40:10,512
(Checking the results)

2531
01:40:12,112 --> 01:40:13,112
(Feeling proud)

2532
01:40:13,582 --> 01:40:14,612
I won.

2533
01:40:18,052 --> 01:40:19,922
(Koo Young checks the final results too.)

2534
01:40:20,352 --> 01:40:21,622
(Nodding)

2535
01:40:22,552 --> 01:40:23,692
(Well done.)

2536
01:40:23,792 --> 01:40:24,861
- Kasper! - Kasper!

2537
01:40:24,862 --> 01:40:27,232
It was a well-earned victory.

2538
01:40:27,432 --> 01:40:28,562
Well done. Great work.

2539
01:40:28,792 --> 01:40:30,732
- Yes! - Yes!

2540
01:40:31,102 --> 01:40:33,001
A wave of mixed feelings came over me.

2541
01:40:33,002 --> 01:40:34,372
- Kasper! - I was happy.

2542
01:40:34,872 --> 01:40:35,901
- But I was concerned about him too. - Kasper!

2543
01:40:35,902 --> 01:40:38,401
- Kasper! - Kasper!

2544
01:40:38,402 --> 01:40:39,541
- Kasper! - Kasper.

2545
01:40:39,542 --> 01:40:41,842
- Kasper! - How do you feel now?

2546
01:40:50,122 --> 01:40:52,822
(Kasper is having a hard time finding his words.)

2547
01:41:03,432 --> 01:41:04,501
My goodness.

2548
01:41:04,502 --> 01:41:06,772
(He bursts into tears he's been holding back.)

2549
01:41:08,272 --> 01:41:10,701
(Koo Young can't bring himself to look at Kasper who's crying now.)

2550
01:41:10,702 --> 01:41:12,872
(Koo Young can't bring himself to look at Kasper who's crying now.)

2551
01:41:17,842 --> 01:41:18,842
To be honest, during this mission,

2552
01:41:19,782 --> 01:41:22,082
I felt like I was standing on the edge of a cliff.

2553
01:41:22,382 --> 01:41:26,822
I did all this to prove to people who the real director was.

2554
01:41:28,692 --> 01:41:30,462
(Fumbling)

2555
01:41:30,922 --> 01:41:32,591
(During the signature choreography takeover match,)

2556
01:41:32,592 --> 01:41:34,632
(he faced crisis after crisis.)

2557
01:41:35,192 --> 01:41:36,502
I lost with the score of 9 to 0.

2558
01:41:37,602 --> 01:41:39,302
My expected rank during the mid-point review...

2559
01:41:39,672 --> 01:41:40,702
(In disbelief)

2560
01:41:41,302 --> 01:41:43,542
I lost again with 7 to 1.

2561
01:41:44,042 --> 01:41:45,272
It made me wonder...

2562
01:41:46,512 --> 01:41:47,672
if I shouldn't have joined this show at all.

2563
01:41:48,672 --> 01:41:49,742
I thought...

2564
01:41:50,242 --> 01:41:51,882
I was doing a good job as a director.

2565
01:41:52,042 --> 01:41:53,481
But afterward, I kept doubting myself...

2566
01:41:53,482 --> 01:41:55,381
and thought I was wrong.

2567
01:41:55,382 --> 01:41:56,382
But now,

2568
01:41:57,182 --> 01:41:59,181
it feels like I finally got the validation...

2569
01:41:59,182 --> 01:42:02,452
that I was right. So I'm very grateful for that.

2570
01:42:09,662 --> 01:42:10,802
He handled this crisis really well.

2571
01:42:12,402 --> 01:42:14,732
I'm very happy right now.

2572
01:42:15,032 --> 01:42:18,441
I felt this way even before getting evaluated.

2573
01:42:18,442 --> 01:42:20,512
It didn't matter who won. Me or Kasper.

2574
01:42:20,672 --> 01:42:22,542
I knew I was going to be happy no matter what.

2575
01:42:22,642 --> 01:42:25,382
Now that it happened, I'm actually very happy for him.

2576
01:42:27,552 --> 01:42:29,052
This is odd, isn't it?

2577
01:42:30,952 --> 01:42:33,322
(During Kasper's performance)

2578
01:42:33,422 --> 01:42:34,551
Clap a lot when he finishes.

2579
01:42:34,552 --> 01:42:35,552
- Okay. - Okay.

2580
01:42:35,692 --> 01:42:39,061
As you saw, Kasper went through a lot...

2581
01:42:39,062 --> 01:42:40,392
to pull off this performance.

2582
01:42:40,992 --> 01:42:44,532
I could see how hard it was for him in his eyes.

2583
01:42:46,602 --> 01:42:49,501
I ended up rooting for Kasper before I realized it.

2584
01:42:49,502 --> 01:42:50,702
That's a cool way to end the performance.

2585
01:42:52,102 --> 01:42:55,312
I prayed with the others that he would finish strong.

2586
01:42:56,212 --> 01:42:59,042
So in a way, I'm happy it turned out this way.

2587
01:42:59,242 --> 01:43:01,482
Kasper got more confidence from this.

2588
01:43:01,882 --> 01:43:04,022
So I'm satisfied with it.

2589
01:43:06,392 --> 01:43:07,622
I was so happy.

2590
01:43:07,852 --> 01:43:11,222
I was incredibly happy to show Koo Young that I had improved.

2591
01:43:11,292 --> 01:43:14,762
I could feel that he was sincerely congratulating me.

2592
01:43:14,932 --> 01:43:16,032
I was so grateful.

2593
01:43:18,862 --> 01:43:23,642
Judging the two of you took a heavy emotional toll...

2594
01:43:24,772 --> 01:43:26,741
on me.

2595
01:43:26,742 --> 01:43:28,911
Actually, this is still taxing on me.

2596
01:43:28,912 --> 01:43:30,541
I know better than anyone...

2597
01:43:30,542 --> 01:43:33,381
how you guys grew as choreographers and about your struggles.

2598
01:43:33,382 --> 01:43:36,312
Watching you perform gave me a lot to think about.

2599
01:43:36,522 --> 01:43:38,552
But this is still a competition.

2600
01:43:38,722 --> 01:43:42,492
I tried my best to judge your performances objectively.

2601
01:43:42,622 --> 01:43:44,761
Both of you are outstanding dancers...

2602
01:43:44,762 --> 01:43:47,031
as performers and players in this competition.

2603
01:43:47,032 --> 01:43:48,661
Your dance skills are on par with each other.

2604
01:43:48,662 --> 01:43:49,702
However...

2605
01:43:49,932 --> 01:43:51,361
To me, I think it is this difference.

2606
01:43:51,362 --> 01:43:53,801
If this was a dance competition,

2607
01:43:53,802 --> 01:43:55,101
then I think this one wins.

2608
01:43:55,102 --> 01:43:56,102
- Right. - Please interpret.

2609
01:43:56,103 --> 01:43:57,771
You also got to understand...

2610
01:43:57,772 --> 01:44:00,212
you're not just talking to dancers. You're talking to the whole world.

2611
01:44:00,412 --> 01:44:02,741
So a non-dancer who watches this...

2612
01:44:02,742 --> 01:44:04,841
What are they going to be able to describe from this? So...

2613
01:44:04,842 --> 01:44:06,312
I feel the same way.

2614
01:44:06,512 --> 01:44:08,211
When I considered the fact that this would air all around the world,

2615
01:44:08,212 --> 01:44:09,922
not just in Korea,

2616
01:44:10,022 --> 01:44:11,921
I thought Kasper came up with...

2617
01:44:11,922 --> 01:44:14,451
more interesting setups that we hadn't seen before.

2618
01:44:14,452 --> 01:44:16,421
The utilization of the dancers...

2619
01:44:16,422 --> 01:44:20,532
was more dynamic and colorful. With that in mind,

2620
01:44:20,632 --> 01:44:22,732
I voted for Kasper.

2621
01:44:24,162 --> 01:44:25,832
(Thank you.)

2622
01:44:28,702 --> 01:44:30,741
In the end, the sole choreographer...

2623
01:44:30,742 --> 01:44:33,111
who successfully got his name on the Credit Board...

2624
01:44:33,112 --> 01:44:35,042
as a director was Kasper.

2625
01:44:37,242 --> 01:44:39,412
- Great job. - Say goodbye to your dancers.

2626
01:44:40,552 --> 01:44:42,212
(Shim Jae Won showers the choreographers with applause.)

2627
01:44:42,552 --> 01:44:43,982
(My team is the best!)

2628
01:44:46,592 --> 01:44:48,752
(I did it!)

2629
01:44:48,922 --> 01:44:50,291
- Kasper! - Kasper!

2630
01:44:50,292 --> 01:44:53,332
(You're such a crybaby)

2631
01:44:53,562 --> 01:44:54,832
(The crybaby is just happy.)

2632
01:44:55,132 --> 01:44:57,761
I felt bad that I might have hurt their feelings...

2633
01:44:57,762 --> 01:44:59,502
by being so blunt.

2634
01:44:59,562 --> 01:45:01,632
For some reason, I felt bad.

2635
01:45:02,202 --> 01:45:03,542
Of course, I was grateful.

2636
01:45:03,602 --> 01:45:06,512
(Enjoying the victory to the fullest)

2637
01:45:07,312 --> 01:45:08,872
Well done, no:ze.

2638
01:45:09,012 --> 01:45:10,811
Seriously. You did a great job.

2639
01:45:10,812 --> 01:45:11,841
You were great, Koo Young.

2640
01:45:11,842 --> 01:45:13,211
Great job, everyone.

2641
01:45:13,212 --> 01:45:14,811
- Good work. - Good work.

2642
01:45:14,812 --> 01:45:16,752
Of course, I'm disappointed. This is a competition.

2643
01:45:17,022 --> 01:45:18,752
I feel bad that we lost.

2644
01:45:19,082 --> 01:45:21,852
My dancers worked really hard.

2645
01:45:22,892 --> 01:45:27,062
I bet everyone got five bruises each.

2646
01:45:27,592 --> 01:45:28,592
They didn't have any stage experience,

2647
01:45:28,593 --> 01:45:30,161
and we met for the first time during this mission.

2648
01:45:30,162 --> 01:45:32,932
I honestly didn't expect them to keep up this well.

2649
01:45:33,302 --> 01:45:34,702
They worked hard...

2650
01:45:34,902 --> 01:45:36,872
to help me win.

2651
01:45:37,142 --> 01:45:39,912
I could totally feel their energy.

2652
01:45:40,142 --> 01:45:41,812
I was really touched.

2653
01:45:43,212 --> 01:45:46,851
We came behind in the judges' evaluation.

2654
01:45:46,852 --> 01:45:49,752
But what we can do is remember this process...

2655
01:45:50,022 --> 01:45:52,452
and we can hopefully meet again.

2656
01:45:53,152 --> 01:45:55,421
- Great job. - Good work!

2657
01:45:55,422 --> 01:45:57,592
(Thank you!)

2658
01:45:58,892 --> 01:46:00,632
Here you go. It's nothing big.

2659
01:46:01,162 --> 01:46:02,532
Thank you.

2660
01:46:02,892 --> 01:46:04,902
- Gosh, no. - Koo Young has handwritten letters.

2661
01:46:05,132 --> 01:46:06,731
(Koo Young wrote a letter by hand for every dancer...)

2662
01:46:06,732 --> 01:46:08,002
(to show his gratitude.)

2663
01:46:08,102 --> 01:46:10,972
I was really grateful that my dancers worked hard.

2664
01:46:11,642 --> 01:46:13,472
I wanted to express my gratitude.

2665
01:46:13,872 --> 01:46:17,242
I thanked everyone in the letters.

2666
01:46:18,082 --> 01:46:19,182
This is so sad.

2667
01:46:23,382 --> 01:46:25,881
If we ever get to work together again, I'll make us win.

2668
01:46:25,882 --> 01:46:28,392
(If we ever get to work together again, I'll make us win.)

2669
01:46:29,292 --> 01:46:31,762
(They're on the verge of tears.)

2670
01:46:36,932 --> 01:46:37,962
My goodness. What is this?

2671
01:46:38,132 --> 01:46:40,532
- Great job, Koo Young. - Thank you.

2672
01:46:40,802 --> 01:46:42,932
- Thank you! - Great job!

2673
01:46:43,772 --> 01:46:45,102
Today was...

2674
01:46:45,502 --> 01:46:47,942
a painful day, but I was happy at the same time.

2675
01:46:48,872 --> 01:46:52,042
The memories I made with them...

2676
01:46:52,182 --> 01:46:55,452
would be my own trophy from this mission.

2677
01:46:56,782 --> 01:46:58,122
JEONG MIN JUN versus Hash.

2678
01:46:58,352 --> 01:47:00,252
I was able to protect my choreography...

2679
01:47:00,692 --> 01:47:02,292
and take over Hash's choreography too.

2680
01:47:02,822 --> 01:47:04,522
She said I might be going home early.

2681
01:47:04,792 --> 01:47:05,962
I'm just getting started.

2682
01:47:06,832 --> 01:47:08,991
(I'll bring everything out in my brain.)

2683
01:47:08,992 --> 01:47:11,362
The director spot wasn't filled yet.

2684
01:47:11,462 --> 01:47:13,832
I really wanted to take the credit as the director.

2685
01:47:14,132 --> 01:47:15,931
My brain started doing its thing.

2686
01:47:15,932 --> 01:47:17,271
"How should I direct this performance?"

2687
01:47:17,272 --> 01:47:20,241
A new performance with features...

2688
01:47:20,242 --> 01:47:21,572
of MIN JUN's choreography.

2689
01:47:21,872 --> 01:47:25,682
I thought that approach might be cooler and more original.

2690
01:47:26,142 --> 01:47:28,851
I felt confident that I could put on...

2691
01:47:28,852 --> 01:47:31,921
a performance where all 40 dancers moving as one.

2692
01:47:31,922 --> 01:47:34,751
Hash wasn't able to take the credit as the choreographer.

2693
01:47:34,752 --> 01:47:37,692
So she'll have to work harder to get credited as the director.

2694
01:47:38,492 --> 01:47:42,132
All right. I'm going to teach you the choreography today.

2695
01:47:42,492 --> 01:47:44,102
First of all, this isn't my choreography.

2696
01:47:44,402 --> 01:47:46,931
I took down Hash in a landslide victory.

2697
01:47:46,932 --> 01:47:48,131
I totally beat her.

2698
01:47:48,132 --> 01:47:49,902
(MIN JUN is the best.)

2699
01:47:50,042 --> 01:47:51,242
I have to learn it too.

2700
01:47:52,072 --> 01:47:56,712
I was worried about how my dancers would think of me.

2701
01:47:56,912 --> 01:47:58,782
So I couldn't look at them.

2702
01:47:59,442 --> 01:48:01,311
Let's start from the top.

2703
01:48:01,312 --> 01:48:02,552
Inhale as much as you can.

2704
01:48:02,752 --> 01:48:05,522
I tried to make it look like I was doing my best to teach them...

2705
01:48:05,722 --> 01:48:07,292
while I deliberately held back.

2706
01:48:07,822 --> 01:48:09,322
(Flustered)

2707
01:48:09,592 --> 01:48:10,721
One, two...

2708
01:48:10,722 --> 01:48:12,022
This was a choreography workshop.

2709
01:48:12,322 --> 01:48:13,592
I wasn't required to teach them every detail.

2710
01:48:13,692 --> 01:48:15,161
One, two, three, four.

2711
01:48:15,162 --> 01:48:17,662
That's it. The steps. And boom.

2712
01:48:18,132 --> 01:48:19,762
(Unable to understand the moves)

2713
01:48:19,902 --> 01:48:22,631
MIN JUN's teaching was just awful.

2714
01:48:22,632 --> 01:48:24,101
When we're performing as a big group,

2715
01:48:24,102 --> 01:48:27,671
we have to execute the same moves in perfect sync.

2716
01:48:27,672 --> 01:48:29,412
Hitting the counts is super crucial.

2717
01:48:30,142 --> 01:48:32,182
(He's not counting the beats at all.)

2718
01:48:32,382 --> 01:48:34,781
So you put your right hand down...

2719
01:48:34,782 --> 01:48:36,781
right after we count six.

2720
01:48:36,782 --> 01:48:38,151
- Right after six. - I was frustrated.

2721
01:48:38,152 --> 01:48:41,021
So I intervened during the workshop and tried to clear things up.

2722
01:48:41,022 --> 01:48:42,821
Three, four, and a five. What was that?

2723
01:48:42,822 --> 01:48:44,191
- Three, four, and a five. - Three, four, and a five.

2724
01:48:44,192 --> 01:48:45,292
Yes.

2725
01:48:45,592 --> 01:48:47,892
How could you be a director...

2726
01:48:48,192 --> 01:48:49,692
if you can't stay on count?

2727
01:48:49,792 --> 01:48:52,462
Getting crafty was my strategy.

2728
01:48:52,862 --> 01:48:54,271
All right, here's what we'll do.

2729
01:48:54,272 --> 01:48:56,702
Hash, could you show us what you have so far?

2730
01:48:56,842 --> 01:48:58,442
- What? Me? - Yes.

2731
01:48:58,672 --> 01:49:02,242
MIN JUN kept trying to provoke me.

2732
01:49:02,342 --> 01:49:03,441
Of course, I feel threatened by her.

2733
01:49:03,442 --> 01:49:04,842
She's my rival. That's only natural.

2734
01:49:05,312 --> 01:49:07,511
Me? Why don't we do it together?

2735
01:49:07,512 --> 01:49:08,911
I'm not feeling well.

2736
01:49:08,912 --> 01:49:10,621
I'm not feeling well either.

2737
01:49:10,622 --> 01:49:12,421
But you have to lead your team.

2738
01:49:12,422 --> 01:49:14,221
It didn't feel good.

2739
01:49:14,222 --> 01:49:17,292
I didn't want to show him any moves I developed at all.

2740
01:49:17,392 --> 01:49:19,392
So I was going to dance exactly what he taught me.

2741
01:49:19,692 --> 01:49:21,832
My choreography is quite hard to learn.

2742
01:49:27,572 --> 01:49:28,602
(Cheering)

2743
01:49:28,732 --> 01:49:29,732
Wow

2744
01:49:32,102 --> 01:49:34,542
(Perfectly copying MIN JUN's choreography)

2745
01:49:34,842 --> 01:49:36,042
(A feast for the eyes)

2746
01:49:36,782 --> 01:49:38,681
I was surprised too. She was good.

2747
01:49:38,682 --> 01:49:41,152
After watching her dance, I was quite worried.

2748
01:49:41,382 --> 01:49:44,251
MIN JUN, when you were teaching the choreography, it was so clear...

2749
01:49:44,252 --> 01:49:45,551
that I was going to win.

2750
01:49:45,552 --> 01:49:48,822
Here's the biggest reason why Team Hash will win.

2751
01:49:49,092 --> 01:49:50,791
Everyone, check out that guy over there.

2752
01:49:50,792 --> 01:49:53,962
He's the youngest dancer of my crew, COME HERE, Yoo Seung Ho.

2753
01:49:55,032 --> 01:49:58,132
I got COME HERE to join us.

2754
01:49:58,302 --> 01:49:59,801
Based on the direction of your performance,

2755
01:49:59,802 --> 01:50:02,731
you may recruit up to ten extra dancers.

2756
01:50:02,732 --> 01:50:06,642
As for my strategy, I'm going to need my crew.

2757
01:50:06,702 --> 01:50:08,171
They've been executing my choreography...

2758
01:50:08,172 --> 01:50:11,441
and performing with me for years and on.

2759
01:50:11,442 --> 01:50:14,752
I don't think I can compare them to anyone else.

2760
01:50:15,382 --> 01:50:16,451
MIN JUN.

2761
01:50:16,452 --> 01:50:19,282
Be honest. Aren't you scared that you're going up against me?

2762
01:50:19,622 --> 01:50:21,222
But Hash doesn't have The Stories.

2763
01:50:21,392 --> 01:50:23,592
My strategy is recruiting my crew.

2764
01:50:24,162 --> 01:50:25,821
My crew takes pride in...

2765
01:50:25,822 --> 01:50:28,162
creating high-quality performances.

2766
01:50:28,592 --> 01:50:29,732
This is my choreography.

2767
01:50:31,002 --> 01:50:32,601
My crew will do a great job executing my choreography.

2768
01:50:32,602 --> 01:50:34,672
I'll bring them in and show people how great my crew is.

2769
01:50:35,832 --> 01:50:37,442
But there's one thing...

2770
01:50:37,502 --> 01:50:40,842
about MIN JUN that I consider as a real threat.

2771
01:50:41,512 --> 01:50:43,811
It's the impact Lip J will bring.

2772
01:50:43,812 --> 01:50:45,542
(Team JEONG MIN JUN's powerful weapon, Lip J)

2773
01:50:48,412 --> 01:50:49,781
Let's try it.

2774
01:50:49,782 --> 01:50:52,421
One, two, three, four, five, six.

2775
01:50:52,422 --> 01:50:54,192
(The dancers including Lip J are sitting on the floor.)

2776
01:50:54,752 --> 01:50:57,191
One, two, three, four, five, six.

2777
01:50:57,192 --> 01:50:58,922
One, two, three, four.

2778
01:50:59,262 --> 01:51:01,691
(While they're practicing nonstop,)

2779
01:51:01,716 --> 01:51:04,226
(these dancers have been on standby for 30 minutes.)

2780
01:51:05,232 --> 01:51:08,001
The dancers are sitting on the floor because they have nothing to do.

2781
01:51:08,002 --> 01:51:09,072
Or they're just resting.

2782
01:51:09,872 --> 01:51:10,971
Okay.

2783
01:51:10,972 --> 01:51:13,441
Could you guys count with me?

2784
01:51:13,442 --> 01:51:16,071
- One, two, three, four, five, six. - One, two, three, four, five, six.

2785
01:51:16,072 --> 01:51:17,541
One, two, three, four...

2786
01:51:17,542 --> 01:51:20,412
I was wondering how he planned to utilize me in the performance.

2787
01:51:21,812 --> 01:51:23,452
Raise your hands if you're in the intro.

2788
01:51:23,982 --> 01:51:25,151
Could you come over here?

2789
01:51:25,152 --> 01:51:26,921
I want the rest of you to stand here...

2790
01:51:26,922 --> 01:51:28,192
(Do we have to count again?)

2791
01:51:28,392 --> 01:51:30,691
Wait, no. Let me finish this up quickly.

2792
01:51:30,692 --> 01:51:32,422
I'll call you guys in afterward.

2793
01:51:33,262 --> 01:51:35,661
When we were waiting, I would have appreciated it...

2794
01:51:35,662 --> 01:51:37,061
if he gave us a clear plan...

2795
01:51:37,062 --> 01:51:39,002
like telling us how long it would take.

2796
01:51:39,632 --> 01:51:42,772
He made poor and inefficient decisions.

2797
01:51:43,302 --> 01:51:44,442
Next...

2798
01:51:45,802 --> 01:51:46,842
Let me see.

2799
01:51:47,642 --> 01:51:48,672
Okay.

2800
01:51:49,812 --> 01:51:51,142
I'm sorry.

2801
01:51:53,282 --> 01:51:56,411
One, two, three.

2802
01:51:56,412 --> 01:51:58,321
(Stopping)

2803
01:51:58,322 --> 01:52:00,591
MIN JUN came up with a lot of ideas.

2804
01:52:00,592 --> 01:52:03,391
Let me show you the hand movements. One, two, three, four.

2805
01:52:03,392 --> 01:52:04,562
I changed them just now.

2806
01:52:05,622 --> 01:52:07,161
He tried something, and when he didn't like it,

2807
01:52:07,162 --> 01:52:08,191
he changed it.

2808
01:52:08,192 --> 01:52:09,791
But as for Director Hash,

2809
01:52:09,792 --> 01:52:12,731
she has a clear plan for her setups and choreography.

2810
01:52:12,732 --> 01:52:15,371
She runs the sessions more efficiently.

2811
01:52:15,372 --> 01:52:17,071
That's where I noticed the gap between them.

2812
01:52:17,072 --> 01:52:19,672
One, two, three, four, five, six.

2813
01:52:20,212 --> 01:52:22,372
I'm sorry. One, two, three...

2814
01:52:25,882 --> 01:52:28,252
To be honest, his teaching wasn't smooth.

2815
01:52:28,412 --> 01:52:30,821
When evaluating a director,

2816
01:52:30,822 --> 01:52:33,051
the overall composition and choreography matter a lot.

2817
01:52:33,052 --> 01:52:36,321
But how a director supports and manages dancers...

2818
01:52:36,322 --> 01:52:39,091
is another major part of their skill set.

2819
01:52:39,092 --> 01:52:40,591
Compares to Hash,

2820
01:52:40,592 --> 01:52:43,462
his ability as a director falls short.

2821
01:52:44,662 --> 01:52:49,172
(Kalvin, the leader of The Stories, is observing MIN JUN direct.)

2822
01:52:49,572 --> 01:52:51,872
Here's what I've noticed about you.

2823
01:52:51,972 --> 01:52:55,072
The biggest difference between you and the rest comes down to...

2824
01:52:55,312 --> 01:52:56,472
dancer management.

2825
01:52:56,712 --> 01:52:58,141
Gosh, it's really tough.

2826
01:52:58,142 --> 01:52:59,382
How do I manage them?

2827
01:53:00,382 --> 01:53:03,752
I'm not really used to managing new dancers.

2828
01:53:04,282 --> 01:53:06,922
I'm having a hard time figuring out what to do.

2829
01:53:08,752 --> 01:53:10,151
How is it for you?

2830
01:53:10,152 --> 01:53:11,621
It was my first time...

2831
01:53:11,622 --> 01:53:13,221
- directing 40 dancers. - Yes.

2832
01:53:13,222 --> 01:53:16,132
I don't know how to bring them together as one team.

2833
01:53:17,362 --> 01:53:19,701
I watched you today. And this question kept popping in.

2834
01:53:19,702 --> 01:53:22,702
"Will everyone enjoy performing your choreography?"

2835
01:53:22,972 --> 01:53:25,172
That question nagged at me.

2836
01:53:25,402 --> 01:53:27,572
(Feeling bitter)

2837
01:53:28,372 --> 01:53:31,241
There must be dancers who might not enjoy it.

2838
01:53:31,242 --> 01:53:32,312
(He kept fixing his choreography to no end.)

2839
01:53:33,612 --> 01:53:34,811
I don't know...

2840
01:53:34,812 --> 01:53:36,711
how to approach them or bond with them.

2841
01:53:36,712 --> 01:53:38,681
I'm so lost when it comes to that.

2842
01:53:38,682 --> 01:53:40,822
I really want to try it, but I don't know where to start.

2843
01:53:42,192 --> 01:53:43,622
What is it for you?

2844
01:53:43,822 --> 01:53:45,022
It's the sense of belonging.

2845
01:53:46,122 --> 01:53:47,992
It's nice to start with small things.

2846
01:53:49,092 --> 01:53:50,802
I'll give it a try.

2847
01:53:50,902 --> 01:53:52,001
Thank you.

2848
01:53:52,002 --> 01:53:53,162
(He finishes the phone call with Kalvin.)

2849
01:53:53,802 --> 01:53:54,802
(Sighing)

2850
01:53:54,803 --> 01:53:56,301
It felt like I missed a huge mistake.

2851
01:53:56,302 --> 01:53:58,772
I treated them strictly as colleagues.

2852
01:53:58,842 --> 01:54:00,072
I realized that...

2853
01:54:00,912 --> 01:54:03,512
I had missed a lot of things as a director.

2854
01:54:04,882 --> 01:54:06,912
(MIN JUN is deep in thought.)

2855
01:54:07,012 --> 01:54:10,921
I kept trying to figure out a way to bring my team together...

2856
01:54:10,922 --> 01:54:12,882
like a family

2857
01:54:14,152 --> 01:54:15,291
Hello.

2858
01:54:15,292 --> 01:54:17,861
Did you get my letters?

2859
01:54:17,862 --> 01:54:18,992
- Yes! - Yes!

2860
01:54:19,462 --> 01:54:20,592
I cried.

2861
01:54:20,962 --> 01:54:22,092
Thank you.

2862
01:54:22,732 --> 01:54:26,031
It was just a small gesture to express...

2863
01:54:26,032 --> 01:54:28,632
how grateful and sorry I was.

2864
01:54:28,732 --> 01:54:30,602
(He wrote letters from the bottom of his heart after their practice.)

2865
01:54:31,072 --> 01:54:33,642
I apologized for not giving them clear explanations.

2866
01:54:34,472 --> 01:54:36,772
I wrote a letter, so they'd open up to me.

2867
01:54:38,142 --> 01:54:39,211
Did you like the food?

2868
01:54:39,212 --> 01:54:40,451
- Yes. - Really?

2869
01:54:40,452 --> 01:54:41,551
How's the practice going?

2870
01:54:41,552 --> 01:54:43,412
- How's the practice going? - It's fun.

2871
01:54:43,452 --> 01:54:44,722
- Really? - Yes.

2872
01:54:44,852 --> 01:54:45,852
(Touched and proud)

2873
01:54:46,122 --> 01:54:48,691
We formed a bond too.

2874
01:54:48,692 --> 01:54:51,321
It felt like I became a director they could rely on.

2875
01:54:51,322 --> 01:54:52,362
I was so happy.

2876
01:54:52,692 --> 01:54:55,032
Team Hash will begin their rehearsal.

2877
01:54:55,192 --> 01:54:57,802
- Hello. - Hello.

2878
01:54:58,132 --> 01:55:00,472
It looks like they have experience in performing as a big group.

2879
01:55:00,572 --> 01:55:01,731
They have a dress code.

2880
01:55:01,732 --> 01:55:03,172
They're trained for competitions like this.

2881
01:55:03,602 --> 01:55:06,441
I remember her being super original.

2882
01:55:06,442 --> 01:55:07,772
I'm looking forward to it.

2883
01:55:07,842 --> 01:55:10,711
I read her synopsis and her strategy for dancer management.

2884
01:55:10,712 --> 01:55:12,482
She was definitely ambitious.

2885
01:55:12,812 --> 01:55:15,211
It's the clash between the ego and the unconscious.

2886
01:55:15,212 --> 01:55:16,981
The ego and the unconscious.

2887
01:55:16,982 --> 01:55:18,322
This is such a complicated idea.

2888
01:55:18,582 --> 01:55:19,781
It's indeed a profound idea to explore.

2889
01:55:19,782 --> 01:55:21,622
She can show all this just in 2 minutes and 15 seconds?

2890
01:55:22,092 --> 01:55:24,492
But I must say I'm curious about her approach.

2891
