3408
02:15:30,962 --> 02:15:32,301
but you looked so beautiful.

3409
02:15:32,302 --> 02:15:34,232
(That's right.)

3410
02:15:34,332 --> 02:15:36,501
You're so beautiful, MIN JUN!

3411
02:15:36,502 --> 02:15:38,231
(Feeling shy)

3412
02:15:38,232 --> 02:15:40,942
My beloved muse,

3413
02:15:41,102 --> 02:15:43,312
Lip J, looked so different.

3414
02:15:43,772 --> 02:15:45,581
Thank you for transforming her...

3415
02:15:45,582 --> 02:15:48,551
into such an unexpected character that it allowed me...

3416
02:15:48,552 --> 02:15:50,012
to imagine her in a completely different way.

3417
02:15:50,482 --> 02:15:52,851
You brought out her hidden talent.

3418
02:15:52,852 --> 02:15:54,022
You showed great qualities...

3419
02:15:54,082 --> 02:15:56,152
as a director.

3420
02:15:56,392 --> 02:15:57,852
That's right, MIN JUN.

3421
02:15:58,222 --> 02:16:00,192
Who would've thought I could do something like that?

3422
02:16:00,922 --> 02:16:02,791
She's such a high-profile figure.

3423
02:16:02,792 --> 02:16:04,732
It felt like he used her just for that purpose.

3424
02:16:05,062 --> 02:16:07,832
I think this is also an element of directing.

3425
02:16:08,332 --> 02:16:10,501
When we saw Hash's performance,

3426
02:16:10,502 --> 02:16:12,872
we were a little worried about it.

3427
02:16:13,372 --> 02:16:14,541
"I'm in trouble. What should I do?"

3428
02:16:14,542 --> 02:16:15,672
That's what I thought.

3429
02:16:16,012 --> 02:16:17,071
This piece...

3430
02:16:17,072 --> 02:16:20,341
explores what humans have made of themselves in their pursuit...

3431
02:16:20,342 --> 02:16:23,251
of becoming something, and what they've lost along the way.

3432
02:16:23,252 --> 02:16:24,582
This is too difficult.

3433
02:16:25,152 --> 02:16:27,021
I think she tried to say a lot with it.

3434
02:16:27,022 --> 02:16:28,322
It's too difficult for the audience to follow.

3435
02:16:29,152 --> 02:16:32,261
I was worried about whether the message would come across.

3436
02:16:32,262 --> 02:16:33,421
The moment I saw the performance,

3437
02:16:33,422 --> 02:16:34,721
I realized I had nothing...

3438
02:16:34,722 --> 02:16:36,431
to worry about.

3439
02:16:36,432 --> 02:16:39,832
I think I'm good at creating standout moments.

3440
02:16:39,902 --> 02:16:41,932
I'm good at expressing things.

3441
02:16:42,072 --> 02:16:45,271
I really liked how you conveyed...

3442
02:16:45,272 --> 02:16:46,842
the emotion and essence of the dance...

3443
02:16:46,942 --> 02:16:48,312
that formed the foundation of your performance.

3444
02:16:48,572 --> 02:16:51,342
The last part where you end up on the stage with all those legs.

3445
02:16:53,282 --> 02:16:55,381
Visually, I thought that was the strongest thing.

3446
02:16:55,382 --> 02:16:57,911
You understand how to make simple movements.

3447
02:16:57,912 --> 02:17:00,022
You frame them the right way.

3448
02:17:00,082 --> 02:17:01,691
You take technical movement,

3449
02:17:01,692 --> 02:17:04,452
you frame stories around characters with it.

3450
02:17:04,892 --> 02:17:06,821
But it was the most visually fun thing that I saw,

3451
02:17:06,822 --> 02:17:08,262
and I'm just letting you know that.

3452
02:17:08,322 --> 02:17:10,361
Your performance...

3453
02:17:10,362 --> 02:17:14,102
felt more like pain and desperation for emancipation.

3454
02:17:14,532 --> 02:17:16,972
I was so immersed in it...

3455
02:17:17,572 --> 02:17:18,871
that I almost cried.

3456
02:17:18,872 --> 02:17:20,371
The way you portrayed the pain...

3457
02:17:20,372 --> 02:17:22,842
The quality was incredible. I was so immersed.

3458
02:17:22,942 --> 02:17:26,042
I could see that the choreographer had a clear goal.

3459
02:17:26,142 --> 02:17:27,181
It was a relief.

3460
02:17:27,182 --> 02:17:29,482
I was grateful that she noticed that.

3461
02:17:29,782 --> 02:17:31,582
It left me feeling a little unsettled.

3462
02:17:32,052 --> 02:17:33,821
To be clear,

3463
02:17:33,822 --> 02:17:35,692
this battle was surely for 1st and 2nd place.

3464
02:17:35,852 --> 02:17:37,252
That's clear.

3465
02:17:37,292 --> 02:17:38,421
The quality was really good.

3466
02:17:38,422 --> 02:17:39,792
I think this is going to be a real neck-and-neck battle.

3467
02:17:40,392 --> 02:17:43,232
I think the point of all this...

3468
02:17:43,332 --> 02:17:45,601
is to evaluate their abilities as directors.

3469
02:17:45,602 --> 02:17:46,631
The director's intention...

3470
02:17:46,632 --> 02:17:47,961
and the ability to convey that.

3471
02:17:47,962 --> 02:17:50,301
These two things meant a lot to me.

3472
02:17:50,302 --> 02:17:52,971
I think the person with more convincing movements...

3473
02:17:52,972 --> 02:17:54,572
was MIN JUN.

3474
02:17:54,672 --> 02:17:57,772
I think it's a moment where I can prove my abilities.

3475
02:17:57,812 --> 02:17:58,911
When Hash started,

3476
02:17:58,912 --> 02:18:00,341
I really thought that she was just going to win...

3477
02:18:00,342 --> 02:18:02,582
because I just felt like it was more powerful.

3478
02:18:02,612 --> 02:18:03,751
I'm so sure of it.

3479
02:18:03,752 --> 02:18:04,912
I'm going to win.

3480
02:18:04,982 --> 02:18:07,252
This match is so hard.

3481
02:18:07,322 --> 02:18:09,122
These people are no joke.

3482
02:18:09,192 --> 02:18:11,491
1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission.

3483
02:18:11,492 --> 02:18:14,191
Who will be the choreographer to showcase their work...

3484
02:18:14,192 --> 02:18:15,891
to the audience and see their name listed as a director...

3485
02:18:15,892 --> 02:18:17,592
on the Credit Board?

3486
02:18:17,662 --> 02:18:19,231
Let's see the result now.

3487
02:18:19,232 --> 02:18:21,102
(JEONG MIN JUN vs Hash, who will be the director?)

3488
02:18:21,162 --> 02:18:22,301
I think I'll win.

3489
02:18:22,302 --> 02:18:23,402
I think I'll win.

3490
02:18:23,732 --> 02:18:25,032
My goodness.

3491
02:18:25,872 --> 02:18:27,071
Hash is the best.

3492
02:18:27,072 --> 02:18:28,402
You're the best.

3493
02:18:28,742 --> 02:18:30,312
They're neck and neck.

3494
02:18:30,372 --> 02:18:31,781
His storytelling is really good.

3495
02:18:31,782 --> 02:18:33,841
I think MIN JUN will win.

3496
02:18:33,842 --> 02:18:35,211
She's simply on a completely different level.

3497
02:18:35,212 --> 02:18:36,552
Hash will win.

3498
02:18:36,812 --> 02:18:39,421
- JEONG MIN JUN! - JEONG MIN JUN!

3499
02:18:39,422 --> 02:18:41,722
- Hash! - Hash!

3500
02:18:42,252 --> 02:18:43,821
I felt like throwing up.

3501
02:18:43,822 --> 02:18:45,361
I deliberately didn't look up.

3502
02:18:45,362 --> 02:18:46,792
Because I thought I'd be disappointed.

3503
02:18:51,192 --> 02:18:52,501
(Shocking!)

3504
02:18:52,502 --> 02:18:55,002
(JEONG MIN JUN vs Hash, who will be the winner?)

3505
02:18:55,132 --> 02:18:57,602
(JEONG MIN JUN vs Hash, who will be the winner?)

3506
02:18:57,702 --> 02:19:00,102
(JEONG MIN JUN!)

3507
02:19:00,372 --> 02:19:02,242
(Hash!)

3508
02:19:03,272 --> 02:19:04,741
I felt like throwing up.

3509
02:19:04,742 --> 02:19:06,241
I deliberately didn't look up.

3510
02:19:06,242 --> 02:19:07,482
Because I thought I'd be disappointed.

3511
02:19:12,022 --> 02:19:13,221
(Shocking!)

3512
02:19:13,222 --> 02:19:14,522
(1-on-1 Signature 400 Mission)

3513
02:19:15,022 --> 02:19:16,022
(JEONG MIN JUN wins.)

3514
02:19:16,023 --> 02:19:17,392
It's JEONG MIN JUN!

3515
02:19:20,922 --> 02:19:23,632
(JEONG MIN JUN got his name on the Director Credit.)

3516
02:19:24,532 --> 02:19:26,761
(Screaming)

3517
02:19:26,762 --> 02:19:29,131
(An emotional hug)

3518
02:19:29,132 --> 02:19:31,271
(Clapping with a sense of regret)

3519
02:19:31,272 --> 02:19:32,842
Good job, Hash!

3520
02:19:33,202 --> 02:19:34,541
Well done!

3521
02:19:34,542 --> 02:19:36,372
I was surprised. It was shocking.

3522
02:19:38,372 --> 02:19:40,282
I couldn't believe it for a second.

3523
02:19:40,312 --> 02:19:44,782
- Team MIN JUN! - Team MIN JUN!

3524
02:19:49,422 --> 02:19:53,292
(An overwhelming surge of emotion upon facing the dancers)

3525
02:19:55,232 --> 02:19:57,862
(The team members are deeply moved as if they could feel him.)

3526
02:20:00,932 --> 02:20:04,872
A flood of thoughts and emotions washed over me.

3527
02:20:05,402 --> 02:20:06,901
David symbolizes...

3528
02:20:06,902 --> 02:20:09,142
a very small and seemingly weak boy...

3529
02:20:09,242 --> 02:20:13,112
who appears incapable of overcoming anything.

3530
02:20:13,482 --> 02:20:17,152
I faced a lot of criticism for being here...

3531
02:20:17,312 --> 02:20:20,082
as a co-director.

3532
02:20:20,882 --> 02:20:23,251
(He summoned the courage to enter the Directors' Lab.)

3533
02:20:23,252 --> 02:20:25,262
Wouldn't he be at the very bottom?

3534
02:20:25,762 --> 02:20:27,422
I think he's weak.

3535
02:20:27,492 --> 02:20:28,661
Gosh.

3536
02:20:28,662 --> 02:20:30,032
I think he'll be the first to leave.

3537
02:20:30,132 --> 02:20:31,631
He can leave.

3538
02:20:31,632 --> 02:20:32,802
Because he's still young.

3539
02:20:32,862 --> 02:20:34,831
Your parents are worrying about you.

3540
02:20:34,832 --> 02:20:36,272
He's still a baby.

3541
02:20:37,032 --> 02:20:38,602
Everyone had a similar reaction.

3542
02:20:38,872 --> 02:20:40,571
They weren't lying.

3543
02:20:40,572 --> 02:20:43,612
I haven't built as much experience as those people.

3544
02:20:43,942 --> 02:20:46,982
I'm a David among many Goliaths.

3545
02:20:47,642 --> 02:20:50,211
I was significantly lacking in that regard.

3546
02:20:50,212 --> 02:20:52,581
So it felt like a heavy burden, and I was very worried.

3547
02:20:52,582 --> 02:20:53,882
In a way,

3548
02:20:54,522 --> 02:20:57,322
I, a David who might appear inadequate and weak,

3549
02:20:57,552 --> 02:21:00,622
defeated the giant Goliath.

3550
02:21:01,322 --> 02:21:05,132
I naturally became emotional.

3551
02:21:05,432 --> 02:21:07,932
I was truly grateful to the team members.

3552
02:21:08,132 --> 02:21:09,731
- Don't cry! - Don't cry!

3553
02:21:09,732 --> 02:21:11,802
- I think I'm going to cry too. - Don't cry!

3554
02:21:12,142 --> 02:21:13,741
Well done.

3555
02:21:13,742 --> 02:21:15,242
(Well done, MIN JUN.)

3556
02:21:16,872 --> 02:21:19,481
Everyone cheered with one heart and one mind.

3557
02:21:19,482 --> 02:21:22,652
Is it okay for me to receive so much energy from these people?

3558
02:21:23,282 --> 02:21:25,852
(Though clumsy, he reached out to the dancers with all his heart.)

3559
02:21:26,382 --> 02:21:27,781
These are the people...

3560
02:21:27,782 --> 02:21:30,191
who helped me in a battle where I had nothing...

3561
02:21:30,192 --> 02:21:32,162
and it seemed impossible to win.

3562
02:21:32,262 --> 02:21:34,122
We became a family.

3563
02:21:34,392 --> 02:21:35,631
I mean it.

3564
02:21:35,632 --> 02:21:36,661
(Team JEONG MIN JUN finally became a united force.)

3565
02:21:36,662 --> 02:21:38,801
In fact, the quality of the work itself...

3566
02:21:38,802 --> 02:21:41,001
was very high for both of you.

3567
02:21:41,002 --> 02:21:42,102
But...

3568
02:21:42,132 --> 02:21:43,971
this is a broadcast.

3569
02:21:43,972 --> 02:21:45,701
I think Hash needs to be...

3570
02:21:45,702 --> 02:21:47,572
a little kinder.

3571
02:21:47,872 --> 02:21:49,711
Mass appeal was a significant factor for me.

3572
02:21:49,712 --> 02:21:52,541
Judging by the synopsis, the story was...

3573
02:21:52,542 --> 02:21:53,581
overly long-winded.

3574
02:21:53,582 --> 02:21:56,451
I wondered if she could capture this...

3575
02:21:56,452 --> 02:21:57,811
within such a short time.

3576
02:21:57,812 --> 02:21:59,721
The synopsis was too difficult for me too.

3577
02:21:59,722 --> 02:22:02,752
I thought Team MIN JUN was kinder in that sense.

3578
02:22:03,252 --> 02:22:06,962
The aspect of mass appeal was mentioned the most.

3579
02:22:07,022 --> 02:22:09,931
How much would people seeing this for the first time...

3580
02:22:09,932 --> 02:22:12,502
be able to understand without reading the synopsis?

3581
02:22:12,632 --> 02:22:14,331
Ultimately, it's about layers.

3582
02:22:14,332 --> 02:22:16,532
Can ordinary people get this?

3583
02:22:16,702 --> 02:22:17,731
Mass appeal?

3584
02:22:17,732 --> 02:22:20,071
My perspective on the performance...

3585
02:22:20,072 --> 02:22:23,641
differs slightly from that of the judges.

3586
02:22:23,642 --> 02:22:26,011
They frequently mentioned "mass appeal."

3587
02:22:26,012 --> 02:22:28,242
Actually, I had time to change it.

3588
02:22:28,442 --> 02:22:29,681
(At the time of mid-point review)

3589
02:22:29,682 --> 02:22:31,212
Is it really 4 to 4?

3590
02:22:31,312 --> 02:22:32,952
I won't change it.

3591
02:22:33,222 --> 02:22:35,552
The reason I didn't change it...

3592
02:22:35,822 --> 02:22:38,151
was that I wanted to win...

3593
02:22:38,152 --> 02:22:39,362
over the public.

3594
02:22:39,592 --> 02:22:41,761
Let's stick to what I have...

3595
02:22:41,762 --> 02:22:43,962
and show it as it is.

3596
02:22:44,032 --> 02:22:47,231
If it had been the competition I usually participate in,

3597
02:22:47,232 --> 02:22:48,232
I would have won.

3598
02:22:48,233 --> 02:22:49,302
No doubt.

3599
02:22:51,032 --> 02:22:53,041
- I'll... - Yes.

3600
02:22:53,042 --> 02:22:54,642
show them on the scene.

3601
02:22:56,042 --> 02:22:58,041
I'm serious. I'll show them.

3602
02:22:58,042 --> 02:22:59,082
Right away.

3603
02:22:59,142 --> 02:23:01,542
I think we put on an amazing performance.

3604
02:23:01,982 --> 02:23:04,382
Yes. So I'm really grateful.

3605
02:23:04,882 --> 02:23:06,481
I'll make you win...

3606
02:23:06,482 --> 02:23:08,621
a different competition in the future.

3607
02:23:08,622 --> 02:23:10,592
(We trust you.)

3608
02:23:11,022 --> 02:23:12,661
Thank you so much.

3609
02:23:12,662 --> 02:23:14,322
(Hash expresses heartfelt gratitude.)

3610
02:23:14,492 --> 02:23:16,162
(Next week)

3611
02:23:16,292 --> 02:23:17,762
(Why am I here?)

3612
02:23:17,932 --> 02:23:19,201
(It feels like being pushed out...)

3613
02:23:19,202 --> 02:23:20,502
(into a wasteland.)

3614
02:23:22,772 --> 02:23:24,201
(Are you ready?)

3615
02:23:24,202 --> 02:23:26,342
(Team BADA)

3616
02:23:26,942 --> 02:23:30,041
(It was a ritual intended to make the world dance.)

3617
02:23:30,042 --> 02:23:31,142
(Team INGYOO, screaming)

3618
02:23:31,912 --> 02:23:34,541
(Team BADA makes a sortie.)

3619
02:23:34,542 --> 02:23:36,552
(Team INGYOO makes a sortie.)

3620
02:23:36,782 --> 02:23:39,322
(I'm not afraid of the directors' fight.)

3621
02:23:41,522 --> 02:23:43,651
(Because there's a difference in physicality,)

3622
02:23:43,652 --> 02:23:45,661
(I have a better chance of winning.)

3623
02:23:45,662 --> 02:23:47,591
(There will be a battle of physique,)

3624
02:23:47,592 --> 02:23:49,631
(but that won't be a problem.)

3625
02:23:49,632 --> 02:23:50,662
(It's already over.)

3626
02:23:50,832 --> 02:23:52,231
(Dumbfounded)

3627
02:23:52,232 --> 02:23:53,401
(They're copying us!)

3628
02:23:53,402 --> 02:23:55,002
(Why does he keep acting so childish?)

3629
02:23:55,332 --> 02:23:56,401
(She's possessed.)

3630
02:23:56,402 --> 02:23:57,402
(It seemed like she was calling ghosts.)

3631
02:23:57,403 --> 02:23:58,602
(She looked like she was going to perform necromancy.)

3632
02:23:58,732 --> 02:24:00,271
(There's a dancer who lacks the fundamentals.)

3633
02:24:00,272 --> 02:24:01,572
(I'm like a stick.)

3634
02:24:01,602 --> 02:24:02,871
(Like a stick?)

3635
02:24:02,872 --> 02:24:04,242
(I'm like a stick.)

3636
02:24:04,672 --> 02:24:05,841
(What am I going to do?)

3637
02:24:05,842 --> 02:24:07,481
(I've never prepared a performance...)

3638
02:24:07,482 --> 02:24:09,252
(with a dancer like this.)

3639
02:24:09,582 --> 02:24:10,611
(What's wrong?)

3640
02:24:10,612 --> 02:24:13,281
(She's wondering if you have any more choreography for her.)

3641
02:24:13,282 --> 02:24:15,521
(I don't want to know.)

3642
02:24:15,522 --> 02:24:16,951
(My goodness.)

3643
02:24:16,952 --> 02:24:19,391
(What? What's going on?)

3644
02:24:19,392 --> 02:24:21,292
(This isn't just a show. It's a competition.)

3645
02:24:21,362 --> 02:24:22,662
(If I mess up, I'll get cut here.)

3646
02:24:22,832 --> 02:24:24,391
(Please don't make a mistake.)

3647
02:24:24,392 --> 02:24:26,732
(It's a bit overwhelming.)

3648
02:24:27,032 --> 02:24:29,471
(Is my level too low?)

3649
02:24:29,472 --> 02:24:31,201
(BABYZOO vs NaiN)

3650
02:24:31,202 --> 02:24:32,601
(BADA vs INGYOO)

3651
02:24:32,602 --> 02:24:34,542
(A fierce Last Run toward the Director Credit)

3652
02:24:36,212 --> 02:24:38,071
(I'll take the Director Credit.)

3653
02:24:38,072 --> 02:24:39,441
(Honestly, I'm going to win.)

3654
02:24:39,442 --> 02:24:40,982
(My heart is going to burst.)

3655
02:24:41,082 --> 02:24:42,782
(I'll win no matter what.)

3656
02:24:43,452 --> 02:24:44,611
(Wait, NaiN. This time,)

3657
02:24:44,612 --> 02:24:45,921
(we're the mannequins.)

3658
02:24:45,922 --> 02:24:46,951
(Dancer?)

3659
02:24:46,952 --> 02:24:47,952
(It's the dancer!)

3660
02:24:47,953 --> 02:24:49,352
(We are becoming the dancers!)

3661
02:24:49,422 --> 02:24:51,121
(There is one director.)

3662
02:24:51,122 --> 02:24:53,061
(This is the Directors' Version of the Class Mission.)

3663
02:24:53,062 --> 02:24:54,062
(The second mission)

3664
02:24:54,063 --> 02:24:55,661
(Title Sequence Film Mission)

3665
02:24:55,662 --> 02:24:57,892
(A choreographer will be eliminated.)

3666
02:24:58,192 --> 02:24:59,231
Gosh!

3667
02:24:59,232 --> 02:25:01,031
(The first choreographer to be eliminated)

3668
02:25:01,032 --> 02:25:02,831
(Final survival showdown)

3669
02:25:02,832 --> 02:25:04,431
(Application for on-site audience of "Last Stage: 24H")

3670
02:25:04,432 --> 02:25:05,701
(There is...)

3671
02:25:05,702 --> 02:25:07,372
(only one condition.)

3672
02:25:07,472 --> 02:25:08,541
(You have...)

3673
02:25:08,542 --> 02:25:09,612
(24 hours.)

3674
02:25:11,142 --> 02:25:12,481
(Are they crazy?)

3675
02:25:12,482 --> 02:25:15,481
(The final director holds the authority to decide...)

3676
02:25:15,482 --> 02:25:17,481
(which candidates are up for elimination.)

3677
02:25:17,482 --> 02:25:19,851
(Can they demonstrate the process of their efforts...)

3678
02:25:19,852 --> 02:25:21,651
(to the director?)

3679
02:25:21,652 --> 02:25:22,991
(Wouldn't that be the ultimate power?)

3680
02:25:22,992 --> 02:25:24,251
(I should become a director.)

3681
02:25:24,252 --> 02:25:25,561
(I don't want to be a dancer.)

3682
02:25:25,562 --> 02:25:28,021
(Directors are getting directed.)

3683
02:25:28,022 --> 02:25:29,791
("Over there, towards the back left. To the back.")

3684
02:25:29,792 --> 02:25:32,231
(If I have to put up with this,)

3685
02:25:32,232 --> 02:25:33,232
(I might as well just go home.)

3686
02:25:33,233 --> 02:25:35,131
(It's been so long since I've been...)

3687
02:25:35,132 --> 02:25:36,701
(directed by anyone.)

3688
02:25:36,702 --> 02:25:40,601
(Draft Creation Mission given to 10 choreographers)

3689
02:25:40,602 --> 02:25:42,511
(We need to find a good dancer for the Draft.)

3690
02:25:42,512 --> 02:25:44,141
(The 9 characters need to be clearly visible.)

3691
02:25:44,142 --> 02:25:46,381
(Vata should be the one to replace BADA.)

3692
02:25:46,382 --> 02:25:48,581
(Here is Vata who will play BADA.)

3693
02:25:48,582 --> 02:25:49,582
(I have to call them.)

3694
02:25:49,583 --> 02:25:51,181
(I called around right away.)

3695
02:25:51,182 --> 02:25:54,151
(I'll use Rozalin as BABYZOO.)

3696
02:25:54,152 --> 02:25:55,281
("Street Woman Fighter," Rozalin of WANT)

3697
02:25:55,282 --> 02:25:56,721
(As BABYZOO...)

3698
02:25:56,722 --> 02:25:58,251
(Who did Back Koo Young choose as BABYZOO?)

3699
02:25:58,252 --> 02:25:59,421
("Street Man Fighter," ROOT of 1MILLION)

3700
02:25:59,422 --> 02:26:01,561
(BADA, Simeez, Renan, BABYZOO)

3701
02:26:01,562 --> 02:26:02,591
(They all called me.)

3702
02:26:02,592 --> 02:26:04,531
(I need to get him before they do.)

3703
02:26:04,532 --> 02:26:05,661
(It's war.)

3704
02:26:05,662 --> 02:26:07,901
(Koo Young is the hardest.)

3705
02:26:07,902 --> 02:26:09,631
(Pick up the phone, Choi Young Jun.)

3706
02:26:09,632 --> 02:26:10,632
(Hello, Koo Young!)

3707
02:26:10,633 --> 02:26:11,831
(Hello, INGYOO!)

3708
02:26:11,832 --> 02:26:12,871
(Help me.)

3709
02:26:12,872 --> 02:26:13,901
(Can you please help me?)

3710
02:26:13,902 --> 02:26:15,501
(As a dancer?)

3711
02:26:15,502 --> 02:26:18,011
(I need you as Koo Young.)

3712
02:26:18,012 --> 02:26:19,941
(Mine has to be picked.)

3713
02:26:19,942 --> 02:26:21,341
(I'm really confident.)

3714
02:26:21,342 --> 02:26:22,651
(They'll like it.)

3715
02:26:22,652 --> 02:26:23,681
(I'm confident.)

3716
02:26:23,682 --> 02:26:25,621
(I must be the director no matter what.)

3717
02:26:25,622 --> 02:26:27,022
(The choreographic staging...)

3718
02:26:27,322 --> 02:26:28,352
(wasn't so good.)

3719
02:26:28,382 --> 02:26:30,151
(It was the standardized format...)

3720
02:26:30,152 --> 02:26:32,221
(required in K-pop videos.)

3721
02:26:32,222 --> 02:26:34,061
(I felt like he was looking down on me.)

3722
02:26:34,062 --> 02:26:35,591
(How can he look down on K-pop,)

3723
02:26:35,592 --> 02:26:36,762
(when he's so young?)

3724
02:26:36,862 --> 02:26:38,791
(Which part are you talking about?)

3725
02:26:38,792 --> 02:26:41,131
(I was expecting a cinematic presentation.)

3726
02:26:41,132 --> 02:26:42,132
(What about you?)

3727
02:26:42,132 --> 02:26:43,132
(Let's see how well you do.)

3728
02:26:43,133 --> 02:26:45,001
(The feeling like a cinema)

3729
02:26:45,002 --> 02:26:46,071
(It comes down to the variety of...)

3730
02:26:46,072 --> 02:26:47,141
(focal lengths and directorial choices.)

3731
02:26:47,142 --> 02:26:49,871
(It felt like a college midterm assignment.)

3732
02:26:49,872 --> 02:26:52,141
(He'll probably think it's really groundbreaking.)

3733
02:26:52,142 --> 02:26:54,181
(He'll probably think of himself...)

3734
02:26:54,182 --> 02:26:55,282
(as an idea bank.)

3735
02:26:55,342 --> 02:26:57,511
(2 candidates for the director position...)

3736
02:26:57,512 --> 02:26:58,851
(will be selected from among the 10 choreographers.)

3737
02:26:58,852 --> 02:27:01,551
(Videos of the two final draft versions released in advance)

3738
02:27:01,552 --> 02:27:04,251
(Who will be the 2 director candidates?)

3739
02:27:04,252 --> 02:27:06,421
(Why does it look like BABYZOO's choreography?)

3740
02:27:06,422 --> 02:27:08,521
(It strongly gives off a Back Koo Young vibe.)

3741
02:27:08,522 --> 02:27:11,431
(It’s got that total Director INGYOO vibe.)

3742
02:27:11,432 --> 02:27:13,661
(This was BADA's choreography. I knew it.)

3743
02:27:13,662 --> 02:27:15,771
(This gives off a Renan vibe.)

3744
02:27:15,772 --> 02:27:19,241
(Who will claim the final director spot?)

3745
02:27:19,242 --> 02:27:21,901
(The result of this...)

3746
02:27:21,902 --> 02:27:23,442
(is just amazing.)

3747
02:27:23,572 --> 02:27:25,011
(Worst Director Candidate)

3748
02:27:25,012 --> 02:27:26,542
(BABYZOO)

3749
02:27:27,382 --> 02:27:29,652
(I'm in trouble.)
